    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-311",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "311 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-311"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must\nprevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so,\ntelecommunications networks and facilities from being used\nto commit offences.\n• The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must give\nthe authorities such help as is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of:\n\n(a)\nenforcing the criminal law and laws imposing\npecuniary penalties; and\n\n(b)\nprotecting the public revenue; and\n\n(c)\nsafeguarding national security.\n• A carriage service provider may suspend the supply of a\ncarriage service in an emergency if requested to do so by a senior\npolice officer.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must\nprevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so,\ntelecommunications networks and facilities from being used\nto commit offences.\n• The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must give\nthe authorities such help as is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of:\n\n(a)\nenforcing the criminal law and laws imposing\npecuniary penalties; and\n\n(b)\nprotecting the public revenue; and\n\n(c)\nsafeguarding national security.\n• A carriage service provider may suspend the supply of a\ncarriage service in an emergency if requested to do so by a senior\npolice officer.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-311-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-311-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "637a88f8c161751da4dfbc126784b836b960139b47e91b64d70db6d70c1f3c6e",
      "skos:note": "Must prevent use of telecommunications networks for committing offences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-311",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "311 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must\nprevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so,\ntelecommunications networks and facilities from being used\nto commit offences.\n• The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must give\nthe authorities such help as is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of:\n\n(a)\nenforcing the criminal law and laws imposing\npecuniary penalties; and\n\n(b)\nprotecting the public revenue; and\n\n(c)\nsafeguarding national security.\n• A carriage service provider may suspend the supply of a\ncarriage service in an emergency if requested to do so by a senior\npolice officer."
    },
    {
