    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-313",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "313 Obligations of carriers and carriage service providers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-313"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A carrier or carriage service provider must, in connection with:\n\n\nNational interest matters  Part 14\nObligations of ACMA and carriers and carriage service providers  Division 2\n\nSection 313\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the operation by the carrier or provider of\ntelecommunications networks or facilities; or\n\n(b) the supply by the carrier or provider of carriage services;\nprevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so,\ntelecommunications networks and facilities from being used in, or\nin relation to, the commission of offences against the laws of the\nCommonwealth or of the States and Territories.\n\n(2) A carriage service intermediary must prevent, so far as it is\nreasonably practicable to do so, telecommunications networks and\nfacilities from being used in, or in relation to, the commission of\noffences against the laws of the Commonwealth or of the States\nand Territories.\n\n(3) A carrier or carriage service provider must, in connection with:\n\n(a) the operation by the carrier or provider of\ntelecommunications networks or facilities; or\n\n(b) the supply by the carrier or provider of carriage services;\ngive officers and authorities of the Commonwealth and of the\nStates and Territories such help as is reasonably necessary for the\nfollowing purposes:\n\n(c) enforcing the criminal law and laws imposing pecuniary\npenalties;\n\n(ca) assisting the enforcement of the criminal laws in force in a\nforeign country;\n\n(cb) assisting the investigation and prosecution of:\n\n(i) crimes within the jurisdiction of the ICC (within the\nmeaning of the International Criminal Court Act 2002);\nand\n\n(ii) Tribunal offences (within the meaning of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995);\n\n(d) protecting the public revenue;\n\n(e) safeguarding national security.\nNote:\nSection 314 deals with the terms and conditions on which such help is\nto be provided.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A carrier or carriage service provider must, in connection with:\n\n\nNational interest matters  Part 14\nObligations of ACMA and carriers and carriage service providers  Division 2\n\nSection 313\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the operation by the carrier or provider of\ntelecommunications networks or facilities; or\n\n(b) the supply by the carrier or provider of carriage services;\nprevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so,\ntelecommunications networks and facilities from being used in, or\nin relation to, the commission of offences against the laws of the\nCommonwealth or of the States and Territories.\n\n(2) A carriage service intermediary must prevent, so far as it is\nreasonably practicable to do so, telecommunications networks and\nfacilities from being used in, or in relation to, the commission of\noffences against the laws of the Commonwealth or of the States\nand Territories.\n\n(3) A carrier or carriage service provider must, in connection with:\n\n(a) the operation by the carrier or provider of\ntelecommunications networks or facilities; or\n\n(b) the supply by the carrier or provider of carriage services;\ngive officers and authorities of the Commonwealth and of the\nStates and Territories such help as is reasonably necessary for the\nfollowing purposes:\n\n(c) enforcing the criminal law and laws imposing pecuniary\npenalties;\n\n(ca) assisting the enforcement of the criminal laws in force in a\nforeign country;\n\n(cb) assisting the investigation and prosecution of:\n\n(i) crimes within the jurisdiction of the ICC (within the\nmeaning of the International Criminal Court Act 2002);\nand\n\n(ii) Tribunal offences (within the meaning of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995);\n\n(d) protecting the public revenue;\n\n(e) safeguarding national security.\nNote:\nSection 314 deals with the terms and conditions on which such help is\nto be provided.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-313-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-313-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-313-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5db08bc6f8ba357626fccc705ad0ca4da7be0a2fce0ffb239ce9937414dd75f0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-313",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "313 Obligations of carriers and carriage service providers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A carrier or carriage service provider must, in connection with:\n\n\nNational interest matters  Part 14\nObligations of ACMA and carriers and carriage service providers  Division 2\n\nSection 313\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the operation by the carrier or provider of\ntelecommunications networks or facilities; or\n\n(b) the supply by the carrier or provider of carriage services;\nprevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so,\ntelecommunications networks and facilities from being used in, or\nin relation to, the commission of offences against the laws of the\nCommonwealth or of the States and Territories.\n\n(2) A carriage service intermediary must prevent, so far as it is\nreasonably practicable to do so, telecommunications networks and\nfacilities from being used in, or in relation to, the commission of\noffences against the laws of the Commonwealth or of the States\nand Territories.\n\n(3) A carrier or carriage service provider must, in connection with:\n\n(a) the operation by the carrier or provider of\ntelecommunications networks or facilities; or\n\n(b) the supply by the carrier or provider of carriage services;\ngive officers and authorities of the Commonwealth and of the\nStates and Territories such help as is reasonably necessary for the\nfollowing purposes:\n\n(c) enforcing the criminal law and laws imposing pecuniary\npenalties;\n\n(ca) assisting the enforcement of the criminal laws in force in a\nforeign country;\n\n(cb) assisting the investigation and prosecution of:\n\n(i) crimes within the jurisdiction of the ICC (within the\nmeaning of the International Criminal Court Act 2002);\nand\n\n(ii) Tribunal offences (within the meaning of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995);\n\n(d) protecting the public revenue;\n\n(e) safeguarding national security.\nNote:\nSection 314 deals with the terms and conditions on which such help is\nto be provided."
    },
