    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-315",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "315 Suspension of supply of carriage service in an emergency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-315"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a senior officer of a police force or service has reasonable\ngrounds to believe that:\n\n(a) an individual has access to a particular carriage service; and\n\n(b) the individual has:\n\n(i) done an act that has resulted, or is likely to result, in loss\nof life or in the infliction of serious personal injury; or\n\n(ii) made an imminent threat to kill, or seriously injure,\nanother person; or\n\n(iii) made an imminent threat to cause serious damage to\nproperty; or\n\n(iv) made an imminent threat to take the individual’s own\nlife; or\n\n(v) made an imminent threat to do an act that will, or is\nlikely to, endanger the individual’s own life or create a\nserious threat to the individual’s health or safety; and\n\n(c) the suspension of the supply of the carriage service is\nreasonably necessary to:\n\n(i) prevent a recurrence of the act mentioned in\nsubparagraph (b)(i); or\n\n(ii) prevent or reduce the likelihood of the carrying out of a\nthreat mentioned in subparagraph (b)(ii), (iii), (iv) or\n(v);\nthe officer may request a carriage service provider to suspend the\nsupply of the carriage service.\n\n(2) The carriage service provider may comply with the request.\n\n(3) This section does not, by implication, limit any other powers that\nthe provider may have to suspend the supply of the carriage\nservice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a senior officer of a police force or service has reasonable\ngrounds to believe that:\n\n(a) an individual has access to a particular carriage service; and\n\n(b) the individual has:\n\n(i) done an act that has resulted, or is likely to result, in loss\nof life or in the infliction of serious personal injury; or\n\n(ii) made an imminent threat to kill, or seriously injure,\nanother person; or\n\n(iii) made an imminent threat to cause serious damage to\nproperty; or\n\n(iv) made an imminent threat to take the individual’s own\nlife; or\n\n(v) made an imminent threat to do an act that will, or is\nlikely to, endanger the individual’s own life or create a\nserious threat to the individual’s health or safety; and\n\n(c) the suspension of the supply of the carriage service is\nreasonably necessary to:\n\n(i) prevent a recurrence of the act mentioned in\nsubparagraph (b)(i); or\n\n(ii) prevent or reduce the likelihood of the carrying out of a\nthreat mentioned in subparagraph (b)(ii), (iii), (iv) or\n(v);\nthe officer may request a carriage service provider to suspend the\nsupply of the carriage service.\n\n(2) The carriage service provider may comply with the request.\n\n(3) This section does not, by implication, limit any other powers that\nthe provider may have to suspend the supply of the carriage\nservice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-315-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-315-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-315-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4904c746b16bb1145e1f9a912a5cd7c000e155ea7a216560575da9bcb0998fdb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-315",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "315 Suspension of supply of carriage service in an emergency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a senior officer of a police force or service has reasonable\ngrounds to believe that:\n\n(a) an individual has access to a particular carriage service; and\n\n(b) the individual has:\n\n(i) done an act that has resulted, or is likely to result, in loss\nof life or in the infliction of serious personal injury; or\n\n(ii) made an imminent threat to kill, or seriously injure,\nanother person; or\n\n(iii) made an imminent threat to cause serious damage to\nproperty; or\n\n(iv) made an imminent threat to take the individual’s own\nlife; or\n\n(v) made an imminent threat to do an act that will, or is\nlikely to, endanger the individual’s own life or create a\nserious threat to the individual’s health or safety; and\n\n(c) the suspension of the supply of the carriage service is\nreasonably necessary to:\n\n(i) prevent a recurrence of the act mentioned in\nsubparagraph (b)(i); or\n\n(ii) prevent or reduce the likelihood of the carrying out of a\nthreat mentioned in subparagraph (b)(ii), (iii), (iv) or\n(v);\nthe officer may request a carriage service provider to suspend the\nsupply of the carriage service.\n\n(2) The carriage service provider may comply with the request.\n\n(3) This section does not, by implication, limit any other powers that\nthe provider may have to suspend the supply of the carriage\nservice."
    },
