      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317D Electronic service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, electronic service means:\n\n(a) a service that allows end-users to access material using a\ncarriage service; or\n\n(b) a service that delivers material to persons having equipment\nappropriate for receiving that material, where the delivery of\nthe service is by means of a carriage service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(c) a broadcasting service; or\n\n(d) a datacasting service (within the meaning of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), service includes a website.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Part, a person does not provide an\nelectronic service merely because the person supplies a carriage\nservice that enables material to be accessed or delivered.\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 317E\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Part, a person does not provide an\nelectronic service merely because the person provides a billing\nservice, or a fee collection service, in relation to an electronic\nservice.\n\n(5) A reference in this section to the use of a thing is a reference to the\nuse of the thing either:\n\n(a) in isolation; or\n\n(b) in conjunction with one or more other things.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, electronic service means:\n\n(a) a service that allows end-users to access material using a\ncarriage service; or\n\n(b) a service that delivers material to persons having equipment\nappropriate for receiving that material, where the delivery of\nthe service is by means of a carriage service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(c) a broadcasting service; or\n\n(d) a datacasting service (within the meaning of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992).\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), service includes a website.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this Part, a person does not provide an\nelectronic service merely because the person supplies a carriage\nservice that enables material to be accessed or delivered.\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 317E\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Part, a person does not provide an\nelectronic service merely because the person provides a billing\nservice, or a fee collection service, in relation to an electronic\nservice.\n\n(5) A reference in this section to the use of a thing is a reference to the\nuse of the thing either:\n\n(a) in isolation; or\n\n(b) in conjunction with one or more other things.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317d-ss-3"
