      "cml:premiseText": "(1) If any of the following persons requests a designated communications provider...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the provider is not subject to any civil liability for, or in relation to, the act or thing mentioned in paragraph (b);"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317g-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317G(2) Voluntary technical assistance provided to ASIO, the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317g-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The specified acts or things must:\n\n(a) be directed towards ensuring that the designated\ncommunications provider is capable of giving help to:\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nVoluntary technical assistance  Division 2\n\nSection 317G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of Security—ASIO; or\n\n(ii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService—the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or\n\n(iii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Signals\nDirectorate—the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(iv) in a case where the request is made by the chief officer\nof an interception agency—the agency;\n\nin relation to:\n\n(v) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a\npower, conferred by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory, so far as the\nfunction or power relates to a relevant objective; or\n\n(vi) a matter that facilitates, or is ancillary or incidental to, a\nmatter covered by subparagraph (v); or\n\n(b) be by way of giving help to:\n\n(i) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of Security—ASIO; or\n\n(ii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService—the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or\n\n(iii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Signals\nDirectorate—the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(iv) in a case where the request is made by the chief officer\nof an interception agency—the agency;\n\nin relation to:\n\n(v) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a\npower, conferred by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory, so far as the\nfunction or power relates to a relevant objective; or\n\n(vi) a matter that facilitates, or is ancillary or incidental to, a\nmatter covered by subparagraph (v).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The specified acts or things must:\n\n(a) be directed towards ensuring that the designated\ncommunications provider is capable of giving help to:\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nVoluntary technical assistance  Division 2\n\nSection 317G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of Security—ASIO; or\n\n(ii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService—the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or\n\n(iii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Signals\nDirectorate—the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(iv) in a case where the request is made by the chief officer\nof an interception agency—the agency;\n\nin relation to:\n\n(v) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a\npower, conferred by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory, so far as the\nfunction or power relates to a relevant objective; or\n\n(vi) a matter that facilitates, or is ancillary or incidental to, a\nmatter covered by subparagraph (v); or\n\n(b) be by way of giving help to:\n\n(i) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of Security—ASIO; or\n\n(ii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService—the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or\n\n(iii) in a case where the request is made by the\nDirector-General of the Australian Signals\nDirectorate—the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(iv) in a case where the request is made by the chief officer\nof an interception agency—the agency;\n\nin relation to:\n\n(v) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a\npower, conferred by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory, so far as the\nfunction or power relates to a relevant objective; or\n\n(vi) a matter that facilitates, or is ancillary or incidental to, a\nmatter covered by subparagraph (v).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317g"
      },
