    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317H Form of technical assistance request",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A technical assistance request may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(2) A technical assistance request must not be given orally unless:\n\n(a) an imminent risk of serious harm to a person or substantial\ndamage to property exists; and\n\n(b) the technical assistance request is necessary for the purpose\nof dealing with that risk; and\n\n(c) it is not practicable in the circumstances to give the technical\nassistance request in writing.\n\n(3) If a technical assistance request is given orally by:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security; or\n\n(b) the Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService; or\n\n(c) the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(d) the chief officer of an interception agency;\nthe Director-General of Security, the Director-General of the\nAustralian Secret Intelligence Service, the Director-General of the\nAustralian Signals Directorate or the chief officer, as the case\nrequires, must:\n\n(e) make a written record of the request; and\n\n(f) do so within 48 hours after the request was given.\n\n(4) If, under subsection (3):\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security; or",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A technical assistance request may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(2) A technical assistance request must not be given orally unless:\n\n(a) an imminent risk of serious harm to a person or substantial\ndamage to property exists; and\n\n(b) the technical assistance request is necessary for the purpose\nof dealing with that risk; and\n\n(c) it is not practicable in the circumstances to give the technical\nassistance request in writing.\n\n(3) If a technical assistance request is given orally by:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security; or\n\n(b) the Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService; or\n\n(c) the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(d) the chief officer of an interception agency;\nthe Director-General of Security, the Director-General of the\nAustralian Secret Intelligence Service, the Director-General of the\nAustralian Signals Directorate or the chief officer, as the case\nrequires, must:\n\n(e) make a written record of the request; and\n\n(f) do so within 48 hours after the request was given.\n\n(4) If, under subsection (3):\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security; or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317h-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f4d264a48add87d69733add367c4eb741ed0931b17ee13b894eaf1bd0631310"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317H Form of technical assistance request",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A technical assistance request may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(2) A technical assistance request must not be given orally unless:\n\n(a) an imminent risk of serious harm to a person or substantial\ndamage to property exists; and\n\n(b) the technical assistance request is necessary for the purpose\nof dealing with that risk; and\n\n(c) it is not practicable in the circumstances to give the technical\nassistance request in writing.\n\n(3) If a technical assistance request is given orally by:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security; or\n\n(b) the Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence\nService; or\n\n(c) the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate; or\n\n(d) the chief officer of an interception agency;\nthe Director-General of Security, the Director-General of the\nAustralian Secret Intelligence Service, the Director-General of the\nAustralian Signals Directorate or the chief officer, as the case\nrequires, must:\n\n(e) make a written record of the request; and\n\n(f) do so within 48 hours after the request was given.\n\n(4) If, under subsection (3):\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security; or"
    },
