    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317J Specified period etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A technical assistance request may include a request that a\nspecified act or thing be done within a specified period.\n\n(2) A technical assistance request may include a request that a\nspecified act or thing be done:\n\n(a) in a specified manner; or\n\n(b) in a way that meets one or more specified conditions.\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) of this section do not limit\nsubsections 317G(1) and (2).\n317JAA  Decision-making criteria\n\n(1) The Director-General of Security must not give a technical\nassistance request to a designated communications provider unless\nthe Director-General of Security is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the request is reasonable and proportionate; and\n\n(b) compliance with the request is:\n\n(i) practicable; and\n\n(ii) technically feasible.\nNote:\nSee also section 317JC.\n\n(2) The Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence Service\nmust not give a technical assistance request to a designated\ncommunications provider unless the Director-General of the\nAustralian Secret Intelligence Service is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the request is reasonable and proportionate; and\n\n(b) compliance with the request is:\n\n(i) practicable; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A technical assistance request may include a request that a\nspecified act or thing be done within a specified period.\n\n(2) A technical assistance request may include a request that a\nspecified act or thing be done:\n\n(a) in a specified manner; or\n\n(b) in a way that meets one or more specified conditions.\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) of this section do not limit\nsubsections 317G(1) and (2).\n317JAA  Decision-making criteria\n\n(1) The Director-General of Security must not give a technical\nassistance request to a designated communications provider unless\nthe Director-General of Security is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the request is reasonable and proportionate; and\n\n(b) compliance with the request is:\n\n(i) practicable; and\n\n(ii) technically feasible.\nNote:\nSee also section 317JC.\n\n(2) The Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence Service\nmust not give a technical assistance request to a designated\ncommunications provider unless the Director-General of the\nAustralian Secret Intelligence Service is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the request is reasonable and proportionate; and\n\n(b) compliance with the request is:\n\n(i) practicable; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "17ac6d22656de8e07041226ac9cda4e391988c124069b53a9d23fca79a52537b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317J Specified period etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A technical assistance request may include a request that a\nspecified act or thing be done within a specified period.\n\n(2) A technical assistance request may include a request that a\nspecified act or thing be done:\n\n(a) in a specified manner; or\n\n(b) in a way that meets one or more specified conditions.\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) of this section do not limit\nsubsections 317G(1) and (2).\n317JAA  Decision-making criteria\n\n(1) The Director-General of Security must not give a technical\nassistance request to a designated communications provider unless\nthe Director-General of Security is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the request is reasonable and proportionate; and\n\n(b) compliance with the request is:\n\n(i) practicable; and\n\n(ii) technically feasible.\nNote:\nSee also section 317JC.\n\n(2) The Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence Service\nmust not give a technical assistance request to a designated\ncommunications provider unless the Director-General of the\nAustralian Secret Intelligence Service is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the request is reasonable and proportionate; and\n\n(b) compliance with the request is:\n\n(i) practicable; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317j-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317J(1) Specified period etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317j-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
