    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317la",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317LA Approval of technical assistance notices given by the chief",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317la"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "officer of an interception agency of a State or Territory\n\n(1) The chief officer of an interception agency of a State or Territory\nmust not give a technical assistance notice to a designated\ncommunications provider unless:\n\n(a) the chief officer has given the AFP Commissioner a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to give the technical assistance\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the AFP Commissioner has approved the giving of the\ntechnical assistance notice.\n\n(2) An approval under paragraph (1)(b) may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(3) If an approval under paragraph (1)(b) is given orally, the AFP\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the approval; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the approval was given.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, AFP Commissioner means the\nCommissioner (within the meaning of the Australian Federal\nPolice Act 1979).",
      "skos:definition": "officer of an interception agency of a State or Territory\n\n(1) The chief officer of an interception agency of a State or Territory\nmust not give a technical assistance notice to a designated\ncommunications provider unless:\n\n(a) the chief officer has given the AFP Commissioner a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to give the technical assistance\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the AFP Commissioner has approved the giving of the\ntechnical assistance notice.\n\n(2) An approval under paragraph (1)(b) may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(3) If an approval under paragraph (1)(b) is given orally, the AFP\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the approval; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the approval was given.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, AFP Commissioner means the\nCommissioner (within the meaning of the Australian Federal\nPolice Act 1979).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317la-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317la-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317la-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317la-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76662355dba39e7993e681dced0433ab630f2cbec4becac630dc61a6a1719d2f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317la",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317LA Approval of technical assistance notices given by the chief",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "officer of an interception agency of a State or Territory\n\n(1) The chief officer of an interception agency of a State or Territory\nmust not give a technical assistance notice to a designated\ncommunications provider unless:\n\n(a) the chief officer has given the AFP Commissioner a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to give the technical assistance\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the AFP Commissioner has approved the giving of the\ntechnical assistance notice.\n\n(2) An approval under paragraph (1)(b) may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(3) If an approval under paragraph (1)(b) is given orally, the AFP\nCommissioner must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the approval; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the approval was given.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, AFP Commissioner means the\nCommissioner (within the meaning of the Australian Federal\nPolice Act 1979)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317la-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317LA(1) Approval of technical assistance notices given by the chief",
