      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a variation is made orally by the Director-General of Security or\nthe chief officer of an interception agency, the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the variation; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the variation was made.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a variation is made orally by the Director-General of Security or\nthe chief officer of an interception agency, the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the variation; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the variation was made.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
