        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d895f6cca39766b433011177673a708ed974368cb2a52a1e0be48731c3e2cf82",
      "skos:note": "Must make a written record of oral variation within 48 hours",
      "dc:description": "Written record of variation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317q-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317Q(5) Variation of technical assistance notices",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a variation is made orally by the Director-General of Security or\nthe chief officer of an interception agency, the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the variation; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the variation was made."
    },
    {
