    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317q-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317Q(6) Variation of technical assistance notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317q-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If, under subsection (5), the Director-General of Security or the\nchief officer of an interception agency makes a written record of a\nvariation, the Director-General of Security or the chief officer, as\nthe case requires, must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the record to the designated communications\nprovider concerned; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the record was made.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If, under subsection (5), the Director-General of Security or the\nchief officer of an interception agency makes a written record of a\nvariation, the Director-General of Security or the chief officer, as\nthe case requires, must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the record to the designated communications\nprovider concerned; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the record was made.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
