        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "764b2e3dd325a216b5214c84f203a23f7a439a142230a85428f5f8953285fe8b",
      "skos:note": "Must provide a copy of the record to the designated communications provider concerned",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317q-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317Q(6) Variation of technical assistance notices",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If, under subsection (5), the Director-General of Security or the\nchief officer of an interception agency makes a written record of a\nvariation, the Director-General of Security or the chief officer, as\nthe case requires, must:\n\n(a) give a copy of the record to the designated communications\nprovider concerned; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after the record was made."
