      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) If a technical assistance notice has been given to a person by the chief officer of an interception agency, and the chief officer is satisfied that: (a) the requirements imposed by the notice are not reasonable and proportionate; or (b) compliance with the notice is not: (i) practicable; and (ii) technically feasible;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(the time period during which the revocation must be given)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317r-ss-4-logic-ltl-3",
