      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317ra",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317RA Whether requirements imposed by a technical assistance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317ra"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "notice are reasonable and proportionate\n\nIn considering whether the requirements imposed by a technical\nassistance notice or a varied technical assistance notice are\nreasonable and proportionate, the Director-General of Security or\nthe chief officer of an interception agency, as the case requires,\nmust have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the interests of national security;\n\n(b) the interests of law enforcement;\n\n(c) the legitimate interests of the designated communications\nprovider to whom the notice relates;\n\n(d) the objectives of the notice;\n\n(e) the availability of other means to achieve the objectives of\nthe notice;\n\n(ea) whether the requirements, when compared to other forms of\nindustry assistance known to the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, are the least\nintrusive form of industry assistance so far as the following\npersons are concerned:\n\n(i) persons whose activities are not of interest to ASIO;\n\n(ii) persons whose activities are not of interest to\ninterception agencies;\n\n(eb) whether the requirements are necessary;\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical assistance notices  Division 3\n\nSection 317RA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(f) the legitimate expectations of the Australian community\nrelating to privacy and cybersecurity;\n\n(g) such other matters (if any) as the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, considers\nrelevant.",
      "skos:definition": "notice are reasonable and proportionate\n\nIn considering whether the requirements imposed by a technical\nassistance notice or a varied technical assistance notice are\nreasonable and proportionate, the Director-General of Security or\nthe chief officer of an interception agency, as the case requires,\nmust have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the interests of national security;\n\n(b) the interests of law enforcement;\n\n(c) the legitimate interests of the designated communications\nprovider to whom the notice relates;\n\n(d) the objectives of the notice;\n\n(e) the availability of other means to achieve the objectives of\nthe notice;\n\n(ea) whether the requirements, when compared to other forms of\nindustry assistance known to the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, are the least\nintrusive form of industry assistance so far as the following\npersons are concerned:\n\n(i) persons whose activities are not of interest to ASIO;\n\n(ii) persons whose activities are not of interest to\ninterception agencies;\n\n(eb) whether the requirements are necessary;\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical assistance notices  Division 3\n\nSection 317RA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(f) the legitimate expectations of the Australian community\nrelating to privacy and cybersecurity;\n\n(g) such other matters (if any) as the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, considers\nrelevant.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317ra-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317ra-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317ra-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9adb7ad9e4f0fd49a2d654615794a46119e07dcb2301830cdd27ff3599389799",
      "skos:note": "Director-General of Security or chief officer must consider various matters when determining whether requirements imposed by a technical assistance notice are reasonable and proportionate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317ra",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317RA Whether requirements imposed by a technical assistance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "notice are reasonable and proportionate\n\nIn considering whether the requirements imposed by a technical\nassistance notice or a varied technical assistance notice are\nreasonable and proportionate, the Director-General of Security or\nthe chief officer of an interception agency, as the case requires,\nmust have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) the interests of national security;\n\n(b) the interests of law enforcement;\n\n(c) the legitimate interests of the designated communications\nprovider to whom the notice relates;\n\n(d) the objectives of the notice;\n\n(e) the availability of other means to achieve the objectives of\nthe notice;\n\n(ea) whether the requirements, when compared to other forms of\nindustry assistance known to the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, are the least\nintrusive form of industry assistance so far as the following\npersons are concerned:\n\n(i) persons whose activities are not of interest to ASIO;\n\n(ii) persons whose activities are not of interest to\ninterception agencies;\n\n(eb) whether the requirements are necessary;\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical assistance notices  Division 3\n\nSection 317RA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(f) the legitimate expectations of the Australian community\nrelating to privacy and cybersecurity;\n\n(g) such other matters (if any) as the Director-General of\nSecurity or the chief officer, as the case requires, considers\nrelevant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317ra-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
