      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317XA Approval of variation of technical capability notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317xa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a designated\ncommunications provider, the Attorney-General must not vary the\nnotice unless:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has given the Minister a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to vary the technical\ncapability notice; and\n\n(ii) the Minister has approved the variation of the technical\ncapability notice; or\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical capability notices  Division 4\n\nSection 317XA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the provider has waived compliance with subsection 317Y(2)\nin relation to the variation of the technical capability notice.\n\n(2) An approval under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(3) If an approval under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) is given orally, the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the approval; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the approval was given.\n\n(4) The Attorney-General may make a representation to the Minister\nabout the proposal to vary the technical capability notice.\n\n(5) A representation may deal with:\n\n(a) any of the matters set out in section 317ZAA; and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the Attorney-General considers\nrelevant.\n\n(6) In considering whether to approve the variation of the technical\ncapability notice, the Minister must have regard to the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the objectives of the notice as proposed to be varied;\n\n(b) the legitimate interests of the designated communications\nprovider to whom the notice relates;\n\n(c) the impact of the notice as proposed to be varied on the\nefficiency and international competitiveness of the Australian\ntelecommunications industry;\n\n(d) the representation (if any) that was made under\nsubsection (4);\n\n(e) such other matters (if any) as the Minister considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a designated\ncommunications provider, the Attorney-General must not vary the\nnotice unless:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has given the Minister a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to vary the technical\ncapability notice; and\n\n(ii) the Minister has approved the variation of the technical\ncapability notice; or\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical capability notices  Division 4\n\nSection 317XA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the provider has waived compliance with subsection 317Y(2)\nin relation to the variation of the technical capability notice.\n\n(2) An approval under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(3) If an approval under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) is given orally, the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the approval; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the approval was given.\n\n(4) The Attorney-General may make a representation to the Minister\nabout the proposal to vary the technical capability notice.\n\n(5) A representation may deal with:\n\n(a) any of the matters set out in section 317ZAA; and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the Attorney-General considers\nrelevant.\n\n(6) In considering whether to approve the variation of the technical\ncapability notice, the Minister must have regard to the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the objectives of the notice as proposed to be varied;\n\n(b) the legitimate interests of the designated communications\nprovider to whom the notice relates;\n\n(c) the impact of the notice as proposed to be varied on the\nefficiency and international competitiveness of the Australian\ntelecommunications industry;\n\n(d) the representation (if any) that was made under\nsubsection (4);\n\n(e) such other matters (if any) as the Minister considers relevant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5b4caa29a694375f58f0da3286c29beff0ec52ddb07a439d1e30f40007a89a63"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317xa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317XA Approval of variation of technical capability notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a designated\ncommunications provider, the Attorney-General must not vary the\nnotice unless:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has given the Minister a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to vary the technical\ncapability notice; and\n\n(ii) the Minister has approved the variation of the technical\ncapability notice; or\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical capability notices  Division 4\n\nSection 317XA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the provider has waived compliance with subsection 317Y(2)\nin relation to the variation of the technical capability notice.\n\n(2) An approval under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) may be given:\n\n(a) orally; or\n\n(b) in writing.\n\n(3) If an approval under subparagraph (1)(a)(ii) is given orally, the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) make a written record of the approval; and\n\n(b) do so within 48 hours after the approval was given.\n\n(4) The Attorney-General may make a representation to the Minister\nabout the proposal to vary the technical capability notice.\n\n(5) A representation may deal with:\n\n(a) any of the matters set out in section 317ZAA; and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the Attorney-General considers\nrelevant.\n\n(6) In considering whether to approve the variation of the technical\ncapability notice, the Minister must have regard to the following\nmatters:\n\n(a) the objectives of the notice as proposed to be varied;\n\n(b) the legitimate interests of the designated communications\nprovider to whom the notice relates;\n\n(c) the impact of the notice as proposed to be varied on the\nefficiency and international competitiveness of the Australian\ntelecommunications industry;\n\n(d) the representation (if any) that was made under\nsubsection (4);\n\n(e) such other matters (if any) as the Minister considers relevant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1",
