      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a designated\ncommunications provider, the Attorney-General must not vary the\nnotice unless:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has given the Minister a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to vary the technical\ncapability notice; and\n\n(ii) the Minister has approved the variation of the technical\ncapability notice; or\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical capability notices  Division 4\n\nSection 317XA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the provider has waived compliance with subsection 317Y(2)\nin relation to the variation of the technical capability notice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a designated\ncommunications provider, the Attorney-General must not vary the\nnotice unless:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has given the Minister a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to vary the technical\ncapability notice; and\n\n(ii) the Minister has approved the variation of the technical\ncapability notice; or\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical capability notices  Division 4\n\nSection 317XA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the provider has waived compliance with subsection 317Y(2)\nin relation to the variation of the technical capability notice.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317xa-ss-1-logic-ltl-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a182c708420aead1e92e26af0fea05b7d24ce6551d45baa0b05daf005b56864e",
      "skos:note": "The Attorney-General must not vary the technical capability notice without approval from the Minister or waiver by the provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317xa-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317XA(1) Approval of variation of technical capability notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a designated\ncommunications provider, the Attorney-General must not vary the\nnotice unless:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has given the Minister a written\nnotice setting out a proposal to vary the technical\ncapability notice; and\n\n(ii) the Minister has approved the variation of the technical\ncapability notice; or\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nTechnical capability notices  Division 4\n\nSection 317XA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the provider has waived compliance with subsection 317Y(2)\nin relation to the variation of the technical capability notice."
    },
