    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317Z Revocation of technical capability notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.109",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a person, the\nAttorney-General may, by written notice given to the person,\nrevoke the notice.\n\n(2) If a technical capability notice has been given to a person, and the\nAttorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the requirements imposed by the notice are not reasonable\nand proportionate; or\n\n(b) compliance with the notice is not:\n\n(i) practicable; and\n\n(ii) technically feasible;\nthe Attorney-General must, by written notice given to the person,\nrevoke the notice.\nNotification obligations\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General revokes a technical capability notice;\nand\n\n(b) the acts or things specified in the revoked notice:\n\n(i) are directed towards ensuring that a designated\ncommunications provider is capable of giving listed\nhelp (within the meaning of section 317T) to ASIO in\nrelation to a matter covered by paragraph 317T(2)(a); or\n\n(ii) are by way of giving help to ASIO in relation to a\nmatter covered by paragraph 317T(2)(b);",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a person, the\nAttorney-General may, by written notice given to the person,\nrevoke the notice.\n\n(2) If a technical capability notice has been given to a person, and the\nAttorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the requirements imposed by the notice are not reasonable\nand proportionate; or\n\n(b) compliance with the notice is not:\n\n(i) practicable; and\n\n(ii) technically feasible;\nthe Attorney-General must, by written notice given to the person,\nrevoke the notice.\nNotification obligations\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General revokes a technical capability notice;\nand\n\n(b) the acts or things specified in the revoked notice:\n\n(i) are directed towards ensuring that a designated\ncommunications provider is capable of giving listed\nhelp (within the meaning of section 317T) to ASIO in\nrelation to a matter covered by paragraph 317T(2)(a); or\n\n(ii) are by way of giving help to ASIO in relation to a\nmatter covered by paragraph 317T(2)(b);",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317z-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317z-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317z-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f04e366c20c2ae1f0fc7e7f44dc4dba92567b51a2c03e66964b5a6e0781f3a9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317Z Revocation of technical capability notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 109,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a technical capability notice has been given to a person, the\nAttorney-General may, by written notice given to the person,\nrevoke the notice.\n\n(2) If a technical capability notice has been given to a person, and the\nAttorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the requirements imposed by the notice are not reasonable\nand proportionate; or\n\n(b) compliance with the notice is not:\n\n(i) practicable; and\n\n(ii) technically feasible;\nthe Attorney-General must, by written notice given to the person,\nrevoke the notice.\nNotification obligations\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General revokes a technical capability notice;\nand\n\n(b) the acts or things specified in the revoked notice:\n\n(i) are directed towards ensuring that a designated\ncommunications provider is capable of giving listed\nhelp (within the meaning of section 317T) to ASIO in\nrelation to a matter covered by paragraph 317T(2)(a); or\n\n(ii) are by way of giving help to ASIO in relation to a\nmatter covered by paragraph 317T(2)(b);"
    },
