    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317za",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317ZA Compliance with notices—carriers and carriage service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317za"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "providers\n\n(1) A carrier or carriage service provider must comply with a\nrequirement under:\n\n(a) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(b) a technical capability notice;\nto the extent that the carrier or provider is capable of doing so.\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "skos:definition": "providers\n\n(1) A carrier or carriage service provider must comply with a\nrequirement under:\n\n(a) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(b) a technical capability notice;\nto the extent that the carrier or provider is capable of doing so.\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317za-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317za-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317za-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1e19bab29bc6432a45375515ae332f5fc9540db0100ac0b05c3ccb42923c189d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317za",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317ZA Compliance with notices—carriers and carriage service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "providers\n\n(1) A carrier or carriage service provider must comply with a\nrequirement under:\n\n(a) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(b) a technical capability notice;\nto the extent that the carrier or provider is capable of doing so.\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions."
    },
