    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317ZD Enforceable undertakings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317zd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.114",
      "values:originalText": "Enforceable provision\n\n(1) Section 317ZB of this Act is enforceable under Part 6 of the\nRegulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014.\nAuthorised person\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator is an authorised person in\nrelation to section 317ZB of this Act for the purposes of Part 6 of\nthe Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014.\nRelevant courts\n\n(3) The Federal Court and the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) are relevant courts in relation to\nsection 317ZB of this Act for the purposes of Part 6 of the\nRegulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014.\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nCompliance and enforcement  Division 5\n\nSection 317ZE\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nExtension to external Territories etc.\n\n(4) Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014,\nas it applies in relation to section 317ZB of this Act, extends to:\n\n(a) every external Territory; and\n\n(b) acts, omissions, matters and things outside Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "Enforceable provision\n\n(1) Section 317ZB of this Act is enforceable under Part 6 of the\nRegulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014.\nAuthorised person\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator is an authorised person in\nrelation to section 317ZB of this Act for the purposes of Part 6 of\nthe Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014.\nRelevant courts\n\n(3) The Federal Court and the Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) are relevant courts in relation to\nsection 317ZB of this Act for the purposes of Part 6 of the\nRegulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014.\n\n\nIndustry assistance  Part 15\nCompliance and enforcement  Division 5\n\nSection 317ZE\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nExtension to external Territories etc.\n\n(4) Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014,\nas it applies in relation to section 317ZB of this Act, extends to:\n\n(a) every external Territory; and\n\n(b) acts, omissions, matters and things outside Australia.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zd-ss-2"
