    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zg-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317ZG(4A) Designated communications provider must not be requested",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317zg-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) In a case where a weakness is selectively introduced to one or more\ntarget technologies that are connected with a particular person, the\nreference in paragraph (1)(a) to implement or build a systemic\nweakness into a form of electronic protection includes a reference\nto any act or thing that will, or is likely to, jeopardise the security\nof any information held by any other person.",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) In a case where a weakness is selectively introduced to one or more\ntarget technologies that are connected with a particular person, the\nreference in paragraph (1)(a) to implement or build a systemic\nweakness into a form of electronic protection includes a reference\nto any act or thing that will, or is likely to, jeopardise the security\nof any information held by any other person.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zg"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zg-ss-4a-norm"
