      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317ZJ Immunity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317zj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.135",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A designated communications provider is not subject to any civil\nliability for, or in relation to, an act or thing done by the provider:\n\n(a) in compliance; or\n\n(b) in good faith in purported compliance;\nwith:\n\n(c) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(d) a technical capability notice.\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to an act or thing done by a\ndesignated communications provider unless the act or thing is in\nconnection with any or all of the eligible activities of the provider.\n\n(3) An officer, employee or agent of a designated communications\nprovider is not subject to any civil liability for, or in relation to, an\nact or thing done by the officer, employee or agent in connection\nwith an act or thing done by the provider:\n\n(a) in compliance; or\n\n(b) in good faith in purported compliance;\nwith:\n\n(c) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(d) a technical capability notice.\n\n(4) Paragraph (3)(b) does not apply to an act or thing done by a\ndesignated communications provider unless the act or thing is in\nconnection with any or all of the eligible activities of the provider.\n317ZK  Terms and conditions on which help is to be given etc.\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if a designated communications provider is\nsubject to a requirement under:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A designated communications provider is not subject to any civil\nliability for, or in relation to, an act or thing done by the provider:\n\n(a) in compliance; or\n\n(b) in good faith in purported compliance;\nwith:\n\n(c) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(d) a technical capability notice.\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to an act or thing done by a\ndesignated communications provider unless the act or thing is in\nconnection with any or all of the eligible activities of the provider.\n\n(3) An officer, employee or agent of a designated communications\nprovider is not subject to any civil liability for, or in relation to, an\nact or thing done by the officer, employee or agent in connection\nwith an act or thing done by the provider:\n\n(a) in compliance; or\n\n(b) in good faith in purported compliance;\nwith:\n\n(c) a technical assistance notice; or\n\n(d) a technical capability notice.\n\n(4) Paragraph (3)(b) does not apply to an act or thing done by a\ndesignated communications provider unless the act or thing is in\nconnection with any or all of the eligible activities of the provider.\n317ZK  Terms and conditions on which help is to be given etc.\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if a designated communications provider is\nsubject to a requirement under:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zj-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zj-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zj-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zj-ss-4"
        },
        {
