    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "317ZR Delegation by the chief officer of an interception agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317zr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.151",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an interception agency mentioned in an item of\ncolumn 1 of the following table may, by writing, delegate any or\nall of the functions or powers of the chief officer under Division 2,\n3 or 6 to a person mentioned in column 2 of the item.\n\nPotential delegates\nItem\nColumn 1\nColumn 2\n\nInterception\nagency\nPotential delegates\nAustralian\nFederal Police\n(a) a Deputy Commissioner (within the meaning of the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979); or\n(b) a senior executive AFP employee (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979)\nAustralian\nCrime\nCommission\na member of the staff of the ACC (within the meaning of\nthe Australian Crime Commission Act 2002) who is an\nSES employee or acting SES employee\n3A\nNational\nAnti-Corruption\nCommission\na staff member of the NACC (within the meaning of the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) who is\na Deputy Commissioner, SES employee or acting SES\nemployee\nPolice Force of a\nState or the\nNorthern\nTerritory\n(a) an Assistant Commissioner of the Police Force or a\nperson holding equivalent rank; or\n(b) a Superintendent of the Police Force or a person\nholding equivalent rank\nIndependent\nCommission\nAgainst\nCorruption of\nNew South\nWales\n(a) a Commissioner (within the meaning of the\nIndependent Commission Against Corruption Act\n1988 (NSW)); or\n(b) an Assistant Commissioner (within the meaning of\nthe Independent Commission Against Corruption Act\n1988 (NSW)); or\n(c) an officer of the Commission (within the meaning of\nthe Independent Commission Against Corruption Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an interception agency mentioned in an item of\ncolumn 1 of the following table may, by writing, delegate any or\nall of the functions or powers of the chief officer under Division 2,\n3 or 6 to a person mentioned in column 2 of the item.\n\nPotential delegates\nItem\nColumn 1\nColumn 2\n\nInterception\nagency\nPotential delegates\nAustralian\nFederal Police\n(a) a Deputy Commissioner (within the meaning of the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979); or\n(b) a senior executive AFP employee (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979)\nAustralian\nCrime\nCommission\na member of the staff of the ACC (within the meaning of\nthe Australian Crime Commission Act 2002) who is an\nSES employee or acting SES employee\n3A\nNational\nAnti-Corruption\nCommission\na staff member of the NACC (within the meaning of the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) who is\na Deputy Commissioner, SES employee or acting SES\nemployee\nPolice Force of a\nState or the\nNorthern\nTerritory\n(a) an Assistant Commissioner of the Police Force or a\nperson holding equivalent rank; or\n(b) a Superintendent of the Police Force or a person\nholding equivalent rank\nIndependent\nCommission\nAgainst\nCorruption of\nNew South\nWales\n(a) a Commissioner (within the meaning of the\nIndependent Commission Against Corruption Act\n1988 (NSW)); or\n(b) an Assistant Commissioner (within the meaning of\nthe Independent Commission Against Corruption Act\n1988 (NSW)); or\n(c) an officer of the Commission (within the meaning of\nthe Independent Commission Against Corruption Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zr-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zr-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b1d24fb313f855a6036d4a48377e1fbb75d181be91b307dace9855476abf74d",
      "skos:note": "Delegate functions or powers to a person"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-317zr",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "317ZR Delegation by the chief officer of an interception agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 151,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an interception agency mentioned in an item of\ncolumn 1 of the following table may, by writing, delegate any or\nall of the functions or powers of the chief officer under Division 2,\n3 or 6 to a person mentioned in column 2 of the item.\n\nPotential delegates\nItem\nColumn 1\nColumn 2\n\nInterception\nagency\nPotential delegates\nAustralian\nFederal Police\n(a) a Deputy Commissioner (within the meaning of the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979); or\n(b) a senior executive AFP employee (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979)\nAustralian\nCrime\nCommission\na member of the staff of the ACC (within the meaning of\nthe Australian Crime Commission Act 2002) who is an\nSES employee or acting SES employee\n3A\nNational\nAnti-Corruption\nCommission\na staff member of the NACC (within the meaning of the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022) who is\na Deputy Commissioner, SES employee or acting SES\nemployee\nPolice Force of a\nState or the\nNorthern\nTerritory\n(a) an Assistant Commissioner of the Police Force or a\nperson holding equivalent rank; or\n(b) a Superintendent of the Police Force or a person\nholding equivalent rank\nIndependent\nCommission\nAgainst\nCorruption of\nNew South\nWales\n(a) a Commissioner (within the meaning of the\nIndependent Commission Against Corruption Act\n1988 (NSW)); or\n(b) an Assistant Commissioner (within the meaning of\nthe Independent Commission Against Corruption Act\n1988 (NSW)); or\n(c) an officer of the Commission (within the meaning of\nthe Independent Commission Against Corruption Act"
    },
