    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-335-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "335(4) Requirement to supply carriage services for defence purposes or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-335-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.158",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a requirement is in force, the provider must supply the carriage\nservice in accordance with the requirement and on such terms and\nconditions as are:\n\n(a) agreed between the provider and the defence authority; or\n\n(b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by\nthe parties.\nIf the parties cannot agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the\nACCC is to be the arbitrator.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If a requirement is in force, the provider must supply the carriage\nservice in accordance with the requirement and on such terms and\nconditions as are:\n\n(a) agreed between the provider and the defence authority; or\n\n(b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by\nthe parties.\nIf the parties cannot agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the\nACCC is to be the arbitrator.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-335"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-335-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-335-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "25543d45ef9847de4480a36eaa8cfb19377773a0b0709b2dabbfe0e939598eeb",
      "skos:note": "Provider must supply carriage service in accordance with requirement and on agreed terms or determined by arbitrator.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-335-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "335(4) Requirement to supply carriage services for defence purposes or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 158,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a requirement is in force, the provider must supply the carriage\nservice in accordance with the requirement and on such terms and\nconditions as are:\n\n(a) agreed between the provider and the defence authority; or\n\n(b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by\nthe parties.\nIf the parties cannot agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the\nACCC is to be the arbitrator."
    },
