    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-336",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "336 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-336"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "In this Division:\ncertified agreement has the meaning given by section 338.\ncrisis means:\n\n(a) war, war-like conflict or war-like operations; or\n\n(b) civil disturbance; or\n\n(c) terrorism; or\n\n(d) earthquakes, floods, fire, cyclones, storms or other disasters\n(whether natural or resulting from the acts or omissions of\nhumans).\ndraft agreement means a draft agreement prepared under\nsection 337.\nnetwork survivability means the ability of a telecommunications\nnetwork, or of a facility, to continue to function in times of crisis.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Division:\ncertified agreement has the meaning given by section 338.\ncrisis means:\n\n(a) war, war-like conflict or war-like operations; or\n\n(b) civil disturbance; or\n\n(c) terrorism; or\n\n(d) earthquakes, floods, fire, cyclones, storms or other disasters\n(whether natural or resulting from the acts or omissions of\nhumans).\ndraft agreement means a draft agreement prepared under\nsection 337.\nnetwork survivability means the ability of a telecommunications\nnetwork, or of a facility, to continue to function in times of crisis.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-336-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "844c2449283dafedc0174b8a4a21306420102f715ce5c0bb02bdec3aa7a3f0ad",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for crisis, draft agreement, and network survivability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-336",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "336 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "In this Division:\ncertified agreement has the meaning given by section 338.\ncrisis means:\n\n(a) war, war-like conflict or war-like operations; or\n\n(b) civil disturbance; or\n\n(c) terrorism; or\n\n(d) earthquakes, floods, fire, cyclones, storms or other disasters\n(whether natural or resulting from the acts or omissions of\nhumans).\ndraft agreement means a draft agreement prepared under\nsection 337.\nnetwork survivability means the ability of a telecommunications\nnetwork, or of a facility, to continue to function in times of crisis."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-336-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-336"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-337",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "337 Preparation of draft agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-337"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A defence authority may prepare a draft agreement to be entered\ninto by the defence authority (on behalf of the Commonwealth)\nand:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a carriage service provider.\n\n(2) The agreement must be about:\n\n(a) planning for network survivability; or\n\n(b) operational requirements in times of crisis;\nor both.\n\n(3) In preparing the draft agreement, the defence authority must\nconsult the carrier or provider concerned.\n\n\nDefence requirements and disaster plans  Part 16\nDefence planning  Division 3\n\nSection 338\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A defence authority may prepare a draft agreement to be entered\ninto by the defence authority (on behalf of the Commonwealth)\nand:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a carriage service provider.\n\n(2) The agreement must be about:\n\n(a) planning for network survivability; or\n\n(b) operational requirements in times of crisis;\nor both.\n\n(3) In preparing the draft agreement, the defence authority must\nconsult the carrier or provider concerned.\n\n\nDefence requirements and disaster plans  Part 16\nDefence planning  Division 3\n\nSection 338\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-337-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-337-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-337-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3334ca1a008774468fa4c9546fc2d44a6e412b98581f880c1d01b105e2b0469a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-337",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "337 Preparation of draft agreement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A defence authority may prepare a draft agreement to be entered\ninto by the defence authority (on behalf of the Commonwealth)\nand:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a carriage service provider.\n\n(2) The agreement must be about:\n\n(a) planning for network survivability; or\n\n(b) operational requirements in times of crisis;\nor both.\n\n(3) In preparing the draft agreement, the defence authority must\nconsult the carrier or provider concerned.\n\n\nDefence requirements and disaster plans  Part 16\nDefence planning  Division 3\n\nSection 338\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
