      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA must make a written determination requiring each\ncarrier or carriage service provider who supplies a specified\ndeclared carriage service to:\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 349\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) provide pre-selection in favour of a specified carriage service\nprovider, in relation to calls made using the carriage service,\nin the manner specified in the determination; and\n\n(b) comply with such ancillary or incidental rules (if any) as are\nset out in the determination.\nNote:\nDeclared carriage service is defined by section 350A.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The ACMA must make a written determination requiring each\ncarrier or carriage service provider who supplies a specified\ndeclared carriage service to:\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 349\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) provide pre-selection in favour of a specified carriage service\nprovider, in relation to calls made using the carriage service,\nin the manner specified in the determination; and\n\n(b) comply with such ancillary or incidental rules (if any) as are\nset out in the determination.\nNote:\nDeclared carriage service is defined by section 350A.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
