    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "349A(1) Local access line",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-349a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carrier to\nprovide pre-selection in favour of a carriage service provider in\nrelation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and\nonly if, the determination requires:\n\n(a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the carrier\nto permit an end-user to:\n\n(i) pre-select the carriage service provider as the end-user’s\npreferred carriage service provider for such of the\nend-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using\nthat carriage service, as are specified in the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) change that selection from time to time; and\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 350\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the carrier\nto provide over-ride dial codes for selecting alternative\ncarriage service providers, in relation to calls made using that\ncarriage service, on a call-by-call basis.\nNote:\nEnd-user is defined by subsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carrier to\nprovide pre-selection in favour of a carriage service provider in\nrelation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and\nonly if, the determination requires:\n\n(a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the carrier\nto permit an end-user to:\n\n(i) pre-select the carriage service provider as the end-user’s\npreferred carriage service provider for such of the\nend-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using\nthat carriage service, as are specified in the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) change that selection from time to time; and\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 350\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the carrier\nto provide over-ride dial codes for selecting alternative\ncarriage service providers, in relation to calls made using that\ncarriage service, on a call-by-call basis.\nNote:\nEnd-user is defined by subsection (3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2424d3eef99e6d22be278da57457b88c58424ac014311b9422b2940a35b7119e",
      "skos:note": "Definition of local access line Carrier must provide pre-selection in favour of carriage service provider.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-349a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "349A(1) Local access line",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carrier to\nprovide pre-selection in favour of a carriage service provider in\nrelation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and\nonly if, the determination requires:\n\n(a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the carrier\nto permit an end-user to:\n\n(i) pre-select the carriage service provider as the end-user’s\npreferred carriage service provider for such of the\nend-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using\nthat carriage service, as are specified in the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) change that selection from time to time; and\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 350\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the carrier\nto provide over-ride dial codes for selecting alternative\ncarriage service providers, in relation to calls made using that\ncarriage service, on a call-by-call basis.\nNote:\nEnd-user is defined by subsection (3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is part of",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Part-of relation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Local access line",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Local access network infrastructure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-1-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Carrier must provide pre-selection.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "349A(2) Local access line",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-349a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carriage\nservice provider (the first provider) to provide pre-selection in\nfavour of another carriage service provider (the second provider)\nin relation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and\nonly if, the determination requires:\n\n(a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first\nprovider to permit an end-user to:\n\n(i) pre-select the second provider as the end-user’s\npreferred carriage service provider for such of the\nend-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using\nthat carriage service, as are specified in the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) change that selection from time to time; and\n\n(c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first\nprovider to provide over-ride dial codes for selecting\nalternative carriage service providers, in relation to calls\nmade using that carriage service, on a call-by-call basis.\nNote:\nEnd-user is defined by subsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carriage\nservice provider (the first provider) to provide pre-selection in\nfavour of another carriage service provider (the second provider)\nin relation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and\nonly if, the determination requires:\n\n(a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first\nprovider to permit an end-user to:\n\n(i) pre-select the second provider as the end-user’s\npreferred carriage service provider for such of the\nend-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using\nthat carriage service, as are specified in the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) change that selection from time to time; and\n\n(c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first\nprovider to provide over-ride dial codes for selecting\nalternative carriage service providers, in relation to calls\nmade using that carriage service, on a call-by-call basis.\nNote:\nEnd-user is defined by subsection (3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56d1bab64a06bbbaa987c6fcef2050ad65f9cb841a451100651515a788996ce3",
      "skos:note": "Carriage service provider must provide pre-selection in favour of another provider. Line does not form part of a local access line to the extent that it is on the customer side of the boundary of a telecommunications network.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-349a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "349A(2) Local access line",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carriage\nservice provider (the first provider) to provide pre-selection in\nfavour of another carriage service provider (the second provider)\nin relation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and\nonly if, the determination requires:\n\n(a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first\nprovider to permit an end-user to:\n\n(i) pre-select the second provider as the end-user’s\npreferred carriage service provider for such of the\nend-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using\nthat carriage service, as are specified in the\ndetermination; and\n\n(ii) change that selection from time to time; and\n\n(c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first\nprovider to provide over-ride dial codes for selecting\nalternative carriage service providers, in relation to calls\nmade using that carriage service, on a call-by-call basis.\nNote:\nEnd-user is defined by subsection (3)."
    },
    {
