    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-350a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "350A Declared carriage services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-350a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may, by written instrument, declare that a specified\ncarriage service is a declared carriage service for the purposes of\nthis Part.\n\n(2) The declaration has effect accordingly.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to make a declaration under this section, the\nACCC must have regard to whether the declaration will promote\nthe long-term interests of end-users of:\n\n(a) carriage services; or\n\n(b) services supplied by means of carriage services.\n\n(4) The ACCC may have regard to any other matters that it thinks are\nrelevant.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a particular\nthing promotes the long-term interests of end-users of:\n\n(a) carriage services; or\n\n(b) services supplied by means of carriage services;\nis to be determined in the same manner in which that question is\ndetermined for the purposes of Part XIC of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010.\nNote:\nSee section 152AB of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACCC may, by written instrument, declare that a specified\ncarriage service is a declared carriage service for the purposes of\nthis Part.\n\n(2) The declaration has effect accordingly.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to make a declaration under this section, the\nACCC must have regard to whether the declaration will promote\nthe long-term interests of end-users of:\n\n(a) carriage services; or\n\n(b) services supplied by means of carriage services.\n\n(4) The ACCC may have regard to any other matters that it thinks are\nrelevant.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a particular\nthing promotes the long-term interests of end-users of:\n\n(a) carriage services; or\n\n(b) services supplied by means of carriage services;\nis to be determined in the same manner in which that question is\ndetermined for the purposes of Part XIC of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010.\nNote:\nSee section 152AB of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-350a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-350a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-350a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-350a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-350a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf484bff7d50f724b5155c1b0d26d0481449fa4428afad21a4bceaa9e8eaa78e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-350a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "350A Declared carriage services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may, by written instrument, declare that a specified\ncarriage service is a declared carriage service for the purposes of\nthis Part.\n\n(2) The declaration has effect accordingly.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to make a declaration under this section, the\nACCC must have regard to whether the declaration will promote\nthe long-term interests of end-users of:\n\n(a) carriage services; or\n\n(b) services supplied by means of carriage services.\n\n(4) The ACCC may have regard to any other matters that it thinks are\nrelevant.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a particular\nthing promotes the long-term interests of end-users of:\n\n(a) carriage services; or\n\n(b) services supplied by means of carriage services;\nis to be determined in the same manner in which that question is\ndetermined for the purposes of Part XIC of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010.\nNote:\nSee section 152AB of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010."
    },
