    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "351 Pre-selection to be provided",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-351"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person if a determination under\nsection 349 is in force and that determination requires the person to\nprovide pre-selection.\n\n(2) A person must provide pre-selection in accordance with the\nrequirements set out in the determination and on such terms and\nconditions as are:\n\n(a) agreed between the following parties:\n\n(i) the person;\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 352\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the carriage service provider in whose favour\npre-selection is required to be provided; or\n\n(b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by\nthe parties.\nIf the parties fail to agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the\nACCC is to be the arbitrator.\n\n(3) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to the\nconduct of an arbitration under this section.\n\n(4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular\narbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC\nmay be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of\nmembers, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or\nthose members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson\nof the ACCC.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection (3).\n\n(6) A person must comply with any rules set out in the determination\nas mentioned in paragraph 349(1)(b) or (2)(b).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a person if a determination under\nsection 349 is in force and that determination requires the person to\nprovide pre-selection.\n\n(2) A person must provide pre-selection in accordance with the\nrequirements set out in the determination and on such terms and\nconditions as are:\n\n(a) agreed between the following parties:\n\n(i) the person;\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 352\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the carriage service provider in whose favour\npre-selection is required to be provided; or\n\n(b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by\nthe parties.\nIf the parties fail to agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the\nACCC is to be the arbitrator.\n\n(3) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to the\nconduct of an arbitration under this section.\n\n(4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular\narbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC\nmay be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of\nmembers, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or\nthose members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson\nof the ACCC.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection (3).\n\n(6) A person must comply with any rules set out in the determination\nas mentioned in paragraph 349(1)(b) or (2)(b).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "72b4ff441b0a5da263bf89c330356d353f0425d82f837b263d27e20eb1f2015b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-351",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "351 Pre-selection to be provided",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 176,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person if a determination under\nsection 349 is in force and that determination requires the person to\nprovide pre-selection.\n\n(2) A person must provide pre-selection in accordance with the\nrequirements set out in the determination and on such terms and\nconditions as are:\n\n(a) agreed between the following parties:\n\n(i) the person;\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 352\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the carriage service provider in whose favour\npre-selection is required to be provided; or\n\n(b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by\nthe parties.\nIf the parties fail to agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the\nACCC is to be the arbitrator.\n\n(3) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to the\nconduct of an arbitration under this section.\n\n(4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular\narbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC\nmay be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of\nmembers, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or\nthose members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson\nof the ACCC.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection (3).\n\n(6) A person must comply with any rules set out in the determination\nas mentioned in paragraph 349(1)(b) or (2)(b)."
    },
