    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-352",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "352 Exemptions from requirement to provide pre-selection",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-352"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.177",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, declare that a specified carrier or\ncarriage service provider is exempt from a requirement imposed\nunder section 349. The declaration has effect accordingly.\nNote:\nCarriers or providers may be specified by name, by inclusion in a\nparticular class or in any other way.\n\n(2) In deciding whether a carrier or carriage service provider should be\nexempt from a requirement imposed under section 349, the ACMA\nmust have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) whether it would be technically feasible for the carrier or\nprovider to comply with the requirement concerned;\n\n(b) whether compliance with the requirement concerned would\nimpose unreasonable financial hardship on the carrier or\nprovider.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, declare that a specified carrier or\ncarriage service provider is exempt from a requirement imposed\nunder section 349. The declaration has effect accordingly.\nNote:\nCarriers or providers may be specified by name, by inclusion in a\nparticular class or in any other way.\n\n(2) In deciding whether a carrier or carriage service provider should be\nexempt from a requirement imposed under section 349, the ACMA\nmust have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) whether it would be technically feasible for the carrier or\nprovider to comply with the requirement concerned;\n\n(b) whether compliance with the requirement concerned would\nimpose unreasonable financial hardship on the carrier or\nprovider.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-352-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-352-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7bc4b000efa8c5563f3398f233e00afb7711ace7fae857df134c84f5236df455"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-352",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "352 Exemptions from requirement to provide pre-selection",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 177,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, declare that a specified carrier or\ncarriage service provider is exempt from a requirement imposed\nunder section 349. The declaration has effect accordingly.\nNote:\nCarriers or providers may be specified by name, by inclusion in a\nparticular class or in any other way.\n\n(2) In deciding whether a carrier or carriage service provider should be\nexempt from a requirement imposed under section 349, the ACMA\nmust have regard to the following matters:\n\n(a) whether it would be technically feasible for the carrier or\nprovider to comply with the requirement concerned;\n\n(b) whether compliance with the requirement concerned would\nimpose unreasonable financial hardship on the carrier or\nprovider."
    },
