    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "353 Use of over-ride dial codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-353"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a carriage service provider (the first\nprovider) if:\n\n(a) the first provider supplies a carriage service that involves the\nuse of a controlled network, or a controlled facility, of a\ncarrier, of the first provider or of another carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) in accordance with a determination under section 349, the\nnetwork or facility, as the case may be, provides over-ride\ndial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers\non a call-by-call basis.\n\n(2) Unless, in the ACMA’s opinion:\n\n(a) it would not be technically feasible; or\n\n(b) it would impose unreasonable financial hardship on the first\nprovider;\nthe first provider must take such steps as are necessary to ensure\nthat each end-user of the carriage service is able to make use of\nthose codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers on a\ncall-by-call basis.\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 353\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) The requirement in subsection (2) does not, by implication, prevent\nan alternative carriage service provider from refusing to supply a\ncarriage service to the end-user concerned.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a carriage service provider (the first\nprovider) if:\n\n(a) the first provider supplies a carriage service that involves the\nuse of a controlled network, or a controlled facility, of a\ncarrier, of the first provider or of another carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) in accordance with a determination under section 349, the\nnetwork or facility, as the case may be, provides over-ride\ndial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers\non a call-by-call basis.\n\n(2) Unless, in the ACMA’s opinion:\n\n(a) it would not be technically feasible; or\n\n(b) it would impose unreasonable financial hardship on the first\nprovider;\nthe first provider must take such steps as are necessary to ensure\nthat each end-user of the carriage service is able to make use of\nthose codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers on a\ncall-by-call basis.\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 353\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) The requirement in subsection (2) does not, by implication, prevent\nan alternative carriage service provider from refusing to supply a\ncarriage service to the end-user concerned.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51b7865032aad5883ccb6a0762f48fabff763c786425c252cf475fb4d849534c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-353",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "353 Use of over-ride dial codes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a carriage service provider (the first\nprovider) if:\n\n(a) the first provider supplies a carriage service that involves the\nuse of a controlled network, or a controlled facility, of a\ncarrier, of the first provider or of another carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) in accordance with a determination under section 349, the\nnetwork or facility, as the case may be, provides over-ride\ndial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers\non a call-by-call basis.\n\n(2) Unless, in the ACMA’s opinion:\n\n(a) it would not be technically feasible; or\n\n(b) it would impose unreasonable financial hardship on the first\nprovider;\nthe first provider must take such steps as are necessary to ensure\nthat each end-user of the carriage service is able to make use of\nthose codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers on a\ncall-by-call basis.\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 353\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) The requirement in subsection (2) does not, by implication, prevent\nan alternative carriage service provider from refusing to supply a\ncarriage service to the end-user concerned."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "353(1) Use of over-ride dial codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-353-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a carriage service provider (the first\nprovider) if:\n\n(a) the first provider supplies a carriage service that involves the\nuse of a controlled network, or a controlled facility, of a\ncarrier, of the first provider or of another carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) in accordance with a determination under section 349, the\nnetwork or facility, as the case may be, provides over-ride\ndial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers\non a call-by-call basis.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a carriage service provider (the first\nprovider) if:\n\n(a) the first provider supplies a carriage service that involves the\nuse of a controlled network, or a controlled facility, of a\ncarrier, of the first provider or of another carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) in accordance with a determination under section 349, the\nnetwork or facility, as the case may be, provides over-ride\ndial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers\non a call-by-call basis.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c50d9dbcaa112019da23843d68d24a59ac0c7edf5b5df470c82728833087ff51",
      "skos:note": "Carriage service provider must supply over-ride dial codes",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-353-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "353(1) Use of over-ride dial codes",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a carriage service provider (the first\nprovider) if:\n\n(a) the first provider supplies a carriage service that involves the\nuse of a controlled network, or a controlled facility, of a\ncarrier, of the first provider or of another carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) in accordance with a determination under section 349, the\nnetwork or facility, as the case may be, provides over-ride\ndial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers\non a call-by-call basis."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
