      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide over-ride dial codes",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "353(2) Use of over-ride dial codes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-353-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Unless, in the ACMA’s opinion:\n\n(a) it would not be technically feasible; or\n\n(b) it would impose unreasonable financial hardship on the first\nprovider;\nthe first provider must take such steps as are necessary to ensure\nthat each end-user of the carriage service is able to make use of\nthose codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers on a\ncall-by-call basis.\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 353\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Unless, in the ACMA’s opinion:\n\n(a) it would not be technically feasible; or\n\n(b) it would impose unreasonable financial hardship on the first\nprovider;\nthe first provider must take such steps as are necessary to ensure\nthat each end-user of the carriage service is able to make use of\nthose codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers on a\ncall-by-call basis.\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 353\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-353-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2f5188f4313a502e2b4809c31ef223d166e09361559cfb362f8f49cf1f7a27b7",
      "skos:note": "First provider must ensure end-users can use over-ride dial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-353-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "353(2) Use of over-ride dial codes",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Unless, in the ACMA’s opinion:\n\n(a) it would not be technically feasible; or\n\n(b) it would impose unreasonable financial hardship on the first\nprovider;\nthe first provider must take such steps as are necessary to ensure\nthat each end-user of the carriage service is able to make use of\nthose codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers on a\ncall-by-call basis.\n\n\nPre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17\n\nSection 353\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
