    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "356 Exemptions from calling line identification requirement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-356"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.180",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, declare that a specified\nperson is exempt from the requirement set out in section 355. The\ndeclaration has effect accordingly.\n\n\nCalling line identification  Part 18\n\nSection 356\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nA person may be identified by name, by inclusion in a particular class\nor in any other way.\n\n(2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the\nrequirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to\nthe following matters:\n\n(a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;\n\n(b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nthe ACMA may have regard.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, declare that a specified\nperson is exempt from the requirement set out in section 355. The\ndeclaration has effect accordingly.\n\n\nCalling line identification  Part 18\n\nSection 356\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nA person may be identified by name, by inclusion in a particular class\nor in any other way.\n\n(2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the\nrequirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to\nthe following matters:\n\n(a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;\n\n(b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nthe ACMA may have regard.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de05ac22a4e30dc8bef1cda5bb3db1daf427cad17a77e2680c2aad2afda96148"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-356",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "356 Exemptions from calling line identification requirement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 180,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, declare that a specified\nperson is exempt from the requirement set out in section 355. The\ndeclaration has effect accordingly.\n\n\nCalling line identification  Part 18\n\nSection 356\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nA person may be identified by name, by inclusion in a particular class\nor in any other way.\n\n(2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the\nrequirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to\nthe following matters:\n\n(a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;\n\n(b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nthe ACMA may have regard."
    },
