    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360AB Associate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.186",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a person (the first\nperson) in relation to control of:\n\n(a) a facility; or\n\n(b) a company;\nis:\n\n(c) a partner of the first person; or\n\n(d) if the first person or another person who is an associate of the\nfirst person under another paragraph receives benefits or is\ncapable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust;\nor\n\n(e) a person (whether a company or not) who:\n\n(i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 360AC\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding\n(whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to\nact;\n\nin accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of,\nor in concert with:\n\n(iii) the first person; or\n\n(iv) the first person and another person who is an associate\nof the first person under another paragraph; or\n\n(f) another company if:\n\n(i) the other company is a related body corporate of the\nfirst person for the purposes of the Corporations Act\n2001; or\n\n(ii) the first person, or the first person and another person\nwho is an associate of the first person under another\nparagraph, is or are in a position to exercise control of\nthe other company.\n\n(2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACMA is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to\nthe facility or company; and\n\n(b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the\nbusiness dealings of the other in relation to the facility or\ncompany.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a person (the first\nperson) in relation to control of:\n\n(a) a facility; or\n\n(b) a company;\nis:\n\n(c) a partner of the first person; or\n\n(d) if the first person or another person who is an associate of the\nfirst person under another paragraph receives benefits or is\ncapable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust;\nor\n\n(e) a person (whether a company or not) who:\n\n(i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 360AC\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding\n(whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to\nact;\n\nin accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of,\nor in concert with:\n\n(iii) the first person; or\n\n(iv) the first person and another person who is an associate\nof the first person under another paragraph; or\n\n(f) another company if:\n\n(i) the other company is a related body corporate of the\nfirst person for the purposes of the Corporations Act\n2001; or\n\n(ii) the first person, or the first person and another person\nwho is an associate of the first person under another\nparagraph, is or are in a position to exercise control of\nthe other company.\n\n(2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACMA is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to\nthe facility or company; and\n\n(b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the\nbusiness dealings of the other in relation to the facility or\ncompany.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ab-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ab-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb2ac96733e4cede38088251fc2b811184dacb31f0c3ca4a42b8925f8e9d4f8f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360AB Associate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 186,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a person (the first\nperson) in relation to control of:\n\n(a) a facility; or\n\n(b) a company;\nis:\n\n(c) a partner of the first person; or\n\n(d) if the first person or another person who is an associate of the\nfirst person under another paragraph receives benefits or is\ncapable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust;\nor\n\n(e) a person (whether a company or not) who:\n\n(i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nIntroduction  Division 1\n\nSection 360AC\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding\n(whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to\nact;\n\nin accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of,\nor in concert with:\n\n(iii) the first person; or\n\n(iv) the first person and another person who is an associate\nof the first person under another paragraph; or\n\n(f) another company if:\n\n(i) the other company is a related body corporate of the\nfirst person for the purposes of the Corporations Act\n2001; or\n\n(ii) the first person, or the first person and another person\nwho is an associate of the first person under another\nparagraph, is or are in a position to exercise control of\nthe other company.\n\n(2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACMA is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to\nthe facility or company; and\n\n(b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the\nbusiness dealings of the other in relation to the facility or\ncompany."
    },
