      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360B Simplified outline of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThere are 4 types of service area, as follows:\n\n(a)\nthe general service area;\n\n(b)\na nominated service area;\n\n(c)\nan anticipated service area;\n\n(d)\na designated service area.\n•\nNBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider for the general\nservice area.\n•\nA nominated service area is an area that is attributable to:\n\n(a)\na declaration made by a carrier or carriage service\nprovider; or\n\n(b)\ncertain carrier licence conditions declarations made by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a declaration made by a carrier or\ncarriage service provider will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier to whom the carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration applies; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360C\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n•\nAn anticipated service area is an area that is attributable to a\nnotice given by a carrier or carriage service provider.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for an anticipated service\narea that is attributable to a notice given by a carrier or\ncarriage service provider will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nA designated service area is an area declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a designated service\narea will be a carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nNominated service areas, anticipated service areas and\ndesignated service areas are excluded from the general service\narea.\n•\nDesignated service areas are excluded from nominated service\nareas.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThere are 4 types of service area, as follows:\n\n(a)\nthe general service area;\n\n(b)\na nominated service area;\n\n(c)\nan anticipated service area;\n\n(d)\na designated service area.\n•\nNBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider for the general\nservice area.\n•\nA nominated service area is an area that is attributable to:\n\n(a)\na declaration made by a carrier or carriage service\nprovider; or\n\n(b)\ncertain carrier licence conditions declarations made by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a declaration made by a carrier or\ncarriage service provider will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier to whom the carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration applies; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360C\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n•\nAn anticipated service area is an area that is attributable to a\nnotice given by a carrier or carriage service provider.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for an anticipated service\narea that is attributable to a notice given by a carrier or\ncarriage service provider will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nA designated service area is an area declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a designated service\narea will be a carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nNominated service areas, anticipated service areas and\ndesignated service areas are excluded from the general service\narea.\n•\nDesignated service areas are excluded from n",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360b-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ffc6b9876bdf90bdf582307e727ec9fa90e2f1c93046dc620014a64140eca8a",
      "skos:note": "Definitions of service areas and statutory infrastructure providers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360B Simplified outline of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThere are 4 types of service area, as follows:\n\n(a)\nthe general service area;\n\n(b)\na nominated service area;\n\n(c)\nan anticipated service area;\n\n(d)\na designated service area.\n•\nNBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider for the general\nservice area.\n•\nA nominated service area is an area that is attributable to:\n\n(a)\na declaration made by a carrier or carriage service\nprovider; or\n\n(b)\ncertain carrier licence conditions declarations made by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a declaration made by a carrier or\ncarriage service provider will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier to whom the carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration applies; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360C\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n•\nAn anticipated service area is an area that is attributable to a\nnotice given by a carrier or carriage service provider.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for an anticipated service\narea that is attributable to a notice given by a carrier or\ncarriage service provider will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier or carriage service provider; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nA designated service area is an area declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a designated service\narea will be a carrier or carriage service provider declared by\nthe Minister.\n•\nNominated service areas, anticipated service areas and\ndesignated service areas are excluded from the general service\narea.\n•\nDesignated service areas are excluded from nominated service\nareas."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
