    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360G Statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.192",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Part, NBN Co is the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the general service area.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Part, NBN Co is the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the general service area.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360g-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3e8f37a4d28800b25ee56d8ec3233c030fa8618f675a8f4d67b53a15357d2c61",
      "skos:note": "NBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360G Statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 192,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Part, NBN Co is the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the general service area."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360g-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360g"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360H Nominated service area—declaration made by a carrier",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.192",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, if a provisional nominated service\narea is attributable to a declaration under this section, so much of\nthe provisional nominated service area as is not:\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360H\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the whole or a part of a provisional nominated service area\nthat is attributable to a subsequent declaration under this\nsection or section 360HB; or\n\n(b) the whole or a part of a designated service area;\nis a nominated service area.\nProvisional nominated service area—real estate development\nproject\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) installs telecommunications network\ninfrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services\nto premises in the whole or a part of the project area of a real\nestate development project; and\n\n(aa) the carrier is not already the statutory infrastructure provider\nfor a service area that consists of, or includes, the project\narea; and\n\n(b) the installation was carried out under a contract with the\nperson responsible for the real estate development project;\nand\n\n(ba) the infrastructure is not backhaul infrastructure; and\n\n(c) the conditions specified in an instrument under subsection (3)\nare satisfied;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) by written instrument, declare that the whole or the part, as\nthe case requires, of the project area is a provisional\nnominated service area for the purposes of this Part; and\n\n(e) do so within 10 business days after completing the\ninstallation of that infrastructure.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(c).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, if a provisional nominated service\narea is attributable to a declaration under this section, so much of\nthe provisional nominated service area as is not:\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360H\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the whole or a part of a provisional nominated service area\nthat is attributable to a subsequent declaration under this\nsection or section 360HB; or\n\n(b) the whole or a part of a designated service area;\nis a nominated service area.\nProvisional nominated service area—real estate development\nproject\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) installs telecommunications network\ninfrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services\nto premises in the whole or a part of the project area of a real\nestate development project; and\n\n(aa) the carrier is not already the statutory infrastructure provider\nfor a service area that consists of, or includes, the project\narea; and\n\n(b) the installation was carried out under a contract with the\nperson responsible for the real estate development project;\nand\n\n(ba) the infrastructure is not backhaul infrastructure; and\n\n(c) the conditions specified in an instrument under subsection (3)\nare satisfied;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) by written instrument, declare that the whole or the part, as\nthe case requires, of the project area is a provisional\nnominated service area for the purposes of this Part; and\n\n(e) do so within 10 business days after completing the\ninstallation of that infrastructure.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(c).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9c469cd3fb1f289833d00eb9caa2116ca23e0168d1a4be313949e1fa0d727470"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360H Nominated service area—declaration made by a carrier",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 192,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, if a provisional nominated service\narea is attributable to a declaration under this section, so much of\nthe provisional nominated service area as is not:\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360H\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the whole or a part of a provisional nominated service area\nthat is attributable to a subsequent declaration under this\nsection or section 360HB; or\n\n(b) the whole or a part of a designated service area;\nis a nominated service area.\nProvisional nominated service area—real estate development\nproject\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) installs telecommunications network\ninfrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services\nto premises in the whole or a part of the project area of a real\nestate development project; and\n\n(aa) the carrier is not already the statutory infrastructure provider\nfor a service area that consists of, or includes, the project\narea; and\n\n(b) the installation was carried out under a contract with the\nperson responsible for the real estate development project;\nand\n\n(ba) the infrastructure is not backhaul infrastructure; and\n\n(c) the conditions specified in an instrument under subsection (3)\nare satisfied;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) by written instrument, declare that the whole or the part, as\nthe case requires, of the project area is a provisional\nnominated service area for the purposes of this Part; and\n\n(e) do so within 10 business days after completing the\ninstallation of that infrastructure.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(c).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360h-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360H(1) Nominated service area—declaration made by a carrier",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360h-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
