    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360HA Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360ha"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "the ACMA by a carrier\nNominated service area—real estate development project\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation\nof telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable\nthe supply of eligible services to premises in the whole or a\npart of the project area of a real estate development project;\nand\n\n(b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(c) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ia) sets out the date on which the contract was entered into;\nand\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360HA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(d) do so within 20 business days after entering into the contract.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other\nthan an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the\ninstallation of telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in\nthe whole or a part of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was not completed before the commencement\nof this section; and\n\n(c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(e) do so:\n\n(i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section;\nor\n\n(ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer\nperiod.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.",
      "skos:definition": "the ACMA by a carrier\nNominated service area—real estate development project\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation\nof telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable\nthe supply of eligible services to premises in the whole or a\npart of the project area of a real estate development project;\nand\n\n(b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(c) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ia) sets out the date on which the contract was entered into;\nand\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360HA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(d) do so within 20 business days after entering into the contract.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other\nthan an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the\ninstallation of telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in\nthe whole or a part of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was not completed before the commencement\nof this section; and\n\n(c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a30af39301583857043816c9bb7b61bc491cc85fbf1ba2a773547b00ed3a962e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360ha",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360HA Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "the ACMA by a carrier\nNominated service area—real estate development project\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation\nof telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable\nthe supply of eligible services to premises in the whole or a\npart of the project area of a real estate development project;\nand\n\n(b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(c) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ia) sets out the date on which the contract was entered into;\nand\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nService areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2\n\nSection 360HA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(d) do so within 20 business days after entering into the contract.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other\nthan an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the\ninstallation of telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in\nthe whole or a part of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was not completed before the commencement\nof this section; and\n\n(c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(e) do so:\n\n(i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section;\nor\n\n(ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer\nperiod.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA."
    },
    {
