    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360HA(2) Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360ha-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other\nthan an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the\ninstallation of telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in\nthe whole or a part of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was not completed before the commencement\nof this section; and\n\n(c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(e) do so:\n\n(i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section;\nor\n\n(ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer\nperiod.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n\n(a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other\nthan an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the\ninstallation of telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in\nthe whole or a part of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was not completed before the commencement\nof this section; and\n\n(c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(e) do so:\n\n(i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section;\nor\n\n(ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer\nperiod.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d91055f79b1ef0a842f9b1f925d80454b58c384d6a632ee67ad67d41b39869b",
      "skos:note": "Carrier must give ACMA written notice within 90 days after commencement.",
      "dc:description": "written notice stating contract details and estimated completion date"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360ha-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360HA(2) Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other\nthan an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the\ninstallation of telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in\nthe whole or a part of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was not completed before the commencement\nof this section; and\n\n(c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be\nrequired, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or\nthe part, as the case requires, of the project area is a\nprovisional nominated service area for the purposes of this\nPart;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) give the ACMA a written notice that:\n\n(i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and\n\n(ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of\nthe project area; and\n\n(iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure\nthat is to be installed under the contract; and\n\n(iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion\ndate for the installation; and\n\n(e) do so:\n\n(i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section;\nor\n\n(ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer\nperiod.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-2-norm",
