    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360na",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360NA Proximity to a project area",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360na"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.223",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, telecommunications network\ninfrastructure forming part of a mobile network is in proximity to a\nproject area if, and only if, once fully deployed and operational, the\ninfrastructure is technically capable of being used to supply\ncarriage services within the whole of the project area.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, telecommunications network\ninfrastructure forming part of a mobile network is in proximity to a\nproject area if, and only if, once fully deployed and operational, the\ninfrastructure is technically capable of being used to supply\ncarriage services within the whole of the project area.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360na-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360na-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5921554b283d099954fe4d6ed9e3b6ce803b9853cd15314dfda729d8f2d9601",
      "skos:note": "Telecommunications network infrastructure must be technically capable of supplying carriage services within the project area."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360na",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360NA Proximity to a project area",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 223,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, telecommunications network\ninfrastructure forming part of a mobile network is in proximity to a\nproject area if, and only if, once fully deployed and operational, the\ninfrastructure is technically capable of being used to supply\ncarriage services within the whole of the project area."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360na-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360na"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360na-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The provision imposes a duty on the state.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360P Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to connect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.224",
      "values:originalText": "premises\n\n(1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on\nreasonable request by a carriage service provider on behalf of an\nend-user at premises in the service area:\n\n(a) connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line\ntelecommunications network in order that the carriage service\nprovider can provide qualifying fixed-line carriage services\nto the end-user at the premises; or\n\n(b) if it is not reasonable for the statutory infrastructure provider\nto connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line\ntelecommunications network—connect the premises to a\nqualifying telecommunications network in order that the\ncarriage service provider can provide:\n\n(i) qualifying fixed wireless carriage services to the\nend-user at the premises; or\n\n(ii) qualifying satellite carriage services to the end-user at\nthe premises.\nExceptions\n\n(2) An obligation does not arise under subsection (1) in relation to the\nconnection of premises in the circumstances (if any) specified in a\ndetermination under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\ncircumstances for the purposes of subsection (2).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nObligations of statutory infrastructure provider  Division 3\n\nSection 360P\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n\n(3A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\nRequirements\n\n(4) In fulfilling its obligations under subsection (1), the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for a service area must comply with such\nrequirements (if any) as are determined under subsection (5).\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore requirements for the purposes of subsection (4).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(6) A requirement may be of general application or may be limited to\none or more service areas.\n\n(7) Subsection (6) does not, by implication, limit the application of\nsubsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nTerms and conditions\n\n(8) If:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1) in relation to the connection of premises in a\nservice area; and\n\n(b) as a result, the statutory infrastructure provider has an\nobligation under subsection (1) to connect the premises; and\n\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider has made available on its\nwebsite:\n\n(i) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and",
      "skos:definition": "premises\n\n(1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on\nreasonable request by a carriage service provider on behalf of an\nend-user at premises in the service area:\n\n(a) connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line\ntelecommunications network in order that the carriage service\nprovider can provide qualifying fixed-line carriage services\nto the end-user at the premises; or\n\n(b) if it is not reasonable for the statutory infrastructure provider\nto connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line\ntelecommunications network—connect the premises to a\nqualifying telecommunications network in order that the\ncarriage service provider can provide:\n\n(i) qualifying fixed wireless carriage services to the\nend-user at the premises; or\n\n(ii) qualifying satellite carriage services to the end-user at\nthe premises.\nExceptions\n\n(2) An obligation does not arise under subsection (1) in relation to the\nconnection of premises in the circumstances (if any) specified in a\ndetermination under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\ncircumstances for the purposes of subsection (2).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nObligations of statutory infrastructure provider  Division 3\n\nSection 360P\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n\n(3A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\nRequirements\n\n(4) In fulfilling its obligations under subsection (1), the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for a service area must comply with such\nrequirements (if any) as are determined under subsection (5).\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, d",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a4b52f4884cdd3a60b527cbbf7527a6082053b6dc9b7e8012d3912cec9f9bc6e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360P Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to connect",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 224,
      "values:originalText": "premises\n\n(1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on\nreasonable request by a carriage service provider on behalf of an\nend-user at premises in the service area:\n\n(a) connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line\ntelecommunications network in order that the carriage service\nprovider can provide qualifying fixed-line carriage services\nto the end-user at the premises; or\n\n(b) if it is not reasonable for the statutory infrastructure provider\nto connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line\ntelecommunications network—connect the premises to a\nqualifying telecommunications network in order that the\ncarriage service provider can provide:\n\n(i) qualifying fixed wireless carriage services to the\nend-user at the premises; or\n\n(ii) qualifying satellite carriage services to the end-user at\nthe premises.\nExceptions\n\n(2) An obligation does not arise under subsection (1) in relation to the\nconnection of premises in the circumstances (if any) specified in a\ndetermination under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine\ncircumstances for the purposes of subsection (2).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nObligations of statutory infrastructure provider  Division 3\n\nSection 360P\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n\n(3A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\nRequirements\n\n(4) In fulfilling its obligations under subsection (1), the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for a service area must comply with such\nrequirements (if any) as are determined under subsection (5).\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore requirements for the purposes of subsection (4).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(6) A requirement may be of general application or may be limited to\none or more service areas.\n\n(7) Subsection (6) does not, by implication, limit the application of\nsubsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\nTerms and conditions\n\n(8) If:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1) in relation to the connection of premises in a\nservice area; and\n\n(b) as a result, the statutory infrastructure provider has an\nobligation under subsection (1) to connect the premises; and\n\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider has made available on its\nwebsite:\n\n(i) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360p-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360P(1) Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to connect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360p-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
