      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360Q Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to supply",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.228",
      "values:originalText": "eligible services—premises\n\n(1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on\nreasonable request by a carriage service provider:\n\n(a) supply an eligible service to the carriage service provider in\norder that the carriage service provider can provide\nqualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the\nservice area; and\n\n(b) do so on the terms and conditions that were made available\non the statutory infrastructure provider’s website at the time\nwhen the request was made.\nNote:\nSee also section 360X.\n\n(1A) The eligible service must enable the carriage service provider to\nsupply, to end-users at premises in the service area, carriage\nservices that can be used by those end-users to make and receive\nvoice calls.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply if the carriage service is supplied\nusing a satellite.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nObligations of statutory infrastructure provider  Division 3\n\nSection 360Q\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(1C) To avoid doubt, the requirement in subsection (1A) is part of the\nobligation under subsection (1).\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nAdjustment\n\n(2A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the service area specified in the\ndetermination is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the service area.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2B) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nException\n\n(3) An obligation does not arise under subsection (1) in relation to\nsupply of an eligible service in the circumstances (if any) specified\nin a determination under subsection (4).",
      "skos:definition": "eligible services—premises\n\n(1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on\nreasonable request by a carriage service provider:\n\n(a) supply an eligible service to the carriage service provider in\norder that the carriage service provider can provide\nqualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the\nservice area; and\n\n(b) do so on the terms and conditions that were made available\non the statutory infrastructure provider’s website at the time\nwhen the request was made.\nNote:\nSee also section 360X.\n\n(1A) The eligible service must enable the carriage service provider to\nsupply, to end-users at premises in the service area, carriage\nservices that can be used by those end-users to make and receive\nvoice calls.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply if the carriage service is supplied\nusing a satellite.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nObligations of statutory infrastructure provider  Division 3\n\nSection 360Q\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(1C) To avoid doubt, the requirement in subsection (1A) is part of the\nobligation under subsection (1).\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nAdjustment\n\n(2A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the service area specified in the\ndetermination is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the service area.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation A",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-1c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-2b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360q-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9787a80d14de3beddd6d971b9d6a7968e7ac338e02b1349eca9e04baabb0c415"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360Q Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to supply",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 228,
      "values:originalText": "eligible services—premises\n\n(1) The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on\nreasonable request by a carriage service provider:\n\n(a) supply an eligible service to the carriage service provider in\norder that the carriage service provider can provide\nqualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the\nservice area; and\n\n(b) do so on the terms and conditions that were made available\non the statutory infrastructure provider’s website at the time\nwhen the request was made.\nNote:\nSee also section 360X.\n\n(1A) The eligible service must enable the carriage service provider to\nsupply, to end-users at premises in the service area, carriage\nservices that can be used by those end-users to make and receive\nvoice calls.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply if the carriage service is supplied\nusing a satellite.\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nObligations of statutory infrastructure provider  Division 3\n\nSection 360Q\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(1C) To avoid doubt, the requirement in subsection (1A) is part of the\nobligation under subsection (1).\nSpecial obligation of NBN Co\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, this section\nhas effect as if:\n\n(a) the area specified in the determination were a service area;\nand\n\n(b) NBN Co were the statutory infrastructure provider for that\narea.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nAdjustment\n\n(2A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for the service area specified in the\ndetermination is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the service area.\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\n\n(2B) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if the\nconditions specified in the determination are satisfied, the statutory\ninfrastructure provider is taken to have complied with the statutory\ninfrastructure provider’s obligations under subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nException\n\n(3) An obligation does not arise under subsection (1) in relation to\nsupply of an eligible service in the circumstances (if any) specified\nin a determination under subsection (4)."
    },
