    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360SA Notification obligations of carriage service provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360sa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.237",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider receives written notice from a\nperson under subsection 360R(2) or (3) of a matter relating to\na service area; and\n\n(b) the matter is likely to result in a change to, or the disruption\nof, qualifying carriage services provided by the carriage\nservice provider to end-users at premises in the service area.\nObligation\n\n(2) The carriage service provider must:\n\n(a) give written notice of the matter to each of those end-users;\nand\n\n(b) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice under\nsubsection 360R(2) or (3).",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider receives written notice from a\nperson under subsection 360R(2) or (3) of a matter relating to\na service area; and\n\n(b) the matter is likely to result in a change to, or the disruption\nof, qualifying carriage services provided by the carriage\nservice provider to end-users at premises in the service area.\nObligation\n\n(2) The carriage service provider must:\n\n(a) give written notice of the matter to each of those end-users;\nand\n\n(b) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice under\nsubsection 360R(2) or (3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360sa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360SA Notification obligations of carriage service provider",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 237,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider receives written notice from a\nperson under subsection 360R(2) or (3) of a matter relating to\na service area; and\n\n(b) the matter is likely to result in a change to, or the disruption\nof, qualifying carriage services provided by the carriage\nservice provider to end-users at premises in the service area.\nObligation\n\n(2) The carriage service provider must:\n\n(a) give written notice of the matter to each of those end-users;\nand\n\n(b) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice under\nsubsection 360R(2) or (3)."
    },
