    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360SB Rules may impose additional notification obligations on a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360sb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.237",
      "values:originalText": "carriage service provider\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules that:\n\n(a) apply to a carriage service provider that is subject to an\nobligation under subsection 360SA(2); and\n\n(b) impose one or more additional notification obligations on the\ncarriage service provider.\n\n(2) A notification obligation imposed by rules under subsection (1)\nmay involve the provision of information prescribed by the rules.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "carriage service provider\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules that:\n\n(a) apply to a carriage service provider that is subject to an\nobligation under subsection 360SA(2); and\n\n(b) impose one or more additional notification obligations on the\ncarriage service provider.\n\n(2) A notification obligation imposed by rules under subsection (1)\nmay involve the provision of information prescribed by the rules.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360sb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9be617b904740533b99bacead52321c24b2f89ee8e00e37cfb4c49e154664a8a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360sb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360SB Rules may impose additional notification obligations on a",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 237,
      "values:originalText": "carriage service provider\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules that:\n\n(a) apply to a carriage service provider that is subject to an\nobligation under subsection 360SA(2); and\n\n(b) impose one or more additional notification obligations on the\ncarriage service provider.\n\n(2) A notification obligation imposed by rules under subsection (1)\nmay involve the provision of information prescribed by the rules.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1)."
    },
