      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 248,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, at a particular time, a statutory infrastructure provider first has\nreason to believe that an event has occurred that is reasonably\nlikely to result in the statutory infrastructure provider being liable\nto pay damages to a particular customer under section 360VD, the\nstatutory infrastructure provider must:\n\n(a) decide whether to accept that liability; and\n\n(b) do so:\n\n(i) within 14 days after that time; or\n\n(ii) if another number of days is the relevant number of days\nfor the purposes of the application of this subsection to\nthe designated compensable rule or designated\ncompensable standard to which the liability relates—\nwithin the relevant number of days after that time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ve-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ve-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
