    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360X Offer to be made available—supply of eligible services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360x"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.252",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must make\navailable on its website:\n\n(a) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and\n\n(b) other terms and conditions;\non which it offers to supply eligible services to carriage service\nproviders in order that the carriage service providers can provide\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nOffers to be made available  Division 5\n\nSection 360X\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nqualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the service\narea.\n\n(2) The terms and conditions mentioned in subsection (1) must\ninclude:\n\n(a) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure\nprovider must begin to supply such an eligible service\nfollowing the making of a request by a carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure\nprovider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to\nsuch an eligible service following the making of a report by a\ncarriage service provider about the fault or service difficulty.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) An offer made available under subsection (1) has no effect to the\nextent to which it is inconsistent with:\n\n(a) a standard determined under section 360U; or\n\n(b) rules made under section 360V.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must make\navailable on its website:\n\n(a) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and\n\n(b) other terms and conditions;\non which it offers to supply eligible services to carriage service\nproviders in order that the carriage service providers can provide\n\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers  Part 19\nOffers to be made available  Division 5\n\nSection 360X\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nqualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the service\narea.\n\n(2) The terms and conditions mentioned in subsection (1) must\ninclude:\n\n(a) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure\nprovider must begin to supply such an eligible service\nfollowing the making of a request by a carriage service\nprovider; and\n\n(b) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure\nprovider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to\nsuch an eligible service following the making of a report by a\ncarriage service provider about the fault or service difficulty.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) An offer made available under subsection (1) has no effect to the\nextent to which it is inconsistent with:\n\n(a) a standard determined under section 360U; or\n\n(b) rules made under section 360V.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x-ss-2"
        },
