      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360za-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360ZA(5) Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360za-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.262",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the ACMA is subject to directions in relation to the exercise of a\npower delegated by the Minister to the ACMA under\nsubsection (1), then:\n\n(a) the ACMA must give corresponding written directions to the\nsecond delegate; and\n\n(b) the ACMA may give other written directions (not\ninconsistent with those corresponding directions) to the\nsecond delegate in relation to the exercise of that power.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the ACMA is subject to directions in relation to the exercise of a\npower delegated by the Minister to the ACMA under\nsubsection (1), then:\n\n(a) the ACMA must give corresponding written directions to the\nsecond delegate; and\n\n(b) the ACMA may give other written directions (not\ninconsistent with those corresponding directions) to the\nsecond delegate in relation to the exercise of that power.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360za"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360za-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360za-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56b5f04d3579c38ac20d4360db95118b4bdb84017ae0a9c4919c460fbd5013c6",
      "skos:note": "ACMA must give written directions to second delegate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-360za-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360ZA(5) Delegation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 262,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the ACMA is subject to directions in relation to the exercise of a\npower delegated by the Minister to the ACMA under\nsubsection (1), then:\n\n(a) the ACMA must give corresponding written directions to the\nsecond delegate; and\n\n(b) the ACMA may give other written directions (not\ninconsistent with those corresponding directions) to the\nsecond delegate in relation to the exercise of that power."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360za-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
