    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372A Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.273",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nIf a real estate development project is specified in a legislative\ninstrument made by the Minister, a person must not install a\nline in the project area unless the line is an optical fibre line.\n•\nA person must not install a fixed-line facility in the project\narea for a real estate development project unless the facility is\na fibre-ready facility.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project is a\nconstitutional corporation, the developer must not, in the\ncourse of carrying out the project, sell or lease a building lot\nor building unit unless a functional fibre-ready facility is\ninstalled in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project in a\nTerritory is not a constitutional corporation, the developer\nmust not, in the course of carrying out the project, sell or lease\na building lot or building unit unless a functional fibre-ready\nfacility is installed in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project in a State\nis not a constitutional corporation, the developer must not, in\nthe course of carrying out the project, sell or lease a building\nlot or building unit unless a functional fibre-ready facility is\ninstalled in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nThese rules are subject to any exemptions specified in a\nlegislative instrument made by the Minister.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nIf a real estate development project is specified in a legislative\ninstrument made by the Minister, a person must not install a\nline in the project area unless the line is an optical fibre line.\n•\nA person must not install a fixed-line facility in the project\narea for a real estate development project unless the facility is\na fibre-ready facility.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project is a\nconstitutional corporation, the developer must not, in the\ncourse of carrying out the project, sell or lease a building lot\nor building unit unless a functional fibre-ready facility is\ninstalled in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project in a\nTerritory is not a constitutional corporation, the developer\nmust not, in the course of carrying out the project, sell or lease\na building lot or building unit unless a functional fibre-ready\nfacility is installed in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project in a State\nis not a constitutional corporation, the developer must not, in\nthe course of carrying out the project, sell or lease a building\nlot or building unit unless a functional fibre-ready facility is\ninstalled in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nThese rules are subject to any exemptions specified in a\nlegislative instrument made by the Minister.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a8000eec535a6ace8bbb5b5867ed07dd83aa3193755588e66cbd62fca809906",
      "skos:note": "No installation of line or facility in project area without fibre-ready facility."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372A Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 273,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nIf a real estate development project is specified in a legislative\ninstrument made by the Minister, a person must not install a\nline in the project area unless the line is an optical fibre line.\n•\nA person must not install a fixed-line facility in the project\narea for a real estate development project unless the facility is\na fibre-ready facility.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project is a\nconstitutional corporation, the developer must not, in the\ncourse of carrying out the project, sell or lease a building lot\nor building unit unless a functional fibre-ready facility is\ninstalled in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project in a\nTerritory is not a constitutional corporation, the developer\nmust not, in the course of carrying out the project, sell or lease\na building lot or building unit unless a functional fibre-ready\nfacility is installed in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nIf the developer of a real estate development project in a State\nis not a constitutional corporation, the developer must not, in\nthe course of carrying out the project, sell or lease a building\nlot or building unit unless a functional fibre-ready facility is\ninstalled in proximity to the lot or unit.\n•\nThese rules are subject to any exemptions specified in a\nlegislative instrument made by the Minister."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372a-norm",
