    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372E Installation of fibre-ready facilities—building lots",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.280",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to the installation of a fixed-line facility in the\nproject area, or any of the project areas, for a real estate\ndevelopment project if:\n\n(a) the project involves the subdivision of one or more areas of\nland into building lots; and\n\n(b) the installation occurs after the commencement of this\nsection; and\n\n(c) sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be,\nsupplied to those lots.\nNote 1:\nFor fixed-line facility, see section 372V.\nNote 2:\nFor real estate development project, see section 372Q.\nNote 3:\nFor subdivision of an area of land, see section 372R.\nNote 4:\nFor building lot, see section 372Q.\nNote 5:\nFor supply of sewerage services, electricity or water, see\nsection 372Z.\nNote 6:\nFor exemptions, see section 372K.\nNote 7:\nFor exemption of certain projects, see section 372P.\nRequirement\n\n(2) A person must not install a fixed-line facility in the project area, or\nany of the project areas, for a real estate development project,\nunless:\n\n(a) the facility is a fibre-ready facility; and\n\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (4) are satisfied.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372F\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote 1:\nFor fibre-ready facility, see section 372W.\nNote 2:\nFor exemptions, see section 372K.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(b).\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(5) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (2); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (2).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(6) Subsections (2) and (5) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to the installation of a fixed-line facility in the\nproject area, or any of the project areas, for a real estate\ndevelopment project if:\n\n(a) the project involves the subdivision of one or more areas of\nland into building lots; and\n\n(b) the installation occurs after the commencement of this\nsection; and\n\n(c) sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be,\nsupplied to those lots.\nNote 1:\nFor fixed-line facility, see section 372V.\nNote 2:\nFor real estate development project, see section 372Q.\nNote 3:\nFor subdivision of an area of land, see section 372R.\nNote 4:\nFor building lot, see section 372Q.\nNote 5:\nFor supply of sewerage services, electricity or water, see\nsection 372Z.\nNote 6:\nFor exemptions, see section 372K.\nNote 7:\nFor exemption of certain projects, see section 372P.\nRequirement\n\n(2) A person must not install a fixed-line facility in the project area, or\nany of the project areas, for a real estate development project,\nunless:\n\n(a) the facility is a fibre-ready facility; and\n\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (4) are satisfied.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372F\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote 1:\nFor fibre-ready facility, see section 372W.\nNote 2:\nFor exemptions, see section 372K.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(b).\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(5) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (2); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (2).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(6) Subsections (2) and (5) are civil penalty provisions.\nNot",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372e-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372e-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372e-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372E Installation of fibre-ready facilities—building lots",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 280,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to the installation of a fixed-line facility in the\nproject area, or any of the project areas, for a real estate\ndevelopment project if:\n\n(a) the project involves the subdivision of one or more areas of\nland into building lots; and\n\n(b) the installation occurs after the commencement of this\nsection; and\n\n(c) sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be,\nsupplied to those lots.\nNote 1:\nFor fixed-line facility, see section 372V.\nNote 2:\nFor real estate development project, see section 372Q.\nNote 3:\nFor subdivision of an area of land, see section 372R.\nNote 4:\nFor building lot, see section 372Q.\nNote 5:\nFor supply of sewerage services, electricity or water, see\nsection 372Z.\nNote 6:\nFor exemptions, see section 372K.\nNote 7:\nFor exemption of certain projects, see section 372P.\nRequirement\n\n(2) A person must not install a fixed-line facility in the project area, or\nany of the project areas, for a real estate development project,\nunless:\n\n(a) the facility is a fibre-ready facility; and\n\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (4) are satisfied.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372F\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote 1:\nFor fibre-ready facility, see section 372W.\nNote 2:\nFor exemptions, see section 372K.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(b).\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(5) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (2); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (2).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(6) Subsections (2) and (5) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions."
    },
