      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372JA Remedial notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372ja"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.288",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a\nperson:\n\n(a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention will\ncontinue or be repeated; or\n\n(c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372JB\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRemedial notice\n\n(2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the\nperson to:\n\n(a) remedy the contravention; or\n\n(b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or\n\n(c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or\nlikely contravention.\n\n(3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a\nperson:\n\n(a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention will\ncontinue or be repeated; or\n\n(c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372JB\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRemedial notice\n\n(2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the\nperson to:\n\n(a) remedy the contravention; or\n\n(b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or\n\n(c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or\nlikely contravention.\n\n(3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372ja",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372JA Remedial notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 288,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a\nperson:\n\n(a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention will\ncontinue or be repeated; or\n\n(c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372JB\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRemedial notice\n\n(2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the\nperson to:\n\n(a) remedy the contravention; or\n\n(b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or\n\n(c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or\nlikely contravention.\n\n(3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice."
    },
