      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a\nperson:\n\n(a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n\n(b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention will\ncontinue or be repeated; or\n\n(c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372JB\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRemedial notice",
