      "skos:definition": "(1) A remedial notice given to a person by the ACMA must state:\n\n(a) that the ACMA reasonably believes that the person:\n\n(i) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or\n\n(ii) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in\ncircumstances that make it likely that the contravention\nwill continue or be repeated; or\n\n(iii) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty\nprovision; and\n\n(b) the provision the ACMA believes is being, has been, or is\nlikely to be, contravened; and\n\n(c) briefly, how the provision is being, has been, or is likely to\nbe, contravened; and\n\n(d) the period within which the person must comply with the\nnotice.\nNote:\nFor designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.",
