      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.291",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and\n\n(b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the\nACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer\nrequired for the purposes of requiring the person to:\n\n(i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty\nprovision; or\n\n(ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil\npenalty provision from occurring; or\n\n(iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention,\nor likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty\nprovision;\nthe ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nnotice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and\n\n(b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the\nACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer\nrequired for the purposes of requiring the person to:\n\n(i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty\nprovision; or\n\n(ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil\npenalty provision from occurring; or\n\n(iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention,\nor likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty\nprovision;\nthe ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nnotice.",
