      },
      "cml:operator": "exclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Excluding formal defects from invalidation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Formal defect or irregularity",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Substantial injustice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372jh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372JH Designated civil penalty provision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372jh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, each of the following\nprovisions is a designated civil penalty provision:\n\n(a) subsection 372E(2);\n\n(b) subsection 372F(2);\n\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n\n(e) subsection 372G(3);\n\n(f) subsection 372G(4);\n\n(g) subsection 372G(4A);\n\n(h) subsection 372G(5).\nSubdivision D—Exemptions",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, each of the following\nprovisions is a designated civil penalty provision:\n\n(a) subsection 372E(2);\n\n(b) subsection 372F(2);\n\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n\n(e) subsection 372G(3);\n\n(f) subsection 372G(4);\n\n(g) subsection 372G(4A);\n\n(h) subsection 372G(5).\nSubdivision D—Exemptions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372jh-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc0db0cc1069689034d7d1d1efd7681e2d5951af9f4909dc101298d5c362fa3d",
      "skos:note": "List of designated civil penalty provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372jh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372JH Designated civil penalty provision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Subdivision, each of the following\nprovisions is a designated civil penalty provision:\n\n(a) subsection 372E(2);\n\n(b) subsection 372F(2);\n\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n\n(e) subsection 372G(3);\n\n(f) subsection 372G(4);\n\n(g) subsection 372G(4A);\n\n(h) subsection 372G(5).\nSubdivision D—Exemptions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372jh-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372jh"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372K Exemptions—Ministerial instrument",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "Real estate development projects\n\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a real estate development project specified in the instrument;\nor\n\n(b) a real estate development project ascertained in accordance\nwith the instrument;\nfrom the scope of any or all of the following provisions:\n\n(c) section 372E;\n\n(d) section 372F;\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372K\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) section 372G;\n\n(f) section 372H.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(2) An exemption under subsection (1) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\nInstallations\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) conduct specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) conduct ascertained in accordance with the instrument;\nfrom the scope of either or both of the following provisions:\n\n(c) subsection 372E(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372F(2).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(4) An exemption under subsection (3) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\nBuilding lots\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a building lot specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) a building lot ascertained in accordance with the instrument;\nfrom the scope of any or all of the following provisions:\n\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n\n(e) subsection 372G(3).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.",
      "skos:definition": "Real estate development projects\n\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a real estate development project specified in the instrument;\nor\n\n(b) a real estate development project ascertained in accordance\nwith the instrument;\nfrom the scope of any or all of the following provisions:\n\n(c) section 372E;\n\n(d) section 372F;\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372K\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) section 372G;\n\n(f) section 372H.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(2) An exemption under subsection (1) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\nInstallations\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) conduct specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) conduct ascertained in accordance with the instrument;\nfrom the scope of either or both of the following provisions:\n\n(c) subsection 372E(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372F(2).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(4) An exemption under subsection (3) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\nBuilding lots\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a building lot specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) a building lot ascertained in accordance with the instrument;\nfrom the scope of any or all of the following provisions:\n\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n\n(e) subsection 372G(3).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372k-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372k-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372k-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "29afa075e3ce75563fc64282b7ef8ac51df16aef9fd0fe3af73e863478a51e16"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372K Exemptions—Ministerial instrument",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "Real estate development projects\n\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a real estate development project specified in the instrument;\nor\n\n(b) a real estate development project ascertained in accordance\nwith the instrument;\nfrom the scope of any or all of the following provisions:\n\n(c) section 372E;\n\n(d) section 372F;\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nInstallation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3\n\nSection 372K\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) section 372G;\n\n(f) section 372H.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(2) An exemption under subsection (1) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\nInstallations\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) conduct specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) conduct ascertained in accordance with the instrument;\nfrom the scope of either or both of the following provisions:\n\n(c) subsection 372E(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372F(2).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(4) An exemption under subsection (3) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\nBuilding lots\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a building lot specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) a building lot ascertained in accordance with the instrument;\nfrom the scope of any or all of the following provisions:\n\n(c) subsection 372G(2);\n\n(d) subsection 372G(2A);\n\n(e) subsection 372G(3).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003."
    },
