    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372l-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372L(4) Third party access regime",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372l-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.295",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The owner or operator of the facility is not required to comply with\nsubsection (2) in relation to the facility if there is in force a written\ncertificate issued by the ACCC stating that, in the ACCC’s\nopinion, compliance with subsection (2) in relation to the facility is\nnot technically feasible.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The owner or operator of the facility is not required to comply with\nsubsection (2) in relation to the facility if there is in force a written\ncertificate issued by the ACCC stating that, in the ACCC’s\nopinion, compliance with subsection (2) in relation to the facility is\nnot technically feasible.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372l-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372l-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b5ac6181c77abddc4d42eb33dd928fdd684664e679081b6a8792d5b49595c34",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from compliance with subsection (2) based on ACCC certificate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372l-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372L(4) Third party access regime",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 295,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The owner or operator of the facility is not required to comply with\nsubsection (2) in relation to the facility if there is in force a written\ncertificate issued by the ACCC stating that, in the ACCC’s\nopinion, compliance with subsection (2) in relation to the facility is\nnot technically feasible."
    },
