    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372N Exemptions—Ministerial instrument",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.298",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a fixed-line facility specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) a fixed-line facility ascertained in accordance with the\ninstrument;\nfrom the scope of section 372L.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(2) An exemption under subsection (1) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) may confer functions or\npowers on the ACCC.\n\n(4) The ACCC may, by writing, delegate any or all of the functions or\npowers conferred on it by an instrument under subsection (1) to a\nmember of the Commission (within the meaning of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a fixed-line facility specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) a fixed-line facility ascertained in accordance with the\ninstrument;\nfrom the scope of section 372L.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(2) An exemption under subsection (1) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) may confer functions or\npowers on the ACCC.\n\n(4) The ACCC may, by writing, delegate any or all of the functions or\npowers conferred on it by an instrument under subsection (1) to a\nmember of the Commission (within the meaning of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372n-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372n-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372n-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372n-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7540b901d1c85db21e70225d7c54ed73136be7ec028a65a050ce4a6073e9cefe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372N Exemptions—Ministerial instrument",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 298,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt:\n\n(a) a fixed-line facility specified in the instrument; or\n\n(b) a fixed-line facility ascertained in accordance with the\ninstrument;\nfrom the scope of section 372L.\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(2) An exemption under subsection (1) may be unconditional or\nsubject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\nexemption.\n\n(3) An instrument under subsection (1) may confer functions or\npowers on the ACCC.\n\n(4) The ACCC may, by writing, delegate any or all of the functions or\npowers conferred on it by an instrument under subsection (1) to a\nmember of the Commission (within the meaning of the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010)."
    },
