    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "372NA Code relating to access",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372na"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.298",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, make a Code setting out\nconditions that are to be complied with in relation to the provision\nof access under this Division.\n\n(2) The owner or operator of a fixed-line facility must comply with the\nCode.\n\n(3) This section does not, by implication, limit a power conferred by or\nunder this Act to make an instrument.\n\n(4) This section does not, by implication, limit the matters that may be\ndealt with by codes or standards referred to in Part 6.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not, by implication, limit\nsubsection 33(3B) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nThird party access regime  Division 4\n\nSection 372NA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(6) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (2); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (2).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(7) Subsections (2) and (6) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, make a Code setting out\nconditions that are to be complied with in relation to the provision\nof access under this Division.\n\n(2) The owner or operator of a fixed-line facility must comply with the\nCode.\n\n(3) This section does not, by implication, limit a power conferred by or\nunder this Act to make an instrument.\n\n(4) This section does not, by implication, limit the matters that may be\ndealt with by codes or standards referred to in Part 6.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not, by implication, limit\nsubsection 33(3B) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nThird party access regime  Division 4\n\nSection 372NA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(6) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (2); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (2).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(7) Subsections (2) and (6) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372na-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a302fdf40c160fa8e28d57d140c956006d973f7ca6132cbea7cd5893685f948"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-372na",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "372NA Code relating to access",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 298,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, make a Code setting out\nconditions that are to be complied with in relation to the provision\nof access under this Division.\n\n(2) The owner or operator of a fixed-line facility must comply with the\nCode.\n\n(3) This section does not, by implication, limit a power conferred by or\nunder this Act to make an instrument.\n\n(4) This section does not, by implication, limit the matters that may be\ndealt with by codes or standards referred to in Part 6.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not, by implication, limit\nsubsection 33(3B) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nDeployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A\nThird party access regime  Division 4\n\nSection 372NA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(6) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (2); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (2); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (2).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(7) Subsections (2) and (6) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions."
    },
