    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-379",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "379 Making technical standards in cases of urgency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-379"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.316",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA is not required to comply with subsection 378(1) in\nrelation to the making of a particular technical standard if the\nACMA is satisfied that it is necessary to make the standard as a\nmatter of urgency in order to:\n\n(a) protect the integrity of a telecommunications network or of a\nfacility; or\n\n(b) protect the health or safety of persons who:\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nTechnical standards about customer equipment and customer cabling  Division 3\n\nSection 379\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(2) If subsection (1) applies to a standard (the urgent standard), the\nurgent standard ceases to have effect 12 months after it came into\noperation. However, this rule does not prevent the ACMA from\nrevoking the urgent standard and making another standard under\nsection 376 that:\n\n(a) is not a standard to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) deals with the same subject matter as the urgent standard.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA is not required to comply with subsection 378(1) in\nrelation to the making of a particular technical standard if the\nACMA is satisfied that it is necessary to make the standard as a\nmatter of urgency in order to:\n\n(a) protect the integrity of a telecommunications network or of a\nfacility; or\n\n(b) protect the health or safety of persons who:\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nTechnical standards about customer equipment and customer cabling  Division 3\n\nSection 379\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(2) If subsection (1) applies to a standard (the urgent standard), the\nurgent standard ceases to have effect 12 months after it came into\noperation. However, this rule does not prevent the ACMA from\nrevoking the urgent standard and making another standard under\nsection 376 that:\n\n(a) is not a standard to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) deals with the same subject matter as the urgent standard.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-379-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-379-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7a7c432dff7edc5f3c203b4793417376dc7974497e9369252a538e27047a230"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-379",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "379 Making technical standards in cases of urgency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 316,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA is not required to comply with subsection 378(1) in\nrelation to the making of a particular technical standard if the\nACMA is satisfied that it is necessary to make the standard as a\nmatter of urgency in order to:\n\n(a) protect the integrity of a telecommunications network or of a\nfacility; or\n\n(b) protect the health or safety of persons who:\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nTechnical standards about customer equipment and customer cabling  Division 3\n\nSection 379\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(2) If subsection (1) applies to a standard (the urgent standard), the\nurgent standard ceases to have effect 12 months after it came into\noperation. However, this rule does not prevent the ACMA from\nrevoking the urgent standard and making another standard under\nsection 376 that:\n\n(a) is not a standard to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) deals with the same subject matter as the urgent standard."
    },
    {
