      },
      "cml:operator": "subclassOf",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Technical standards about customer equipment and customer cabling",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Division 3",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Section 379"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-379-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "379(2) Making technical standards in cases of urgency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-379-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.316",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If subsection (1) applies to a standard (the urgent standard), the\nurgent standard ceases to have effect 12 months after it came into\noperation. However, this rule does not prevent the ACMA from\nrevoking the urgent standard and making another standard under\nsection 376 that:\n\n(a) is not a standard to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) deals with the same subject matter as the urgent standard.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If subsection (1) applies to a standard (the urgent standard), the\nurgent standard ceases to have effect 12 months after it came into\noperation. However, this rule does not prevent the ACMA from\nrevoking the urgent standard and making another standard under\nsection 376 that:\n\n(a) is not a standard to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) deals with the same subject matter as the urgent standard.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-379"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-379-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cdfcc705819387818e209de0f09e023a51e0e25b7a0fdfb82aeaaa09457ff0cd",
      "skos:note": "Standard ceases to have effect after 12 months."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-379-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "379(2) Making technical standards in cases of urgency",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 316,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If subsection (1) applies to a standard (the urgent standard), the\nurgent standard ceases to have effect 12 months after it came into\noperation. However, this rule does not prevent the ACMA from\nrevoking the urgent standard and making another standard under\nsection 376 that:\n\n(a) is not a standard to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) deals with the same subject matter as the urgent standard."
    },
    {
