      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-380",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "380 Disability standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-380"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.318",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make a standard\nrelating to specified customer equipment if:\n\n(a) the customer equipment is for use in connection with the\nstandard telephone service; and\n\n(b) the customer equipment is for use primarily by persons who\ndo not have a disability; and\n\n(c) the standard relates to the features of the equipment that are\ndesigned to cater for any or all of the special needs of persons\nwith disabilities.\n\n(2) The following are examples of features mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(c):\n\n(a) an induction loop that is designed to assist in the operation of\na hearing aid;\n\n(b) a raised dot on the button labelled “5” on a telephone.\n\n(3) A standard under this section may be of general application or may\nbe limited as provided in the standard. This subsection does not, by\nimplication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(6) In this section:\ndisability has the same meaning as in the Disability Discrimination\nAct 1992.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make a standard\nrelating to specified customer equipment if:\n\n(a) the customer equipment is for use in connection with the\nstandard telephone service; and\n\n(b) the customer equipment is for use primarily by persons who\ndo not have a disability; and\n\n(c) the standard relates to the features of the equipment that are\ndesigned to cater for any or all of the special needs of persons\nwith disabilities.\n\n(2) The following are examples of features mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(c):\n\n(a) an induction loop that is designed to assist in the operation of\na hearing aid;\n\n(b) a raised dot on the button labelled “5” on a telephone.\n\n(3) A standard under this section may be of general application or may\nbe limited as provided in the standard. This subsection does not, by\nimplication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(6) In this section:\ndisability has the same meaning as in the Disability Discrimination\nAct 1992.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-380-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-380-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-380-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-380-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6132fd1219531f850c6adae5094e770ea4892d4e830a6ce9b9f73d8d5a0cc66f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-380",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "380 Disability standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 318,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make a standard\nrelating to specified customer equipment if:\n\n(a) the customer equipment is for use in connection with the\nstandard telephone service; and\n\n(b) the customer equipment is for use primarily by persons who\ndo not have a disability; and\n\n(c) the standard relates to the features of the equipment that are\ndesigned to cater for any or all of the special needs of persons\nwith disabilities.\n\n(2) The following are examples of features mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(c):\n\n(a) an induction loop that is designed to assist in the operation of\na hearing aid;\n\n(b) a raised dot on the button labelled “5” on a telephone.\n\n(3) A standard under this section may be of general application or may\nbe limited as provided in the standard. This subsection does not, by\nimplication, limit subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901.\n\n(6) In this section:\ndisability has the same meaning as in the Disability Discrimination\nAct 1992."
    },
