    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "382 Procedures for making disability standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-382"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.319",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making a standard under section 380, the ACMA must, so\nfar as is practicable, try to ensure that:\n\n(a) interested persons have had an adequate opportunity to make\nrepresentations about the proposed standard (either directly,\nor indirectly by means of a report under paragraph (2)(g));\nand\n\n(b) due consideration has been given to any representation so\nmade.\n\n(2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following\nbodies or associations:\n\n(a) Standards Australia;\n\n(b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards\nAustralia for the purposes of this subsection;\n\n(c) a body or association specified in a written determination\nmade by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection;\nunder which the body or association:\n\n(d) prepares a draft of a standard; and\n\n(e) publishes the draft standard; and\n\n(f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft\nstandard; and\n\n(g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public\nconsultation.\n\n(3) A copy of an approval under paragraph (2)(b) is to be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under paragraph (2)(c) is to be\npublished in the Gazette.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before making a standard under section 380, the ACMA must, so\nfar as is practicable, try to ensure that:\n\n(a) interested persons have had an adequate opportunity to make\nrepresentations about the proposed standard (either directly,\nor indirectly by means of a report under paragraph (2)(g));\nand\n\n(b) due consideration has been given to any representation so\nmade.\n\n(2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following\nbodies or associations:\n\n(a) Standards Australia;\n\n(b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards\nAustralia for the purposes of this subsection;\n\n(c) a body or association specified in a written determination\nmade by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection;\nunder which the body or association:\n\n(d) prepares a draft of a standard; and\n\n(e) publishes the draft standard; and\n\n(f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft\nstandard; and\n\n(g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public\nconsultation.\n\n(3) A copy of an approval under paragraph (2)(b) is to be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under paragraph (2)(c) is to be\npublished in the Gazette.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd42b1b0f2e326081594500b25ab70c18dcabc35ab28a0372a4d81595afcd6f1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-382",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "382 Procedures for making disability standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 319,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making a standard under section 380, the ACMA must, so\nfar as is practicable, try to ensure that:\n\n(a) interested persons have had an adequate opportunity to make\nrepresentations about the proposed standard (either directly,\nor indirectly by means of a report under paragraph (2)(g));\nand\n\n(b) due consideration has been given to any representation so\nmade.\n\n(2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following\nbodies or associations:\n\n(a) Standards Australia;\n\n(b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards\nAustralia for the purposes of this subsection;\n\n(c) a body or association specified in a written determination\nmade by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection;\nunder which the body or association:\n\n(d) prepares a draft of a standard; and\n\n(e) publishes the draft standard; and\n\n(f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft\nstandard; and\n\n(g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public\nconsultation.\n\n(3) A copy of an approval under paragraph (2)(b) is to be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\n(4) A copy of a determination under paragraph (2)(c) is to be\npublished in the Gazette."
    },
