      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following\nbodies or associations:\n\n(a) Standards Australia;\n\n(b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards\nAustralia for the purposes of this subsection;\n\n(c) a body or association specified in a written determination\nmade by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection;\nunder which the body or association:\n\n(d) prepares a draft of a standard; and\n\n(e) publishes the draft standard; and\n\n(f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft\nstandard; and\n\n(g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public\nconsultation.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following\nbodies or associations:\n\n(a) Standards Australia;\n\n(b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards\nAustralia for the purposes of this subsection;\n\n(c) a body or association specified in a written determination\nmade by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection;\nunder which the body or association:\n\n(d) prepares a draft of a standard; and\n\n(e) publishes the draft standard; and\n\n(f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft\nstandard; and\n\n(g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public\nconsultation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-382-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d52673ae34e10d33eebe7960a72d94cf061d1521fc861274b1e12283e701af8",
      "skos:note": "ACMA may make an arrangement with bodies or associations for preparing and publishing standards"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-382-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "382(2) Procedures for making disability standards",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 319,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following\nbodies or associations:\n\n(a) Standards Australia;\n\n(b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards\nAustralia for the purposes of this subsection;\n\n(c) a body or association specified in a written determination\nmade by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection;\nunder which the body or association:\n\n(d) prepares a draft of a standard; and\n\n(e) publishes the draft standard; and\n\n(f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft\nstandard; and\n\n(g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public\nconsultation."
    },
