    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-383",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "383 Effect of compliance with disability standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-383"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.320",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In determining whether a person has infringed section 24 of the\nDisability Discrimination Act 1992 in relation to the supply or\nprovision of customer equipment, regard must be had to whether\nthe customer equipment complies with a standard in force under\nsection 380.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nregard may be had.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nTechnical standards about the interconnection of facilities  Division 5\n\nSection 384\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In determining whether a person has infringed section 24 of the\nDisability Discrimination Act 1992 in relation to the supply or\nprovision of customer equipment, regard must be had to whether\nthe customer equipment complies with a standard in force under\nsection 380.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nregard may be had.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nTechnical standards about the interconnection of facilities  Division 5\n\nSection 384\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
