    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-384-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "384(5) ACMA’s power to make technical standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-384-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.321",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The ACCC must not give a direction under subsection (3) unless,\nin the ACCC’s opinion, it is necessary to do so in order to:\n\n(a) promote the long-term interests of end-users of carriage\nservices or of services supplied by means of carriage\nservices; or\n\n(b) reduce or eliminate the likelihood of hindrance to the\nprovision of access to declared services.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The ACCC must not give a direction under subsection (3) unless,\nin the ACCC’s opinion, it is necessary to do so in order to:\n\n(a) promote the long-term interests of end-users of carriage\nservices or of services supplied by means of carriage\nservices; or\n\n(b) reduce or eliminate the likelihood of hindrance to the\nprovision of access to declared services.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-384"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-384-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-384-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-384-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "470e10f5a7c5f06d56dbf9c4a50b402213b01ed1b28e6ad2a47622748459099e",
      "skos:note": "The ACCC must give a direction under subsection (3) if necessary to promote end-users' interests or reduce hindrance to access."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-384-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "384(5) ACMA’s power to make technical standards",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 321,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The ACCC must not give a direction under subsection (3) unless,\nin the ACCC’s opinion, it is necessary to do so in order to:\n\n(a) promote the long-term interests of end-users of carriage\nservices or of services supplied by means of carriage\nservices; or\n\n(b) reduce or eliminate the likelihood of hindrance to the\nprovision of access to declared services."
    },
