    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-390",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "390 Application for connection permit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-390"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.327",
      "values:originalText": "Customer equipment\n\n(1) A person (the applicant) may apply to the ACMA for a permit\nauthorising the applicant, and such other persons as are from time\nto time nominated by the applicant, to:\n\n(a) connect specified customer equipment to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility; and\n\n(b) maintain such a connection.\nThe permit is called a connection permit.\nCustomer cabling\n\n(2) A person (the applicant) may apply to the ACMA for a permit\nauthorising the applicant, and such other persons as are from time\nto time nominated by the applicant, to:\n\n(a) connect specified customer cabling to a telecommunications\nnetwork or to a facility; and\n\n(b) maintain such a connection.\nThe permit is called a connection permit.",
      "skos:definition": "Customer equipment\n\n(1) A person (the applicant) may apply to the ACMA for a permit\nauthorising the applicant, and such other persons as are from time\nto time nominated by the applicant, to:\n\n(a) connect specified customer equipment to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility; and\n\n(b) maintain such a connection.\nThe permit is called a connection permit.\nCustomer cabling\n\n(2) A person (the applicant) may apply to the ACMA for a permit\nauthorising the applicant, and such other persons as are from time\nto time nominated by the applicant, to:\n\n(a) connect specified customer cabling to a telecommunications\nnetwork or to a facility; and\n\n(b) maintain such a connection.\nThe permit is called a connection permit.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-390-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-390-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6d6dd7bcbb3a484e9dbb4b85cea467a73a579656b5591e39ef01a87bbc42a928"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-390",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "390 Application for connection permit",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 327,
      "values:originalText": "Customer equipment\n\n(1) A person (the applicant) may apply to the ACMA for a permit\nauthorising the applicant, and such other persons as are from time\nto time nominated by the applicant, to:\n\n(a) connect specified customer equipment to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility; and\n\n(b) maintain such a connection.\nThe permit is called a connection permit.\nCustomer cabling\n\n(2) A person (the applicant) may apply to the ACMA for a permit\nauthorising the applicant, and such other persons as are from time\nto time nominated by the applicant, to:\n\n(a) connect specified customer cabling to a telecommunications\nnetwork or to a facility; and\n\n(b) maintain such a connection.\nThe permit is called a connection permit."
    },
