    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-394",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "394 Issue of connection permits",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-394"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application, the ACMA may issue a\nconnection permit in accordance with the application.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to issue a connection permit, the ACMA may\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) whether the purpose for which the permit is sought is a\npurpose related to:\n\n(i) education or research; or\n\n(ii) the testing of customer equipment or customer cabling;\nor\n\n(iii) the demonstration of customer equipment or customer\ncabling; and\n\n(b) the knowledge and experience of the applicant.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to issue a connection permit, the ACMA must\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) the protection of the integrity of a telecommunications\nnetwork or of a facility; and\n\n(b) the protection of the health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nConnection permits and connection rules  Division 6\n\nSection 395\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not, by implication, limit the matters to\nwhich the ACMA may have regard.\n\n(5) If the ACMA decides to refuse to issue the connection permit, it\nmust give the applicant a written notice setting out the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After considering an application, the ACMA may issue a\nconnection permit in accordance with the application.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to issue a connection permit, the ACMA may\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) whether the purpose for which the permit is sought is a\npurpose related to:\n\n(i) education or research; or\n\n(ii) the testing of customer equipment or customer cabling;\nor\n\n(iii) the demonstration of customer equipment or customer\ncabling; and\n\n(b) the knowledge and experience of the applicant.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to issue a connection permit, the ACMA must\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) the protection of the integrity of a telecommunications\nnetwork or of a facility; and\n\n(b) the protection of the health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nConnection permits and connection rules  Division 6\n\nSection 395\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not, by implication, limit the matters to\nwhich the ACMA may have regard.\n\n(5) If the ACMA decides to refuse to issue the connection permit, it\nmust give the applicant a written notice setting out the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-394-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-394-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-394-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-394-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-394-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "413ab20b3eb4f2a242c50b5717abb9c70472c71b6472671ec180231b9a4a0319"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-394",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "394 Issue of connection permits",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application, the ACMA may issue a\nconnection permit in accordance with the application.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to issue a connection permit, the ACMA may\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) whether the purpose for which the permit is sought is a\npurpose related to:\n\n(i) education or research; or\n\n(ii) the testing of customer equipment or customer cabling;\nor\n\n(iii) the demonstration of customer equipment or customer\ncabling; and\n\n(b) the knowledge and experience of the applicant.\n\n(3) In deciding whether to issue a connection permit, the ACMA must\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) the protection of the integrity of a telecommunications\nnetwork or of a facility; and\n\n(b) the protection of the health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nConnection permits and connection rules  Division 6\n\nSection 395\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(4) Subsections (2) and (3) do not, by implication, limit the matters to\nwhich the ACMA may have regard.\n\n(5) If the ACMA decides to refuse to issue the connection permit, it\nmust give the applicant a written notice setting out the decision."
    },
