    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-397",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "397 Duration of connection permits",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-397"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.329",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A connection permit comes into force when it is issued and\nremains in force:\n\n(a) if the permit specifies a day of expiration—until the end of\nthat day; or\n\n(b) otherwise—indefinitely.\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a\nconnection permit, declare that the permit has effect as if the\npermit had specified a day specified in the notice as the day of\nexpiration of the connection permit. The declaration has effect\naccordingly.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A connection permit comes into force when it is issued and\nremains in force:\n\n(a) if the permit specifies a day of expiration—until the end of\nthat day; or\n\n(b) otherwise—indefinitely.\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a\nconnection permit, declare that the permit has effect as if the\npermit had specified a day specified in the notice as the day of\nexpiration of the connection permit. The declaration has effect\naccordingly.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-397-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-397-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0884c8ee0b557e1bcfe91125bdf54a8b52fdb7898cf5f1b722967e78fd51ef77"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-397",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "397 Duration of connection permits",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 329,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A connection permit comes into force when it is issued and\nremains in force:\n\n(a) if the permit specifies a day of expiration—until the end of\nthat day; or\n\n(b) otherwise—indefinitely.\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a\nconnection permit, declare that the permit has effect as if the\npermit had specified a day specified in the notice as the day of\nexpiration of the connection permit. The declaration has effect\naccordingly."
    },
