    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "404 Connection rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-404"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.333",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules\n(connection rules) that:\n\n(a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and\n\n(b) relate to any or all of the following:\n\n(i) the connection of specified customer equipment to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility;\n\n(ii) maintaining a connection referred to in\nsubparagraph (i);\n\n(iii) the connection of specified customer cabling to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility;\n\n(iv) maintaining a connection referred to in\nsubparagraph (iii).\nNote 1:\nA person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class\nor in any other way.\nNote 2:\nEquipment or cabling may be specified by name, by inclusion in a\nspecified class or in any other way.\n\n(2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to\nthe connection rules.\n\n(3) The connection rules may make provision for or in relation to a\nparticular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of\nan administrative character.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules\n(connection rules) that:\n\n(a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and\n\n(b) relate to any or all of the following:\n\n(i) the connection of specified customer equipment to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility;\n\n(ii) maintaining a connection referred to in\nsubparagraph (i);\n\n(iii) the connection of specified customer cabling to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility;\n\n(iv) maintaining a connection referred to in\nsubparagraph (iii).\nNote 1:\nA person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class\nor in any other way.\nNote 2:\nEquipment or cabling may be specified by name, by inclusion in a\nspecified class or in any other way.\n\n(2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to\nthe connection rules.\n\n(3) The connection rules may make provision for or in relation to a\nparticular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of\nan administrative character.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ea10a1458f146a5f39938ac1546a8f2195f7a072bce8acc55145dd0b02831c53"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-404",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "404 Connection rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 333,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules\n(connection rules) that:\n\n(a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and\n\n(b) relate to any or all of the following:\n\n(i) the connection of specified customer equipment to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility;\n\n(ii) maintaining a connection referred to in\nsubparagraph (i);\n\n(iii) the connection of specified customer cabling to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility;\n\n(iv) maintaining a connection referred to in\nsubparagraph (iii).\nNote 1:\nA person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class\nor in any other way.\nNote 2:\nEquipment or cabling may be specified by name, by inclusion in a\nspecified class or in any other way.\n\n(2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to\nthe connection rules.\n\n(3) The connection rules may make provision for or in relation to a\nparticular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of\nan administrative character."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "404(1) Connection rules",
