          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-408-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-408-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ffa7afeb652eed833de3415b9614cbe0c9ca19c967aa69fa06309961478c2fdf",
      "skos:note": "Manufacturer or importer must retain records and declaration for inspection.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-408-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "408(6) Requirements to apply labels—ancillary matters",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 336,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The instrument may specify requirements that must be met after a\nlabel has been applied to customer equipment or customer cabling,\nincluding (but not limited to) a requirement that a manufacturer or\nimporter retain for inspection, for the period specified in the\ninstrument:\n\n(a) records of the quality assurance programs conducted in\naccordance with the instrument in respect of the equipment\nor cabling; and\n\n(b) records of any results of any tests conducted in relation to\ncompliance with the standards specified in the instrument;\nand\n\n(c) a declaration, or a copy of a declaration, made as mentioned\nin paragraph (5)(e)."
    },
