    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-412-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "412(3) Connection of labelled customer equipment or customer cabling",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-412-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.340",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A manager of a telecommunications network, or of a facility, does\nnot contravene subsection (1) in relation to a refusal to give\nconsent to the connection of customer equipment, or customer\ncabling, to the network, or to the facility, if:\n\n(a) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that a label\nhas been applied to the equipment or cabling in contravention\nof section 414 or 416; or\n\n(b) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that the\nconnection would, or would be likely to, constitute a threat to\nthe integrity of a telecommunications network or of a facility;\nor\n\n(c) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that the\nconnection would, or would be likely to, constitute a threat to\nthe health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A manager of a telecommunications network, or of a facility, does\nnot contravene subsection (1) in relation to a refusal to give\nconsent to the connection of customer equipment, or customer\ncabling, to the network, or to the facility, if:\n\n(a) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that a label\nhas been applied to the equipment or cabling in contravention\nof section 414 or 416; or\n\n(b) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that the\nconnection would, or would be likely to, constitute a threat to\nthe integrity of a telecommunications network or of a facility;\nor\n\n(c) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that the\nconnection would, or would be likely to, constitute a threat to\nthe health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-412"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-412-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-412-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-412-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-412-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4cff5df98757f47aa5f76bc11a728d9bce8f5465f52986d1051a61500fdf7cc6",
      "skos:note": "Manager's refusal to connect customer equipment or cabling is justified if there are reasonable grounds for concern about integrity, health, or safety."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-412-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "412(3) Connection of labelled customer equipment or customer cabling",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 340,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A manager of a telecommunications network, or of a facility, does\nnot contravene subsection (1) in relation to a refusal to give\nconsent to the connection of customer equipment, or customer\ncabling, to the network, or to the facility, if:\n\n(a) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that a label\nhas been applied to the equipment or cabling in contravention\nof section 414 or 416; or\n\n(b) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that the\nconnection would, or would be likely to, constitute a threat to\nthe integrity of a telecommunications network or of a facility;\nor\n\n(c) the manager has reasonable grounds to believe that the\nconnection would, or would be likely to, constitute a threat to\nthe health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;"
    },
