    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-413",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "413 Supply of unlabelled customer equipment or unlabelled",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-413"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.342",
      "values:originalText": "customer cabling\n\n(1) If a person:\n\n(a) is a manufacturer or importer of customer equipment or\ncustomer cabling; and\n\n(b) is required under section 407 to apply to it a label in a\nparticular form;\nthe person must not supply the equipment or cabling unless a label\nin that form has been applied to the equipment or cabling.\n\n(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 100 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\nNote 2:\nSee also Division 13 of this Part (which deals with the payment of\npenalties as an alternative to prosecution).\n\n(2A) Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2A) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase.",
      "skos:definition": "customer cabling\n\n(1) If a person:\n\n(a) is a manufacturer or importer of customer equipment or\ncustomer cabling; and\n\n(b) is required under section 407 to apply to it a label in a\nparticular form;\nthe person must not supply the equipment or cabling unless a label\nin that form has been applied to the equipment or cabling.\n\n(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 100 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\nNote 2:\nSee also Division 13 of this Part (which deals with the payment of\npenalties as an alternative to prosecution).\n\n(2A) Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2A) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-413-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-413-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-413-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-413-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7c42b4d72e99422696106cbc8e3b1303f36772dd20fe2d6218dcfceea4a43f4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-413",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "413 Supply of unlabelled customer equipment or unlabelled",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 342,
      "values:originalText": "customer cabling\n\n(1) If a person:\n\n(a) is a manufacturer or importer of customer equipment or\ncustomer cabling; and\n\n(b) is required under section 407 to apply to it a label in a\nparticular form;\nthe person must not supply the equipment or cabling unless a label\nin that form has been applied to the equipment or cabling.\n\n(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 100 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\nNote 2:\nSee also Division 13 of this Part (which deals with the payment of\npenalties as an alternative to prosecution).\n\n(2A) Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2A) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase."
    },
