    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-420-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPart",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the scope of the prohibition.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) A person must not perform a particular type of cabling work\nunless:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-421",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "421 Cabling provider rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-421"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.350",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules (cabling\nprovider rules) that:\n\n(a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and\n\n(b) relate to:\n\n(i) the performance of cabling work; or\n\n(ii) the supervision of the performance of cabling work;\n\nor both.\nNote:\nA person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class\nor in any other way.\n\n(2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to\nthe cabling provider rules.\n\n(3) A person who is subject to the cabling provider rules must comply\nwith the cabling provider rules.\n\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 100 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\nNote 2:\nSee also Division 13 of this Part (which deals with the payment of\npenalties as an alternative to prosecution).\n\n(5) The cabling provider rules may make provision for or in relation to\na particular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of\nan administrative character.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 422\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules (cabling\nprovider rules) that:\n\n(a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and\n\n(b) relate to:\n\n(i) the performance of cabling work; or\n\n(ii) the supervision of the performance of cabling work;\n\nor both.\nNote:\nA person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class\nor in any other way.\n\n(2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to\nthe cabling provider rules.\n\n(3) A person who is subject to the cabling provider rules must comply\nwith the cabling provider rules.\n\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 100 penalty units.\nNote 1:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\nNote 2:\nSee also Division 13 of this Part (which deals with the payment of\npenalties as an alternative to prosecution).\n\n(5) The cabling provider rules may make provision for or in relation to\na particular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of\nan administrative character.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 422\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-421-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-421-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-421-ss-3"
