    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-427",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "427 Grant of cabling licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-427"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.352",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application, the ACMA may grant a cabling\nlicence in accordance with the application.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 428\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The ACMA must not grant a cabling licence authorising the\nperformance of a particular type of cabling work unless it is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the applicant has the necessary knowledge and experience to\nperform cabling work of that type; and\n\n(b) cabling work of that type performed in accordance with the\nconditions included in the licence would comply with\nstandards in force under section 376; and\n\n(c) the issue of the licence is not contrary to directions given by\nthe Minister under section 440.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After considering an application, the ACMA may grant a cabling\nlicence in accordance with the application.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 428\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The ACMA must not grant a cabling licence authorising the\nperformance of a particular type of cabling work unless it is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the applicant has the necessary knowledge and experience to\nperform cabling work of that type; and\n\n(b) cabling work of that type performed in accordance with the\nconditions included in the licence would comply with\nstandards in force under section 376; and\n\n(c) the issue of the licence is not contrary to directions given by\nthe Minister under section 440.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-427-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-427-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2eafc5293f762de39ca8cced5102e7a8385a4a18303d27ce46f7a7c0b0bee406"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-427",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "427 Grant of cabling licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 352,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application, the ACMA may grant a cabling\nlicence in accordance with the application.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 428\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The ACMA must not grant a cabling licence authorising the\nperformance of a particular type of cabling work unless it is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the applicant has the necessary knowledge and experience to\nperform cabling work of that type; and\n\n(b) cabling work of that type performed in accordance with the\nconditions included in the licence would comply with\nstandards in force under section 376; and\n\n(c) the issue of the licence is not contrary to directions given by\nthe Minister under section 440."
    },
