      "cml:premiseText": "the issue of the licence is not contrary to directions given by the Minister under section 440"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-428",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "428 Time limit on licence decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-428"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.353",
      "values:originalText": "If the ACMA neither grants, nor refuses to grant, a cabling licence\nbefore the end of whichever of the following periods is applicable:\n\n(a) if the ACMA did not give a request under section 426 in\nrelation to the licence application—the period of 30 days\nafter the day on which the ACMA received the application;\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the ACMA gave a request under section 426 in relation\nto the licence application; and\n\n(ii) the request was complied with;\n\nthe period of 30 days after the day on which the request was\ncomplied with;\n\n(c) if:\n\n(i) the ACMA gave a request under section 426 in relation\nto the licence application; and\n\n(ii) the request was not complied with;\n\nthe period of 30 days after the end of the period specified in\nthe request;\nthe ACMA is taken, at the end of that 30-day period, to have\nrefused to grant the licence under section 427.",
      "skos:definition": "If the ACMA neither grants, nor refuses to grant, a cabling licence\nbefore the end of whichever of the following periods is applicable:\n\n(a) if the ACMA did not give a request under section 426 in\nrelation to the licence application—the period of 30 days\nafter the day on which the ACMA received the application;\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the ACMA gave a request under section 426 in relation\nto the licence application; and\n\n(ii) the request was complied with;\n\nthe period of 30 days after the day on which the request was\ncomplied with;\n\n(c) if:\n\n(i) the ACMA gave a request under section 426 in relation\nto the licence application; and\n\n(ii) the request was not complied with;\n\nthe period of 30 days after the end of the period specified in\nthe request;\nthe ACMA is taken, at the end of that 30-day period, to have\nrefused to grant the licence under section 427.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-428-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-428-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ee94fdbae7caaa543510121bbe0000fb5ff0970c7e6000eb8f585148e1aea47",
      "skos:note": "Time limit for ACMA decision on licence application"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-428",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "428 Time limit on licence decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 353,
      "values:originalText": "If the ACMA neither grants, nor refuses to grant, a cabling licence\nbefore the end of whichever of the following periods is applicable:\n\n(a) if the ACMA did not give a request under section 426 in\nrelation to the licence application—the period of 30 days\nafter the day on which the ACMA received the application;\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the ACMA gave a request under section 426 in relation\nto the licence application; and\n\n(ii) the request was complied with;\n\nthe period of 30 days after the day on which the request was\ncomplied with;\n\n(c) if:\n\n(i) the ACMA gave a request under section 426 in relation\nto the licence application; and\n\n(ii) the request was not complied with;\n\nthe period of 30 days after the end of the period specified in\nthe request;\nthe ACMA is taken, at the end of that 30-day period, to have\nrefused to grant the licence under section 427."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-428-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
