    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "432 Conditions of cabling licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-432"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.354",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A cabling licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in a\nwritten determination made by the ACMA for the purposes of this\nsubsection.\n\n(2) A cabling licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in\nthe licence.\n\n(3) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence:\n\n(a) impose one or more further conditions to which the licence is\nsubject; or\n\n(b) revoke or vary any condition:\n\n(i) imposed under paragraph (a); or\n\n(ii) specified in the licence.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 433\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The following are examples of conditions to which a cabling\nlicence could be subject:\n\n(a) conditions relating to the types of premises in or on which\nthe holder of the licence may perform cabling work;\n\n(b) conditions requiring customer cabling to be inspected by\npersons authorised in writing by the ACMA for the purposes\nof this paragraph.\n\n(5) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A cabling licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in a\nwritten determination made by the ACMA for the purposes of this\nsubsection.\n\n(2) A cabling licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in\nthe licence.\n\n(3) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence:\n\n(a) impose one or more further conditions to which the licence is\nsubject; or\n\n(b) revoke or vary any condition:\n\n(i) imposed under paragraph (a); or\n\n(ii) specified in the licence.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 433\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The following are examples of conditions to which a cabling\nlicence could be subject:\n\n(a) conditions relating to the types of premises in or on which\nthe holder of the licence may perform cabling work;\n\n(b) conditions requiring customer cabling to be inspected by\npersons authorised in writing by the ACMA for the purposes\nof this paragraph.\n\n(5) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37a3b12679f317cb659a61bedef82f2631bb519030543f682e43462c8b9e3c53"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-432",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "432 Conditions of cabling licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 354,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A cabling licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in a\nwritten determination made by the ACMA for the purposes of this\nsubsection.\n\n(2) A cabling licence is subject to such conditions as are specified in\nthe licence.\n\n(3) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence:\n\n(a) impose one or more further conditions to which the licence is\nsubject; or\n\n(b) revoke or vary any condition:\n\n(i) imposed under paragraph (a); or\n\n(ii) specified in the licence.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 433\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The following are examples of conditions to which a cabling\nlicence could be subject:\n\n(a) conditions relating to the types of premises in or on which\nthe holder of the licence may perform cabling work;\n\n(b) conditions requiring customer cabling to be inspected by\npersons authorised in writing by the ACMA for the purposes\nof this paragraph.\n\n(5) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument."
    },
