        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-432-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99fe419923d467b6f2371c47a8a4d7d337bd060250d18a901dc877526853587c",
      "skos:note": "Conditions for cabling licence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-432-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "432(4) Conditions of cabling licence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 354,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The following are examples of conditions to which a cabling\nlicence could be subject:\n\n(a) conditions relating to the types of premises in or on which\nthe holder of the licence may perform cabling work;\n\n(b) conditions requiring customer cabling to be inspected by\npersons authorised in writing by the ACMA for the purposes\nof this paragraph."
    },
