    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-433",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "433 Procedures for changing licence conditions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-433"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.355",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA’s powers under subsection 432(3) may be exercised:\n\n(a) on the ACMA’s own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application made to the ACMA by the holder of the\nlicence.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) be in accordance with the form approved in writing by the\nACMA.\n\n(3) The approved form of application may provide for verification by\nstatutory declaration of statements in applications.\n\n(4) If the ACMA refuses an application under paragraph (1)(b), the\nACMA must give written notice of the refusal to the applicant.\n\n(5) If the ACMA neither grants, nor refuses to grant, an application\nunder paragraph (1)(b) before the end of 30 days after receiving the\napplication, the ACMA is taken, at the end of that period, to have\nrefused the application.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA’s powers under subsection 432(3) may be exercised:\n\n(a) on the ACMA’s own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application made to the ACMA by the holder of the\nlicence.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) be in accordance with the form approved in writing by the\nACMA.\n\n(3) The approved form of application may provide for verification by\nstatutory declaration of statements in applications.\n\n(4) If the ACMA refuses an application under paragraph (1)(b), the\nACMA must give written notice of the refusal to the applicant.\n\n(5) If the ACMA neither grants, nor refuses to grant, an application\nunder paragraph (1)(b) before the end of 30 days after receiving the\napplication, the ACMA is taken, at the end of that period, to have\nrefused the application.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-433-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-433-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-433-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-433-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-433-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9ef809b0e86e5d0c4f6fbe9d23df3422de16a170598ecad207be3f476b694379"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-433",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "433 Procedures for changing licence conditions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 355,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA’s powers under subsection 432(3) may be exercised:\n\n(a) on the ACMA’s own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application made to the ACMA by the holder of the\nlicence.\n\n(2) An application under paragraph (1)(b) must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) be in accordance with the form approved in writing by the\nACMA.\n\n(3) The approved form of application may provide for verification by\nstatutory declaration of statements in applications.\n\n(4) If the ACMA refuses an application under paragraph (1)(b), the\nACMA must give written notice of the refusal to the applicant.\n\n(5) If the ACMA neither grants, nor refuses to grant, an application\nunder paragraph (1)(b) before the end of 30 days after receiving the\napplication, the ACMA is taken, at the end of that period, to have\nrefused the application."
    },
    {
