    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "437 Suspension of cabling licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-437"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.357",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence, suspend the cabling licence for a period of not longer than\n28 days.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to suspend the cabling licence, the ACMA\nmust have regard to:\n\n(a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under\nsection 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a\ncabling licence; and\n\n(b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been\nconvicted of an offence against this Division.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nthe ACMA may have regard.\n\n(4) During the period of suspension, section 420 has effect as if the\nlicence did not exist.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence, suspend the cabling licence for a period of not longer than\n28 days.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to suspend the cabling licence, the ACMA\nmust have regard to:\n\n(a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under\nsection 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a\ncabling licence; and\n\n(b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been\nconvicted of an offence against this Division.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nthe ACMA may have regard.\n\n(4) During the period of suspension, section 420 has effect as if the\nlicence did not exist.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ab39035877bc83956641ad79b3df59e0f2fe7e7a03a6f590e4876423c0f4655"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-437",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "437 Suspension of cabling licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 357,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence, suspend the cabling licence for a period of not longer than\n28 days.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to suspend the cabling licence, the ACMA\nmust have regard to:\n\n(a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under\nsection 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a\ncabling licence; and\n\n(b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been\nconvicted of an offence against this Division.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which\nthe ACMA may have regard.\n\n(4) During the period of suspension, section 420 has effect as if the\nlicence did not exist."
    },
