    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-438",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "438 Cancellation of cabling licence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-438"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.357",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence, cancel the cabling licence.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to cancel the cabling licence, the ACMA must\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under\nsection 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a\ncabling licence; and\n\n(b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been\nconvicted of an offence against this Division.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence, cancel the cabling licence.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to cancel the cabling licence, the ACMA must\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under\nsection 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a\ncabling licence; and\n\n(b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been\nconvicted of an offence against this Division.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-438-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-438-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cc380e4a18e1fce5d0162873545b37d718446f5dc47a13528a996ab5959dedf1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-438",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "438 Cancellation of cabling licence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 357,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling\nlicence, cancel the cabling licence.\n\n(2) In deciding whether to cancel the cabling licence, the ACMA must\nhave regard to:\n\n(a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under\nsection 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a\ncabling licence; and\n\n(b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been\nconvicted of an offence against this Division."
    },
