    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-439",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "439 ACMA may limit application of Division in relation to customer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-439"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.358",
      "values:originalText": "cabling\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, declare that this\nDivision, or specified provisions of it, do not apply in relation to\nspecified kinds of customer cabling.\n\n(2) An instrument under subsection (1) may specify a kind of customer\ncabling:\n\n(a) by reference to the technical characteristics of the cabling; or\n\n(b) by reference to the functions of the cabling; or\n\n(c) by reference to the purposes for which the cabling is used, or\nis intended to be used, by the customer concerned; or\n\n(d) by reference to the location of the cabling.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) This Division has effect in accordance with an instrument in force\nunder subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "cabling\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, declare that this\nDivision, or specified provisions of it, do not apply in relation to\nspecified kinds of customer cabling.\n\n(2) An instrument under subsection (1) may specify a kind of customer\ncabling:\n\n(a) by reference to the technical characteristics of the cabling; or\n\n(b) by reference to the functions of the cabling; or\n\n(c) by reference to the purposes for which the cabling is used, or\nis intended to be used, by the customer concerned; or\n\n(d) by reference to the location of the cabling.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) This Division has effect in accordance with an instrument in force\nunder subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-439-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-439-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-439-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-439-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f62bf83dfd84cce77a3daa9fa3e3f681a5c7f8770e3ae8b10d52ad05ab183a15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-439",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "439 ACMA may limit application of Division in relation to customer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 358,
      "values:originalText": "cabling\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, declare that this\nDivision, or specified provisions of it, do not apply in relation to\nspecified kinds of customer cabling.\n\n(2) An instrument under subsection (1) may specify a kind of customer\ncabling:\n\n(a) by reference to the technical characteristics of the cabling; or\n\n(b) by reference to the functions of the cabling; or\n\n(c) by reference to the purposes for which the cabling is used, or\nis intended to be used, by the customer concerned; or\n\n(d) by reference to the location of the cabling.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) This Division has effect in accordance with an instrument in force\nunder subsection (1)."
    },
    {
