    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-440",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "440 Ministerial directions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-440"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.358",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give the ACMA\nwritten directions about how it is to perform its functions or\nexercise its powers under this Division.\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) may require the ACMA to make\ncabling provider rules that deal with one or more specified matters.\n\n(2A) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(3) A direction under subsection (1) must not concern the way in\nwhich the ACMA is to deal with a particular application for a\ncabling licence.\n\n(4) The Minister must not give the ACMA a direction under section 14\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 441\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nabout how the ACMA is to perform its functions or exercise its\npowers under this Division.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give the ACMA\nwritten directions about how it is to perform its functions or\nexercise its powers under this Division.\n\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) may require the ACMA to make\ncabling provider rules that deal with one or more specified matters.\n\n(2A) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(3) A direction under subsection (1) must not concern the way in\nwhich the ACMA is to deal with a particular application for a\ncabling licence.\n\n(4) The Minister must not give the ACMA a direction under section 14\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nCabling providers  Division 9\n\nSection 441\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nabout how the ACMA is to perform its functions or exercise its\npowers under this Division.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-440-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-440-ss-2"
        },
