    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-442",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "442 Register of cabling licences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-442"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA is to maintain a Register in which it includes:\n\n(a) all cabling licences currently in force; and\n\n(b) all conditions of such licences.\n\n(2) The Register may be maintained by electronic means.\n\n(3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a\ndetermination under section 60 of the Australian Communications\nand Media Authority Act 2005:\n\n(a) inspect the Register; and\n\n(b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, if the Register is maintained by\nelectronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or\ntaken an extract from, the Register if the ACMA gives the person a\nprintout of, or of the relevant parts of, the Register.\n\n(5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form,\nthe ACMA may provide the relevant information:\n\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 443\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA is to maintain a Register in which it includes:\n\n(a) all cabling licences currently in force; and\n\n(b) all conditions of such licences.\n\n(2) The Register may be maintained by electronic means.\n\n(3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a\ndetermination under section 60 of the Australian Communications\nand Media Authority Act 2005:\n\n(a) inspect the Register; and\n\n(b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, if the Register is maintained by\nelectronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or\ntaken an extract from, the Register if the ACMA gives the person a\nprintout of, or of the relevant parts of, the Register.\n\n(5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form,\nthe ACMA may provide the relevant information:\n\n(a) on a data processing device; or\n\n(b) by way of electronic transmission.\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 443\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-442-ss-1"
        },
