    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "444 Remedy for contravention of labelling requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-444"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.362",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person (the first person) contravenes section 413, 414 or\n415 in relation to particular customer equipment or particular\ncustomer cabling; and\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 445\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person (who may be the first person) connects the\nequipment or cabling to a telecommunications network or to\na facility; and\n\n(c) as a result of:\n\n(i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the\nnetwork or facility; or\n\n(ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so\nconnected;\n\neither:\n\n(iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or\n\n(iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss;\nthe manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal\nCourt for the recovery from the first person of the amount of the\nloss or damage.\n\n(2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after\nthe damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case\nrequires.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person (the first person) contravenes section 413, 414 or\n415 in relation to particular customer equipment or particular\ncustomer cabling; and\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 445\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person (who may be the first person) connects the\nequipment or cabling to a telecommunications network or to\na facility; and\n\n(c) as a result of:\n\n(i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the\nnetwork or facility; or\n\n(ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so\nconnected;\n\neither:\n\n(iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or\n\n(iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss;\nthe manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal\nCourt for the recovery from the first person of the amount of the\nloss or damage.\n\n(2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after\nthe damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case\nrequires.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "379ef88d037012728a7dea193b94c6e8ce50f1697759ed23bab9d8de06af9949"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-444",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "444 Remedy for contravention of labelling requirements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 362,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person (the first person) contravenes section 413, 414 or\n415 in relation to particular customer equipment or particular\ncustomer cabling; and\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 445\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person (who may be the first person) connects the\nequipment or cabling to a telecommunications network or to\na facility; and\n\n(c) as a result of:\n\n(i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the\nnetwork or facility; or\n\n(ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so\nconnected;\n\neither:\n\n(iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or\n\n(iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss;\nthe manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal\nCourt for the recovery from the first person of the amount of the\nloss or damage.\n\n(2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after\nthe damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case\nrequires."
    },
