      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the manager of the network or facility has an honest belief...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the manager of the network or facility may:..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "447(2) Disconnection of customer equipment or customer cabling—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-447-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.367",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) equipment or cabling is disconnected, or purportedly\ndisconnected, under subsection (1); and\n\n(b) the ACMA is satisfied that there were no reasonable grounds\nfor the belief mentioned in paragraph (1)(b);\nthe ACMA may, by written notice given to the manager of the\nnetwork or facility, direct the manager to reconnect the equipment\nor cabling.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n\n(a) equipment or cabling is disconnected, or purportedly\ndisconnected, under subsection (1); and\n\n(b) the ACMA is satisfied that there were no reasonable grounds\nfor the belief mentioned in paragraph (1)(b);\nthe ACMA may, by written notice given to the manager of the\nnetwork or facility, direct the manager to reconnect the equipment\nor cabling.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-447-ss-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2eab82c009f5bd9b62270859abc685c4f6d96618b2104ee141359dd58889cb6",
      "skos:note": "Direct manager to reconnect equipment or cabling if ACMA believes no reasonable grounds for disconnection existed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-447-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "447(2) Disconnection of customer equipment or customer cabling—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 367,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) equipment or cabling is disconnected, or purportedly\ndisconnected, under subsection (1); and\n\n(b) the ACMA is satisfied that there were no reasonable grounds\nfor the belief mentioned in paragraph (1)(b);\nthe ACMA may, by written notice given to the manager of the\nnetwork or facility, direct the manager to reconnect the equipment\nor cabling."
    },
    {
