    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-448",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "448 Civil action for dangerous connections to telecommunications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-448"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.368",
      "values:originalText": "networks etc.\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person:\n\n(i) connects customer equipment, or customer cabling, to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility; or\n\n(ii) has under his or her control customer equipment, or\ncustomer cabling, connected to a telecommunications\nnetwork or to a facility; and\n\n(b) the equipment or cabling is, or is likely to be, a threat to the\nhealth or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility; and\n\n(c) as a result of:\n\n(i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the\nnetwork or facility; or\n\n(ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so\nconnected;\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 449\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\neither:\n\n(iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or\n\n(iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss;\nthe manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal\nCourt for the recovery from the person of the amount of the loss or\ndamage.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) must be made within 3 years\nafter the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case\nrequires.",
      "skos:definition": "networks etc.\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person:\n\n(i) connects customer equipment, or customer cabling, to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility; or\n\n(ii) has under his or her control customer equipment, or\ncustomer cabling, connected to a telecommunications\nnetwork or to a facility; and\n\n(b) the equipment or cabling is, or is likely to be, a threat to the\nhealth or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility; and\n\n(c) as a result of:\n\n(i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the\nnetwork or facility; or\n\n(ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so\nconnected;\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 449\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\neither:\n\n(iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or\n\n(iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss;\nthe manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal\nCourt for the recovery from the person of the amount of the loss or\ndamage.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) must be made within 3 years\nafter the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case\nrequires.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-448-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-448-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de2738bf7af07d81f92d5fde35c72597dec17c168a041d6b54f16087b9aa9daf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-448",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "448 Civil action for dangerous connections to telecommunications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 368,
      "values:originalText": "networks etc.\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person:\n\n(i) connects customer equipment, or customer cabling, to a\ntelecommunications network or to a facility; or\n\n(ii) has under his or her control customer equipment, or\ncustomer cabling, connected to a telecommunications\nnetwork or to a facility; and\n\n(b) the equipment or cabling is, or is likely to be, a threat to the\nhealth or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility; and\n\n(c) as a result of:\n\n(i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the\nnetwork or facility; or\n\n(ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so\nconnected;\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nRemedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division\n\nSection 449\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\neither:\n\n(iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or\n\n(iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss;\nthe manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal\nCourt for the recovery from the person of the amount of the loss or\ndamage.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) must be made within 3 years\nafter the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case\nrequires."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-448-ss-1",
