    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-450",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "450 Declaration of prohibited customer equipment or prohibited",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-450"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.370",
      "values:originalText": "customer cabling\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, declare that operation\nor supply, or possession for the purpose of operation or supply, of:\n\n(a) specified customer equipment; or\n\n(b) specified customer cabling;\nis prohibited for the reasons set out in the instrument.\n\n(2) Those reasons must relate to:\n\n(a) the protection of the integrity of a telecommunications\nnetwork or of a facility; or\n\n(b) the protection of the health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(3) A copy of an instrument under subsection (1) must be published on\nthe ACMA’s website.\n\n(5) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase.",
      "skos:definition": "customer cabling\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, declare that operation\nor supply, or possession for the purpose of operation or supply, of:\n\n(a) specified customer equipment; or\n\n(b) specified customer cabling;\nis prohibited for the reasons set out in the instrument.\n\n(2) Those reasons must relate to:\n\n(a) the protection of the integrity of a telecommunications\nnetwork or of a facility; or\n\n(b) the protection of the health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(3) A copy of an instrument under subsection (1) must be published on\nthe ACMA’s website.\n\n(5) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-450-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-450-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-450-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-450-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7c42b4d72e99422696106cbc8e3b1303f36772dd20fe2d6218dcfceea4a43f4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-450",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "450 Declaration of prohibited customer equipment or prohibited",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 370,
      "values:originalText": "customer cabling\n\n(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, declare that operation\nor supply, or possession for the purpose of operation or supply, of:\n\n(a) specified customer equipment; or\n\n(b) specified customer cabling;\nis prohibited for the reasons set out in the instrument.\n\n(2) Those reasons must relate to:\n\n(a) the protection of the integrity of a telecommunications\nnetwork or of a facility; or\n\n(b) the protection of the health or safety of persons who:\n\n(i) operate; or\n\n(ii) work on; or\n\n(iii) use services supplied by means of; or\n\n(iv) are otherwise reasonably likely to be affected by the\noperation of;\n\na telecommunications network or a facility.\n\n(3) A copy of an instrument under subsection (1) must be published on\nthe ACMA’s website.\n\n(5) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase."
    },
