    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-452",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "452 Operation of prohibited customer equipment or customer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-452"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.370",
      "values:originalText": "cabling\n\n(1) A person must not:\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nProhibited customer equipment and prohibited customer cabling  Division 11\n\nSection 452\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) operate or supply customer equipment, or customer cabling,\nin respect of which a declaration is in force under\nsection 450; or\n\n(b) have in his or her possession customer equipment, or\ncustomer cabling, in respect of which such a declaration is in\nforce, if the possession is for the purpose of operating or\nsupplying the equipment or cabling.\n\n(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 2,000 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\n\n(3) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase.",
      "skos:definition": "cabling\n\n(1) A person must not:\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nProhibited customer equipment and prohibited customer cabling  Division 11\n\nSection 452\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) operate or supply customer equipment, or customer cabling,\nin respect of which a declaration is in force under\nsection 450; or\n\n(b) have in his or her possession customer equipment, or\ncustomer cabling, in respect of which such a declaration is in\nforce, if the possession is for the purpose of operating or\nsupplying the equipment or cabling.\n\n(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 2,000 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\n\n(3) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-452-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-452-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-452-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f62bf83dfd84cce77a3daa9fa3e3f681a5c7f8770e3ae8b10d52ad05ab183a15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-452",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "452 Operation of prohibited customer equipment or customer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 370,
      "values:originalText": "cabling\n\n(1) A person must not:\n\n\nTechnical regulation  Part 21\nProhibited customer equipment and prohibited customer cabling  Division 11\n\nSection 452\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) operate or supply customer equipment, or customer cabling,\nin respect of which a declaration is in force under\nsection 450; or\n\n(b) have in his or her possession customer equipment, or\ncustomer cabling, in respect of which such a declaration is in\nforce, if the possession is for the purpose of operating or\nsupplying the equipment or cabling.\n\n(2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence\npunishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 2,000 penalty\nunits.\nNote:\nSee also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.\n\n(3) In this section:\nsupply includes supply (including re-supply) by way of sale,\nexchange, lease, hire or hire-purchase."
    },
