      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) The amount of penalty payable to the Commonwealth..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "454 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe numbering of carriages services in Australia, and the use\nof numbers in connection with the supply of such services,\nmay either be:\n\n(a)\nmanaged by a numbering scheme manager determined\nby the Minister; or\n\n(b)\nadministered by the ACMA under a numbering plan.\n•\nNumbers may be allocated to carriage service providers:\n\n(a)\nin accordance with an allocation system; or\n\n(b)\notherwise than in accordance with such a system.\n•\nThe ACMA will specify emergency service numbers.\n•\nThe ACMA and the ACCC may give directions to managers\nof electronic addressing so long as the electronic addressing is\nof public importance.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 454A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe numbering of carriages services in Australia, and the use\nof numbers in connection with the supply of such services,\nmay either be:\n\n(a)\nmanaged by a numbering scheme manager determined\nby the Minister; or\n\n(b)\nadministered by the ACMA under a numbering plan.\n•\nNumbers may be allocated to carriage service providers:\n\n(a)\nin accordance with an allocation system; or\n\n(b)\notherwise than in accordance with such a system.\n•\nThe ACMA will specify emergency service numbers.\n•\nThe ACMA and the ACCC may give directions to managers\nof electronic addressing so long as the electronic addressing is\nof public importance.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 454A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6af00787fb3f8f2f6617097c2db0c75322dc1b28d17f666e9c4285daca91e2ce",
      "skos:note": "Simplified outline of Part 22, Division 2, Section 454A"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "454 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe numbering of carriages services in Australia, and the use\nof numbers in connection with the supply of such services,\nmay either be:\n\n(a)\nmanaged by a numbering scheme manager determined\nby the Minister; or\n\n(b)\nadministered by the ACMA under a numbering plan.\n•\nNumbers may be allocated to carriage service providers:\n\n(a)\nin accordance with an allocation system; or\n\n(b)\notherwise than in accordance with such a system.\n•\nThe ACMA will specify emergency service numbers.\n•\nThe ACMA and the ACCC may give directions to managers\nof electronic addressing so long as the electronic addressing is\nof public importance.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 454A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "454A Minister may determine numbering scheme manager",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.375",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified person is to manage the numbering scheme.\n\n(2) The person is the numbering scheme manager.\n\n(3) The Minister must not determine a person as the numbering\nscheme manager unless the Minister is satisfied that the person will\nmanage the numbering scheme in accordance with the numbering\nscheme principles.\n\n(4) Before determining a person as the numbering scheme manager,\nthe Minister must consult with the ACMA and the ACCC.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified person is to manage the numbering scheme.\n\n(2) The person is the numbering scheme manager.\n\n(3) The Minister must not determine a person as the numbering\nscheme manager unless the Minister is satisfied that the person will\nmanage the numbering scheme in accordance with the numbering\nscheme principles.\n\n(4) Before determining a person as the numbering scheme manager,\nthe Minister must consult with the ACMA and the ACCC.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f8279d8a4978c9b7125dfe68973d181a4162556e92b840db3850f3a4931bbd93"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "454A Minister may determine numbering scheme manager",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 375,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified person is to manage the numbering scheme.\n\n(2) The person is the numbering scheme manager.\n\n(3) The Minister must not determine a person as the numbering\nscheme manager unless the Minister is satisfied that the person will\nmanage the numbering scheme in accordance with the numbering\nscheme principles.\n\n(4) Before determining a person as the numbering scheme manager,\nthe Minister must consult with the ACMA and the ACCC."
    },
