    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "454D Revocation of determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.377",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke the\ndetermination of a person as the numbering scheme manager if:\n\n(a) the Minister is not satisfied the person is managing the\nnumbering scheme in accordance with the numbering scheme\nprinciples; or\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of one or\nmore of the following:\n\n(i) the telecommunications industry;\n\n(ii) users of carriage services;\n\n(iii) the general community; or\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of national\nsecurity.\n\n(2) Before the Minister revokes the determination of a person as the\nnumbering scheme manager, the Minister must consult the person,\nthe ACMA and the ACCC.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke the\ndetermination of a person as the numbering scheme manager if:\n\n(a) the Minister is not satisfied the person is managing the\nnumbering scheme in accordance with the numbering scheme\nprinciples; or\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of one or\nmore of the following:\n\n(i) the telecommunications industry;\n\n(ii) users of carriage services;\n\n(iii) the general community; or\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of national\nsecurity.\n\n(2) Before the Minister revokes the determination of a person as the\nnumbering scheme manager, the Minister must consult the person,\nthe ACMA and the ACCC.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a74f7064d71b3cd9362f37d783c9df398c34ff9fd34ac0930b240c6d25cf68c7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "454D Revocation of determination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 377,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke the\ndetermination of a person as the numbering scheme manager if:\n\n(a) the Minister is not satisfied the person is managing the\nnumbering scheme in accordance with the numbering scheme\nprinciples; or\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of one or\nmore of the following:\n\n(i) the telecommunications industry;\n\n(ii) users of carriage services;\n\n(iii) the general community; or\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of national\nsecurity.\n\n(2) Before the Minister revokes the determination of a person as the\nnumbering scheme manager, the Minister must consult the person,\nthe ACMA and the ACCC."
    },
