    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "454F Numbering scheme manager providing information to the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.378",
      "values:originalText": "ACMA\n\n(1) The ACMA may, in writing, request information from the\nnumbering scheme manager relating to numbers for carriage\nservices.\n\n(2) The ACMA may request the information for the following\npurposes:\n\n(a) identifying persons liable for a charge under the\nTelecommunications (Numbering Charges) Act 1997;\n\n(b) working out the amount of a charge under that Act;\n\n(c) otherwise administering charges under that Act.\n\n(3) The request may specify the form in which the information is\nrequired, such as a written report.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 454G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The numbering scheme manager must comply with a request under\nthis section.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "skos:definition": "ACMA\n\n(1) The ACMA may, in writing, request information from the\nnumbering scheme manager relating to numbers for carriage\nservices.\n\n(2) The ACMA may request the information for the following\npurposes:\n\n(a) identifying persons liable for a charge under the\nTelecommunications (Numbering Charges) Act 1997;\n\n(b) working out the amount of a charge under that Act;\n\n(c) otherwise administering charges under that Act.\n\n(3) The request may specify the form in which the information is\nrequired, such as a written report.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 454G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The numbering scheme manager must comply with a request under\nthis section.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454f-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454f-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eff82b672edf854734fe840185a284784b0f9444182cbe5bb142f60f518c8456"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "454F Numbering scheme manager providing information to the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 378,
      "values:originalText": "ACMA\n\n(1) The ACMA may, in writing, request information from the\nnumbering scheme manager relating to numbers for carriage\nservices.\n\n(2) The ACMA may request the information for the following\npurposes:\n\n(a) identifying persons liable for a charge under the\nTelecommunications (Numbering Charges) Act 1997;\n\n(b) working out the amount of a charge under that Act;\n\n(c) otherwise administering charges under that Act.\n\n(3) The request may specify the form in which the information is\nrequired, such as a written report.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 454G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The numbering scheme manager must comply with a request under\nthis section.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions."
    },
