    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "454G Directions to comply with rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.379",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA or the ACCC may, by written notice given to a person\nwho is:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider; or\n\n(b) a carrier; or\n\n(c) a person of a kind determined by the Minister in a\nlegislative instrument;\ndirect the person to comply with a rule or process published by the\nnumbering scheme manager.\n\n(2) The person must comply with the direction.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(4) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA or the ACCC may, by written notice given to a person\nwho is:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider; or\n\n(b) a carrier; or\n\n(c) a person of a kind determined by the Minister in a\nlegislative instrument;\ndirect the person to comply with a rule or process published by the\nnumbering scheme manager.\n\n(2) The person must comply with the direction.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(4) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454g-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90721ed15a277b8f2d8941e2eff324fd7afe2dd48eecacbe904d974d6ef6595b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-454g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "454G Directions to comply with rules",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 379,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA or the ACCC may, by written notice given to a person\nwho is:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider; or\n\n(b) a carrier; or\n\n(c) a person of a kind determined by the Minister in a\nlegislative instrument;\ndirect the person to comply with a rule or process published by the\nnumbering scheme manager.\n\n(2) The person must comply with the direction.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(4) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
