    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-455-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "455(5) Numbering plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-455-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.380",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The numbering plan may set out rules about:\n\n(a) the allocation of numbers to carriage service providers; and\n\n(b) the transfer of allocated numbers between carriage service\nproviders; and\n\n(c) the surrender or withdrawal of allocated numbers; and\n\n(d) the portability of allocated numbers (including rules about\nthe maintenance of, and access to, databases that facilitate\nportability); and\n\n(e) the use of allocated numbers in connection with the supply of\ncarriage services to the public in Australia (including rules\nabout the issue of allocated numbers by carriage service\nproviders to customers for use in connection with the supply\nof carriage services).\nNote 1:\nAllocation is the “second tier” concept. It operates at the level of\nparticular carriage service providers.\nNote 2:\nIssue is the “third tier” concept. It operates at the level of particular\ncustomers of carriage service providers. The issue of an allocated\nnumber to a customer does not affect the allocation of the number to\nthe carriage service provider concerned.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 456\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The numbering plan may set out rules about:\n\n(a) the allocation of numbers to carriage service providers; and\n\n(b) the transfer of allocated numbers between carriage service\nproviders; and\n\n(c) the surrender or withdrawal of allocated numbers; and\n\n(d) the portability of allocated numbers (including rules about\nthe maintenance of, and access to, databases that facilitate\nportability); and\n\n(e) the use of allocated numbers in connection with the supply of\ncarriage services to the public in Australia (including rules\nabout the issue of allocated numbers by carriage service\nproviders to customers for use in connection with the supply\nof carriage services).\nNote 1:\nAllocation is the “second tier” concept. It operates at the level of\nparticular carriage service providers.\nNote 2:\nIssue is the “third tier” concept. It operates at the level of particular\ncustomers of carriage service providers. The issue of an allocated\nnumber to a customer does not affect the allocation of the number to\nthe carriage service provider concerned.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 456\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-455"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-455-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-455-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "edb02ef869b2f61ee1930875dbfd700a0c50c5bf7399467987bdb7b1b71bc593",
      "skos:note": "Rules about allocation, transfer, surrender, portability and use of allocated numbers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-455-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "455(5) Numbering plan",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 380,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The numbering plan may set out rules about:\n\n(a) the allocation of numbers to carriage service providers; and\n\n(b) the transfer of allocated numbers between carriage service\nproviders; and\n\n(c) the surrender or withdrawal of allocated numbers; and\n\n(d) the portability of allocated numbers (including rules about\nthe maintenance of, and access to, databases that facilitate\nportability); and\n\n(e) the use of allocated numbers in connection with the supply of\ncarriage services to the public in Australia (including rules\nabout the issue of allocated numbers by carriage service\nproviders to customers for use in connection with the supply\nof carriage services).\nNote 1:\nAllocation is the “second tier” concept. It operates at the level of\nparticular carriage service providers.\nNote 2:\nIssue is the “third tier” concept. It operates at the level of particular\ncustomers of carriage service providers. The issue of an allocated\nnumber to a customer does not affect the allocation of the number to\nthe carriage service provider concerned.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 456\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
