    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-457",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "457 Numbering plan—allocation otherwise than in accordance with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-457"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.382",
      "values:originalText": "an allocation system\n\n(1) The numbering plan must impose the following requirements in\nrelation to an application for the allocation of a number otherwise\nthan in accordance with an allocation system determined under\nsection 463:\n\n(a) a requirement that the application must be accompanied by\nthe charge (if any) fixed by a determination under section 60\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act\n2005;\n\n(b) a requirement that the applicant must tender the amount of\ncharge (if any) imposed on the allocation by Part 2 of the\nTelecommunications (Numbering Charges) Act 1997.\n\n(2) If an applicant tenders an amount as mentioned in paragraph (1)(b),\nbut the application is not successful, the amount is to be refunded\nto the applicant.",
      "skos:definition": "an allocation system\n\n(1) The numbering plan must impose the following requirements in\nrelation to an application for the allocation of a number otherwise\nthan in accordance with an allocation system determined under\nsection 463:\n\n(a) a requirement that the application must be accompanied by\nthe charge (if any) fixed by a determination under section 60\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act\n2005;\n\n(b) a requirement that the applicant must tender the amount of\ncharge (if any) imposed on the allocation by Part 2 of the\nTelecommunications (Numbering Charges) Act 1997.\n\n(2) If an applicant tenders an amount as mentioned in paragraph (1)(b),\nbut the application is not successful, the amount is to be refunded\nto the applicant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-457-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-457-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "79b09d6d9276e2c23c0c097f65f0a517ee100301128d1b0e0b222f23bcbfb510"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-457",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "457 Numbering plan—allocation otherwise than in accordance with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 382,
      "values:originalText": "an allocation system\n\n(1) The numbering plan must impose the following requirements in\nrelation to an application for the allocation of a number otherwise\nthan in accordance with an allocation system determined under\nsection 463:\n\n(a) a requirement that the application must be accompanied by\nthe charge (if any) fixed by a determination under section 60\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act\n2005;\n\n(b) a requirement that the applicant must tender the amount of\ncharge (if any) imposed on the allocation by Part 2 of the\nTelecommunications (Numbering Charges) Act 1997.\n\n(2) If an applicant tenders an amount as mentioned in paragraph (1)(b),\nbut the application is not successful, the amount is to be refunded\nto the applicant."
    },
