    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "458 Numbering plan—rules about portability of allocated numbers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-458"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.382",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA must not make a numbering plan that sets out rules\nabout the matter mentioned in paragraph 455(5)(d) (portability of\nallocated numbers) unless the ACMA is directed to do so by the\nACCC under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The ACCC may give written directions to the ACMA in relation to\nthe exercise of the power to determine a numbering plan setting out\nrules as mentioned in subsection (1).\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 459\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) In exercising the power conferred by subsection (2), the ACCC\nmust ensure that, at all times when the numbering plan is in force,\nthe plan sets out rules about the matter mentioned in\nparagraph 455(5)(d).\n\n(4) The ACMA must exercise its powers under section 455 in a\nmanner consistent with any directions given by the ACCC under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(5) In exercising the power conferred by subsection (2), the ACCC\nmust have regard to whether portability of particular allocated\nnumbers is required in order to promote the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by means of\ncarriage services.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a particular\nthing promotes the long-term interests of end-users of carriage\nservices or of services supplied by means of carriage services is to\nbe determined in the same manner as that question is determined\nfor the purposes of Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act\n2010.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA must not make a numbering plan that sets out rules\nabout the matter mentioned in paragraph 455(5)(d) (portability of\nallocated numbers) unless the ACMA is directed to do so by the\nACCC under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The ACCC may give written directions to the ACMA in relation to\nthe exercise of the power to determine a numbering plan setting out\nrules as mentioned in subsection (1).\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 459\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) In exercising the power conferred by subsection (2), the ACCC\nmust ensure that, at all times when the numbering plan is in force,\nthe plan sets out rules about the matter mentioned in\nparagraph 455(5)(d).\n\n(4) The ACMA must exercise its powers under section 455 in a\nmanner consistent with any directions given by the ACCC under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(5) In exercising the power conferred by subsection (2), the ACCC\nmust have regard to whether portability of particular allocated\nnumbers is required in order to promote the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by means of\ncarriage services.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a particular\nthing promotes the long-term interests of end-users of carriage\nservices or of services supplied by means of carriage services is to\nbe determined in the same manner as that question is determined\nfor the purposes of Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act\n2010.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-458-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e99fc50ff15c1a35e7a852a2d16f49d7909937982d7362dd35277dc22561ab11"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-458",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "458 Numbering plan—rules about portability of allocated numbers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 382,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA must not make a numbering plan that sets out rules\nabout the matter mentioned in paragraph 455(5)(d) (portability of\nallocated numbers) unless the ACMA is directed to do so by the\nACCC under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The ACCC may give written directions to the ACMA in relation to\nthe exercise of the power to determine a numbering plan setting out\nrules as mentioned in subsection (1).\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 459\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) In exercising the power conferred by subsection (2), the ACCC\nmust ensure that, at all times when the numbering plan is in force,\nthe plan sets out rules about the matter mentioned in\nparagraph 455(5)(d).\n\n(4) The ACMA must exercise its powers under section 455 in a\nmanner consistent with any directions given by the ACCC under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(5) In exercising the power conferred by subsection (2), the ACCC\nmust have regard to whether portability of particular allocated\nnumbers is required in order to promote the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by means of\ncarriage services.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a particular\nthing promotes the long-term interests of end-users of carriage\nservices or of services supplied by means of carriage services is to\nbe determined in the same manner as that question is determined\nfor the purposes of Part XIC of the Competition and Consumer Act\n2010."
    },
