      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-459a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "459A Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-459a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.383",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate any or all of the powers\nconferred on the ACMA by the numbering plan to a body\ncorporate.\n\n(2) If, under section 50 of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005, the ACMA has delegated a power referred to\nin subsection (1) to a Division of the ACMA:\n\n(a) the Division may delegate the power to a body corporate; and\n\n(b) subsections 52(2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005 have effect",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate any or all of the powers\nconferred on the ACMA by the numbering plan to a body\ncorporate.\n\n(2) If, under section 50 of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005, the ACMA has delegated a power referred to\nin subsection (1) to a Division of the ACMA:\n\n(a) the Division may delegate the power to a body corporate; and\n\n(b) subsections 52(2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005 have effect",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-459a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-459a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b5f0b7ed640a7031191293c064e8cfb1f833e7c6ef12aca54a6d30acd7a2d6ee"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-459a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "459A Delegation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 383,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate any or all of the powers\nconferred on the ACMA by the numbering plan to a body\ncorporate.\n\n(2) If, under section 50 of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005, the ACMA has delegated a power referred to\nin subsection (1) to a Division of the ACMA:\n\n(a) the Division may delegate the power to a body corporate; and\n\n(b) subsections 52(2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005 have effect"
    },
