      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.383",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If, under section 50 of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005, the ACMA has delegated a power referred to\nin subsection (1) to a Division of the ACMA:\n\n(a) the Division may delegate the power to a body corporate; and\n\n(b) subsections 52(2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005 have effect",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If, under section 50 of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005, the ACMA has delegated a power referred to\nin subsection (1) to a Division of the ACMA:\n\n(a) the Division may delegate the power to a body corporate; and\n\n(b) subsections 52(2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005 have effect",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-459a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-459a-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2dbb5b67988a752025161e8a9e87824d8554cadf65dde21307779533e7bc9ce",
      "skos:note": "Delegation of power to a Division of the ACMA"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-459a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "459A(2) Delegation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 383,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If, under section 50 of the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority Act 2005, the ACMA has delegated a power referred to\nin subsection (1) to a Division of the ACMA:\n\n(a) the Division may delegate the power to a body corporate; and\n\n(b) subsections 52(2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005 have effect"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-459a-ss-2-norm",
