    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-460",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "460 Consultation about numbering plan",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-460"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.384",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making a numbering plan, the ACMA must publish on its\nwebsite a notice:\n\n(a) stating that the ACMA has prepared a draft of the plan; and\n\n(b) setting out the draft; and\n\n(c) inviting interested persons to give written comments about\nthe draft to the ACMA within 90 days after the publication of\nthe notice.\n\n(2) If interested persons have given comments about the draft in\naccordance with the notice, the ACMA must have due regard to\nthose comments in making the plan.\n\n(3) If the ACMA is of the opinion:\n\n(a) that a variation of a numbering plan:\n\n(i) will affect a number issued to a customer of a carriage\nservice provider; and\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 461\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) is not a variation that, under a written declaration made\nby the ACMA under this subparagraph, is taken to be a\nminor variation; or\n\n(b) that it is in the public interest that the public should be\nconsulted about a variation of a numbering plan;\nthe ACMA must publish on its website a notice:\n\n(c) stating that the ACMA has prepared a draft of the variation;\nand\n\n(d) setting out the draft; and\n\n(e) inviting interested persons to give written comments about\nthe draft to the ACMA within 30 days after the publication of\nthe notice.\n\n(4) If interested persons have given comments about the draft in\naccordance with the notice, the ACMA must have due regard to\nthose comments in varying the plan.\n\n(4A) A declaration under subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before making a numbering plan, the ACMA must publish on its\nwebsite a notice:\n\n(a) stating that the ACMA has prepared a draft of the plan; and\n\n(b) setting out the draft; and\n\n(c) inviting interested persons to give written comments about\nthe draft to the ACMA within 90 days after the publication of\nthe notice.\n\n(2) If interested persons have given comments about the draft in\naccordance with the notice, the ACMA must have due regard to\nthose comments in making the plan.\n\n(3) If the ACMA is of the opinion:\n\n(a) that a variation of a numbering plan:\n\n(i) will affect a number issued to a customer of a carriage\nservice provider; and\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 461\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) is not a variation that, under a written declaration made\nby the ACMA under this subparagraph, is taken to be a\nminor variation; or\n\n(b) that it is in the public interest that the public should be\nconsulted about a variation of a numbering plan;\nthe ACMA must publish on its website a notice:\n\n(c) stating that the ACMA has prepared a draft of the variation;\nand\n\n(d) setting out the draft; and\n\n(e) inviting interested persons to give written comments about\nthe draft to the ACMA within 30 days after the publication of\nthe notice.\n\n(4) If interested persons have given comments about the draft in\naccordance with the notice, the ACMA must have due regard to\nthose comments in varying the plan.\n\n(4A) A declaration under subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-460-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-460-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-460-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-460-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-460-ss-4a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "09d5fe7d6c14d015c59577264ab66c28c5e97b0549a050bd02749cf437691dad"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-460",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "460 Consultation about numbering plan",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 384,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before making a numbering plan, the ACMA must publish on its\nwebsite a notice:\n\n(a) stating that the ACMA has prepared a draft of the plan; and\n\n(b) setting out the draft; and\n\n(c) inviting interested persons to give written comments about\nthe draft to the ACMA within 90 days after the publication of\nthe notice.\n\n(2) If interested persons have given comments about the draft in\naccordance with the notice, the ACMA must have due regard to\nthose comments in making the plan.\n\n(3) If the ACMA is of the opinion:\n\n(a) that a variation of a numbering plan:\n\n(i) will affect a number issued to a customer of a carriage\nservice provider; and\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 461\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) is not a variation that, under a written declaration made\nby the ACMA under this subparagraph, is taken to be a\nminor variation; or\n\n(b) that it is in the public interest that the public should be\nconsulted about a variation of a numbering plan;\nthe ACMA must publish on its website a notice:\n\n(c) stating that the ACMA has prepared a draft of the variation;\nand\n\n(d) setting out the draft; and\n\n(e) inviting interested persons to give written comments about\nthe draft to the ACMA within 30 days after the publication of\nthe notice.\n\n(4) If interested persons have given comments about the draft in\naccordance with the notice, the ACMA must have due regard to\nthose comments in varying the plan.\n\n(4A) A declaration under subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) is a legislative\ninstrument."
    },
