    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-465",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "465 Register of allocated numbers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-465"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.389",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the designated authority is:\n\n(a) the ACMA; or\n\n(aa) if there is a numbering scheme manager—the numbering\nscheme manager; or\n\n(b) if the ACMA enters into an arrangement with another person\nunder which the other person agrees to perform the functions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the designated authority is:\n\n(a) the ACMA; or\n\n(aa) if there is a numbering scheme manager—the numbering\nscheme manager; or\n\n(b) if the ACMA enters into an arrangement with another person\nunder which the other person agrees to perform the functions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-465-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf244f88396fe6b9d1b46ee6f97d98ce81647dc81e02be8f1404061d763e6c57",
      "skos:note": "Designated authority for purposes of section"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-465",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "465 Register of allocated numbers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 389,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this section, the designated authority is:\n\n(a) the ACMA; or\n\n(aa) if there is a numbering scheme manager—the numbering\nscheme manager; or\n\n(b) if the ACMA enters into an arrangement with another person\nunder which the other person agrees to perform the functions"
    },
