    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-466",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "466 Emergency service numbers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-466"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.391",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The object of this section is to identify numbers for the purpose of\ncalling an emergency call service in connection with emergencies\nthat are likely to require the provision of assistance by any or all of\nthe following services (each an emergency service):\n\n(a) a police force or service;\n\n(b) a fire service;\n\n(c) an ambulance service;\n\n(d) if there is a numbering scheme manager—a service specified\nby the ACMA for the purposes of this paragraph in a\nlegislative instrument;\n\n(e) if there is no numbering scheme manager—a service\nspecified for the purposes of this paragraph in the numbering\nplan made by the ACMA.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, an emergency service number is a\nnumber specified for the purposes of this section in:\n\n(a) if there is a numbering scheme manager—a legislative\ninstrument made by the ACMA; or\n\n(b) if there is no numbering scheme manager—the numbering\nplan made by the ACMA.\n\n(3) Different emergency service numbers may be specified for use in\ndifferent areas.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The object of this section is to identify numbers for the purpose of\ncalling an emergency call service in connection with emergencies\nthat are likely to require the provision of assistance by any or all of\nthe following services (each an emergency service):\n\n(a) a police force or service;\n\n(b) a fire service;\n\n(c) an ambulance service;\n\n(d) if there is a numbering scheme manager—a service specified\nby the ACMA for the purposes of this paragraph in a\nlegislative instrument;\n\n(e) if there is no numbering scheme manager—a service\nspecified for the purposes of this paragraph in the numbering\nplan made by the ACMA.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, an emergency service number is a\nnumber specified for the purposes of this section in:\n\n(a) if there is a numbering scheme manager—a legislative\ninstrument made by the ACMA; or\n\n(b) if there is no numbering scheme manager—the numbering\nplan made by the ACMA.\n\n(3) Different emergency service numbers may be specified for use in\ndifferent areas.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-466-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-466-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-466-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a3abe63dd9437a0571cf5cdbb116f8ffeff242cf38d394ecee9aa9e96769b7e2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-466",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "466 Emergency service numbers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 391,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The object of this section is to identify numbers for the purpose of\ncalling an emergency call service in connection with emergencies\nthat are likely to require the provision of assistance by any or all of\nthe following services (each an emergency service):\n\n(a) a police force or service;\n\n(b) a fire service;\n\n(c) an ambulance service;\n\n(d) if there is a numbering scheme manager—a service specified\nby the ACMA for the purposes of this paragraph in a\nlegislative instrument;\n\n(e) if there is no numbering scheme manager—a service\nspecified for the purposes of this paragraph in the numbering\nplan made by the ACMA.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, an emergency service number is a\nnumber specified for the purposes of this section in:\n\n(a) if there is a numbering scheme manager—a legislative\ninstrument made by the ACMA; or\n\n(b) if there is no numbering scheme manager—the numbering\nplan made by the ACMA.\n\n(3) Different emergency service numbers may be specified for use in\ndifferent areas."
    },
