    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-468-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "468(4) Collection of numbering charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-468-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.392",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The ACMA may, by written instrument, determine that, if any\nannual charge payable by a person remains unpaid after the time\nwhen it became due for payment, the person is liable to pay to the\nCommonwealth, by way of penalty, an amount calculated at the\nrate of:\n\n(a) 20% per annum; or\n\n(b) if the determination specifies a lower percentage—that lower\npercentage per annum;\non the amount unpaid, computed from that time.\nDetermination has effect",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The ACMA may, by written instrument, determine that, if any\nannual charge payable by a person remains unpaid after the time\nwhen it became due for payment, the person is liable to pay to the\nCommonwealth, by way of penalty, an amount calculated at the\nrate of:\n\n(a) 20% per annum; or\n\n(b) if the determination specifies a lower percentage—that lower\npercentage per annum;\non the amount unpaid, computed from that time.\nDetermination has effect",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-468"
      },
