    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-471-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "471(2) Commonwealth not liable to charge",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-471-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.394",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Even though the Commonwealth is not liable to pay charge\nimposed by Division 1 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 472\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(Numbering Charges) Act 1997, it is the intention of the Parliament\nthat the following should be notionally liable for such a charge:\n\n(a) a Department of State;\n\n(b) a Department of the Parliament established under the\nParliamentary Service Act 1999;\n\n(c) a branch or part of the Australian Public Service in relation to\nwhich a person has, under an Act, the powers of, or\nexercisable by, the Secretary of a Department of the\nAustralian Public Service;\n\n(d) an authority of the Commonwealth that cannot, by a law of\nthe Commonwealth, be made liable to taxation by the\nCommonwealth.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Even though the Commonwealth is not liable to pay charge\nimposed by Division 1 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 472\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(Numbering Charges) Act 1997, it is the intention of the Parliament\nthat the following should be notionally liable for such a charge:\n\n(a) a Department of State;\n\n(b) a Department of the Parliament established under the\nParliamentary Service Act 1999;\n\n(c) a branch or part of the Australian Public Service in relation to\nwhich a person has, under an Act, the powers of, or\nexercisable by, the Secretary of a Department of the\nAustralian Public Service;\n\n(d) an authority of the Commonwealth that cannot, by a law of\nthe Commonwealth, be made liable to taxation by the\nCommonwealth.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-471"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-471-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-471-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5d16ce4db26143252877c91c690fd95b1678f3518e6e80eb253650a440b3194",
      "skos:note": "Notionally liable for charge"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-471-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "471(2) Commonwealth not liable to charge",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 394,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Even though the Commonwealth is not liable to pay charge\nimposed by Division 1 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nNumbering of carriage services  Division 2\n\nSection 472\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(Numbering Charges) Act 1997, it is the intention of the Parliament\nthat the following should be notionally liable for such a charge:\n\n(a) a Department of State;\n\n(b) a Department of the Parliament established under the\nParliamentary Service Act 1999;\n\n(c) a branch or part of the Australian Public Service in relation to\nwhich a person has, under an Act, the powers of, or\nexercisable by, the Secretary of a Department of the\nAustralian Public Service;\n\n(d) an authority of the Commonwealth that cannot, by a law of\nthe Commonwealth, be made liable to taxation by the\nCommonwealth."
    },
