    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-473",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "473 Letters and symbols taken to be numbers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-473"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.396",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Division, a letter or a symbol is taken to be\na number.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nRegulation of electronic addressing  Division 3\n\nSection 474\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Division, a letter or a symbol is taken to be\na number.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nRegulation of electronic addressing  Division 3\n\nSection 474\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-473-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "69b17bb9ebf898f9b89b776e149b7540500a6e28e88f843a1c97b6c4790fee6c",
      "skos:note": "A letter or symbol is taken to be a number."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-473",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "473 Letters and symbols taken to be numbers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 396,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Division, a letter or a symbol is taken to be\na number.\n\n\nNumbering of carriage services and regulation of electronic addressing  Part 22\nRegulation of electronic addressing  Division 3\n\nSection 474\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-473-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-473"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "474 Declared manager of electronic addressing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-474"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.397",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, determine that, for the\npurposes of this Division, a specified person or association is a\ndeclared manager of electronic addressing in relation to a\nspecified kind of electronic addressing and a specified kind of\nlisted carriage service.\n\n(2) The determination has effect accordingly.\n\n(3) The ACMA must not make a determination under subsection (1) in\nrelation to a particular person or association unless:\n\n(a) the ACMA is directed to do so by the ACCC under\nsubsection (4); or\n\n(b) the ACMA considers that the person or association is not\nmanaging that kind of electronic addressing to the ACMA’s\nsatisfaction.\n\n(4) The ACCC may give written directions to the ACMA in relation to\nthe exercise of the power conferred by subsection (1).\n\n(5) The ACMA must exercise its powers under subsection (1) in a\nmanner consistent with directions given by the ACCC under\nsubsection (4).\n\n(6) The ACCC must not give a direction under subsection (4) unless,\nin the ACCC’s opinion, compliance with the direction is likely to\nhave a bearing on competition or consumer protection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, determine that, for the\npurposes of this Division, a specified person or association is a\ndeclared manager of electronic addressing in relation to a\nspecified kind of electronic addressing and a specified kind of\nlisted carriage service.\n\n(2) The determination has effect accordingly.\n\n(3) The ACMA must not make a determination under subsection (1) in\nrelation to a particular person or association unless:\n\n(a) the ACMA is directed to do so by the ACCC under\nsubsection (4); or\n\n(b) the ACMA considers that the person or association is not\nmanaging that kind of electronic addressing to the ACMA’s\nsatisfaction.\n\n(4) The ACCC may give written directions to the ACMA in relation to\nthe exercise of the power conferred by subsection (1).\n\n(5) The ACMA must exercise its powers under subsection (1) in a\nmanner consistent with directions given by the ACCC under\nsubsection (4).\n\n(6) The ACCC must not give a direction under subsection (4) unless,\nin the ACCC’s opinion, compliance with the direction is likely to\nhave a bearing on competition or consumer protection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-474-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b96f99bbe4695dfcae367b72e1e61c1d6ec5f17de45a223f882d013321e0d05b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-474",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "474 Declared manager of electronic addressing",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 397,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, determine that, for the\npurposes of this Division, a specified person or association is a\ndeclared manager of electronic addressing in relation to a\nspecified kind of electronic addressing and a specified kind of\nlisted carriage service.\n\n(2) The determination has effect accordingly.\n\n(3) The ACMA must not make a determination under subsection (1) in\nrelation to a particular person or association unless:\n\n(a) the ACMA is directed to do so by the ACCC under\nsubsection (4); or\n\n(b) the ACMA considers that the person or association is not\nmanaging that kind of electronic addressing to the ACMA’s\nsatisfaction.\n\n(4) The ACCC may give written directions to the ACMA in relation to\nthe exercise of the power conferred by subsection (1).\n\n(5) The ACMA must exercise its powers under subsection (1) in a\nmanner consistent with directions given by the ACCC under\nsubsection (4).\n\n(6) The ACCC must not give a direction under subsection (4) unless,\nin the ACCC’s opinion, compliance with the direction is likely to\nhave a bearing on competition or consumer protection."
    },
