    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "484C Definition of sender identification",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.406",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A sender identification is one or more of the things covered by\nsubsection (2) that is a message header that is, or is to be, used in a\ncommunication that is, or is to be, sent using any of the following\nservices:\n\n(a) a short message service;\n\n(b) a multimedia message service;\n\n(c) if another service is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (4)—that other service.\n\n(2) This subsection covers the following things:\n\n(a) letters;\n\n(b) numbers;\n\n(c) symbols;\n\n\nSMS Sender ID Register  Part 24B\n\nSection 484D\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) if another thing is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (5)—that other thing.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), a message header is not a sender\nidentification if the message header consists only of numbers.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a service for\nthe purposes of paragraph (1)(c).\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a thing for the\npurposes of paragraph (2)(d).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A sender identification is one or more of the things covered by\nsubsection (2) that is a message header that is, or is to be, used in a\ncommunication that is, or is to be, sent using any of the following\nservices:\n\n(a) a short message service;\n\n(b) a multimedia message service;\n\n(c) if another service is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (4)—that other service.\n\n(2) This subsection covers the following things:\n\n(a) letters;\n\n(b) numbers;\n\n(c) symbols;\n\n\nSMS Sender ID Register  Part 24B\n\nSection 484D\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) if another thing is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (5)—that other thing.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), a message header is not a sender\nidentification if the message header consists only of numbers.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a service for\nthe purposes of paragraph (1)(c).\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a thing for the\npurposes of paragraph (2)(d).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484c-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484c-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484c-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fa54b035d1e80f4868fa6880e00ca09a924d48ff0ef593fe7b90e63018eea5cb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "484C Definition of sender identification",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 406,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A sender identification is one or more of the things covered by\nsubsection (2) that is a message header that is, or is to be, used in a\ncommunication that is, or is to be, sent using any of the following\nservices:\n\n(a) a short message service;\n\n(b) a multimedia message service;\n\n(c) if another service is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (4)—that other service.\n\n(2) This subsection covers the following things:\n\n(a) letters;\n\n(b) numbers;\n\n(c) symbols;\n\n\nSMS Sender ID Register  Part 24B\n\nSection 484D\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) if another thing is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (5)—that other thing.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), a message header is not a sender\nidentification if the message header consists only of numbers.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a service for\nthe purposes of paragraph (1)(c).\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify a thing for the\npurposes of paragraph (2)(d)."
    },
