    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "484F Application for approval under this section",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.409",
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) An entity covered by subsection (2) may apply to the ACMA for\nan approval under this section.\n\n(2) This subsection covers the following entities:\n\n(a) an individual;\n\n(b) a body corporate;\n\n(c) a corporation sole;\n\n(d) a body politic;\n\n(e) a government entity (within the meaning of the A New Tax\nSystem (Australian Business Number) Act 1999);\n\n(f) a partnership;\n\n(g) any other unincorporated association or body of persons;\n\n(h) a trust;\n\n(i) a superannuation fund (within the meaning of the\nSuperannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993).\n\n(3) An application by an entity under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form approved under subsection (10); and\n\n(b) contain such information as the form requires; and",
      "skos:definition": "Application\n\n(1) An entity covered by subsection (2) may apply to the ACMA for\nan approval under this section.\n\n(2) This subsection covers the following entities:\n\n(a) an individual;\n\n(b) a body corporate;\n\n(c) a corporation sole;\n\n(d) a body politic;\n\n(e) a government entity (within the meaning of the A New Tax\nSystem (Australian Business Number) Act 1999);\n\n(f) a partnership;\n\n(g) any other unincorporated association or body of persons;\n\n(h) a trust;\n\n(i) a superannuation fund (within the meaning of the\nSuperannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993).\n\n(3) An application by an entity under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form approved under subsection (10); and\n\n(b) contain such information as the form requires; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7ad522ea327e5ba95534ef8355038ef7f7b86328c7cf9175886f60464c40d28"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "484F Application for approval under this section",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 409,
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) An entity covered by subsection (2) may apply to the ACMA for\nan approval under this section.\n\n(2) This subsection covers the following entities:\n\n(a) an individual;\n\n(b) a body corporate;\n\n(c) a corporation sole;\n\n(d) a body politic;\n\n(e) a government entity (within the meaning of the A New Tax\nSystem (Australian Business Number) Act 1999);\n\n(f) a partnership;\n\n(g) any other unincorporated association or body of persons;\n\n(h) a trust;\n\n(i) a superannuation fund (within the meaning of the\nSuperannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993).\n\n(3) An application by an entity under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) be made in the form approved under subsection (10); and\n\n(b) contain such information as the form requires; and"
    },
