    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "484H Removal of entries from the SMS Sender ID Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.413",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may remove an entry from the SMS Sender ID\nRegister if the ACMA is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the sender identification covered by the entry is offensive or\nmisleading or deceptive; or\n\n(b) the sender identification covered by the entry is a spoofing\nsender identification; or\n\n(c) it would be appropriate in all the circumstances to remove the\nentry.\n\n(2) The ACMA is not required to observe any requirements of the\nnatural justice hearing rule in exercising the power under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not limit a determination made under\nsubsection 484L(4) about the matter mentioned in\nparagraph 484L(4)(c).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may remove an entry from the SMS Sender ID\nRegister if the ACMA is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the sender identification covered by the entry is offensive or\nmisleading or deceptive; or\n\n(b) the sender identification covered by the entry is a spoofing\nsender identification; or\n\n(c) it would be appropriate in all the circumstances to remove the\nentry.\n\n(2) The ACMA is not required to observe any requirements of the\nnatural justice hearing rule in exercising the power under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not limit a determination made under\nsubsection 484L(4) about the matter mentioned in\nparagraph 484L(4)(c).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2853f39de275480c5fcd3ad63117a6f30ce1419da417092531a935d94ba91ba8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "484H Removal of entries from the SMS Sender ID Register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 413,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may remove an entry from the SMS Sender ID\nRegister if the ACMA is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the sender identification covered by the entry is offensive or\nmisleading or deceptive; or\n\n(b) the sender identification covered by the entry is a spoofing\nsender identification; or\n\n(c) it would be appropriate in all the circumstances to remove the\nentry.\n\n(2) The ACMA is not required to observe any requirements of the\nnatural justice hearing rule in exercising the power under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not limit a determination made under\nsubsection 484L(4) about the matter mentioned in\nparagraph 484L(4)(c)."
    },
