      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Administrative action taken by computer program",
      "cml:conclusionText": "ACMA's administrative action"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "484J(4) Automation of administrative action",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484j-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.414",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The ACMA may make a decision in substitution for a decision the\nACMA is treated as having taken under subsection (3) if:\n\n(a) in any case—the ACMA is satisfied that the decision taken\nby the operation of the computer program is not correct; or\n\n(b) if the decision taken by the operation of the computer\nprogram is a decision under subsection 484G(4) to accept\none or more sender identifications—the ACMA is satisfied\nthat one or more of those sender identifications are spoofing\nsender identifications.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The ACMA may make a decision in substitution for a decision the\nACMA is treated as having taken under subsection (3) if:\n\n(a) in any case—the ACMA is satisfied that the decision taken\nby the operation of the computer program is not correct; or\n\n(b) if the decision taken by the operation of the computer\nprogram is a decision under subsection 484G(4) to accept\none or more sender identifications—the ACMA is satisfied\nthat one or more of those sender identifications are spoofing\nsender identifications.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2cc8d52f07a40736a3af1ad4906a2918e978931c28bd9bc16c172ebd3b97464a",
      "skos:note": "ACMA may make a decision in substitution for an incorrect computer program decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484j-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "484J(4) Automation of administrative action",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 414,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The ACMA may make a decision in substitution for a decision the\nACMA is treated as having taken under subsection (3) if:\n\n(a) in any case—the ACMA is satisfied that the decision taken\nby the operation of the computer program is not correct; or\n\n(b) if the decision taken by the operation of the computer\nprogram is a decision under subsection 484G(4) to accept\none or more sender identifications—the ACMA is satisfied\nthat one or more of those sender identifications are spoofing\nsender identifications."
    },
