    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "484M Application of the Privacy Act 1988 to a contracted service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.418",
      "values:originalText": "provider\n\n(1) For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, if the SMS Sender ID\nRegister is established, or maintained (in whole or in part), by a\ncontracted service provider under a contract:\n\n(a) the establishing, or maintaining, of the SMS Sender ID\nRegister by the contracted service provider; and\n\n(b) the operation of the SMS Sender ID Register by the\ncontracted service provider; and\n\n(c) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, by\nthe contracted service provider under:\n\n(i) this Part; or\n\n(ii) a determination under this Part;\nis taken to be the provision of a service to the ACMA under the\ncontract.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is enacted for the avoidance of doubt.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nSimplified outline  Division 1\n\nSection 485\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "provider\n\n(1) For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, if the SMS Sender ID\nRegister is established, or maintained (in whole or in part), by a\ncontracted service provider under a contract:\n\n(a) the establishing, or maintaining, of the SMS Sender ID\nRegister by the contracted service provider; and\n\n(b) the operation of the SMS Sender ID Register by the\ncontracted service provider; and\n\n(c) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, by\nthe contracted service provider under:\n\n(i) this Part; or\n\n(ii) a determination under this Part;\nis taken to be the provision of a service to the ACMA under the\ncontract.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is enacted for the avoidance of doubt.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nSimplified outline  Division 1\n\nSection 485\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5c4c1964340aca5b65393bbe9d3249cdd71be26665b3320ad694f034f2743283"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "484M Application of the Privacy Act 1988 to a contracted service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 418,
      "values:originalText": "provider\n\n(1) For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, if the SMS Sender ID\nRegister is established, or maintained (in whole or in part), by a\ncontracted service provider under a contract:\n\n(a) the establishing, or maintaining, of the SMS Sender ID\nRegister by the contracted service provider; and\n\n(b) the operation of the SMS Sender ID Register by the\ncontracted service provider; and\n\n(c) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, by\nthe contracted service provider under:\n\n(i) this Part; or\n\n(ii) a determination under this Part;\nis taken to be the provision of a service to the ACMA under the\ncontract.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is enacted for the avoidance of doubt.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nSimplified outline  Division 1\n\nSection 485\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "484M(1) Application of the Privacy Act 1988 to a contracted service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484m-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.418",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, if the SMS Sender ID\nRegister is established, or maintained (in whole or in part), by a\ncontracted service provider under a contract:\n\n(a) the establishing, or maintaining, of the SMS Sender ID\nRegister by the contracted service provider; and\n\n(b) the operation of the SMS Sender ID Register by the\ncontracted service provider; and\n\n(c) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, by\nthe contracted service provider under:\n\n(i) this Part; or\n\n(ii) a determination under this Part;\nis taken to be the provision of a service to the ACMA under the\ncontract.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, if the SMS Sender ID\nRegister is established, or maintained (in whole or in part), by a\ncontracted service provider under a contract:\n\n(a) the establishing, or maintaining, of the SMS Sender ID\nRegister by the contracted service provider; and\n\n(b) the operation of the SMS Sender ID Register by the\ncontracted service provider; and\n\n(c) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, by\nthe contracted service provider under:\n\n(i) this Part; or\n\n(ii) a determination under this Part;\nis taken to be the provision of a service to the ACMA under the\ncontract.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484m-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8e11ac61d244a4dd44d062f109d6a5d88e4d3be1b6411f97b0ad9b6bdd98ca3",
      "skos:note": "Contracted service provider must provide a service to ACMA under the contract.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-484m-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "484M(1) Application of the Privacy Act 1988 to a contracted service",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 418,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, if the SMS Sender ID\nRegister is established, or maintained (in whole or in part), by a\ncontracted service provider under a contract:\n\n(a) the establishing, or maintaining, of the SMS Sender ID\nRegister by the contracted service provider; and\n\n(b) the operation of the SMS Sender ID Register by the\ncontracted service provider; and\n\n(c) the performance of a function, or the exercise of a power, by\nthe contracted service provider under:\n\n(i) this Part; or\n\n(ii) a determination under this Part;\nis taken to be the provision of a service to the ACMA under the\ncontract."
    },
