    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-488",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "488 Informing the public about an inquiry",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-488"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.421",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACMA holds a public inquiry, it must publish, in whatever\nways it thinks appropriate, notice of:\n\n(a) the fact that it is holding the inquiry; and\n\n(b) the period during which the inquiry is to be held; and\n\n(c) the nature of the matter to which the inquiry relates; and\n\n(d) the period within which, and the form in which, members of\nthe public may make submissions to the ACMA about that\nmatter; and\n\n(e) the matters that the ACMA would like such submissions to\ndeal with; and\n\n(f) the address or addresses to which submissions may be sent.\n\n(2) The ACMA need not publish at the same time or in the same way\nnotice of all the matters referred to in subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the ACMA holds a public inquiry, it must publish, in whatever\nways it thinks appropriate, notice of:\n\n(a) the fact that it is holding the inquiry; and\n\n(b) the period during which the inquiry is to be held; and\n\n(c) the nature of the matter to which the inquiry relates; and\n\n(d) the period within which, and the form in which, members of\nthe public may make submissions to the ACMA about that\nmatter; and\n\n(e) the matters that the ACMA would like such submissions to\ndeal with; and\n\n(f) the address or addresses to which submissions may be sent.\n\n(2) The ACMA need not publish at the same time or in the same way\nnotice of all the matters referred to in subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-488-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-488-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "265f93a592086af1563722ac2bcc0a52f77b5fbcfcc10bc4264dda38fe02ad8e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-488",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "488 Informing the public about an inquiry",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 421,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACMA holds a public inquiry, it must publish, in whatever\nways it thinks appropriate, notice of:\n\n(a) the fact that it is holding the inquiry; and\n\n(b) the period during which the inquiry is to be held; and\n\n(c) the nature of the matter to which the inquiry relates; and\n\n(d) the period within which, and the form in which, members of\nthe public may make submissions to the ACMA about that\nmatter; and\n\n(e) the matters that the ACMA would like such submissions to\ndeal with; and\n\n(f) the address or addresses to which submissions may be sent.\n\n(2) The ACMA need not publish at the same time or in the same way\nnotice of all the matters referred to in subsection (1)."
    },
