    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-489",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "489 Discussion paper",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-489"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.421",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACMA\nmay cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:\n\n(a) identifies the issues that, in the ACMA’s opinion, are\nrelevant to that matter; and\n\n(b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of,\nthose issues as the ACMA thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACMA must make copies of the discussion paper available at\neach of the ACMA’s offices. The ACMA may charge a reasonable\nprice for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance\nwith this subsection.\n\n(3) The ACMA may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including\nin electronic form. The ACMA may charge for supplying a\npublication under this subsection in accordance with a\ndetermination under section 60 of the Australian Communications\nand Media Authority Act 2005.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACMA\nmay cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:\n\n(a) identifies the issues that, in the ACMA’s opinion, are\nrelevant to that matter; and\n\n(b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of,\nthose issues as the ACMA thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACMA must make copies of the discussion paper available at\neach of the ACMA’s offices. The ACMA may charge a reasonable\nprice for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance\nwith this subsection.\n\n(3) The ACMA may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including\nin electronic form. The ACMA may charge for supplying a\npublication under this subsection in accordance with a\ndetermination under section 60 of the Australian Communications\nand Media Authority Act 2005.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-489-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-489-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-489-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ad42c6e886cd5c488c269d55f9a436ee769274a8a88bf92d31cb754dabd417ab"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-489",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "489 Discussion paper",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 421,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACMA\nmay cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:\n\n(a) identifies the issues that, in the ACMA’s opinion, are\nrelevant to that matter; and\n\n(b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of,\nthose issues as the ACMA thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACMA must make copies of the discussion paper available at\neach of the ACMA’s offices. The ACMA may charge a reasonable\nprice for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance\nwith this subsection.\n\n(3) The ACMA may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including\nin electronic form. The ACMA may charge for supplying a\npublication under this subsection in accordance with a\ndetermination under section 60 of the Australian Communications\nand Media Authority Act 2005."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-489-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "489(1) Discussion paper",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
