    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-490",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "490 Written submissions and protection from civil actions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-490"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.422",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA must provide a reasonable opportunity for any\nmember of the public to make a written submission to the ACMA\nabout the matter to which a public inquiry relates.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ACMA is taken not to have\nprovided a reasonable opportunity to make submissions unless\nthere was a period of at least 28 days during which the submissions\ncould be made.\n\n(3) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss,\ndamage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because\nof the making in good faith of a statement, or the giving in good\nfaith of a document or information, to the ACMA in connection\nwith a public inquiry under this Division.\n\n(4) The rule in subsection (3) applies whether or not the statement is\nmade, or the document or information is given, in connection with\na written submission or a public hearing.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA must provide a reasonable opportunity for any\nmember of the public to make a written submission to the ACMA\nabout the matter to which a public inquiry relates.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ACMA is taken not to have\nprovided a reasonable opportunity to make submissions unless\nthere was a period of at least 28 days during which the submissions\ncould be made.\n\n(3) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss,\ndamage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because\nof the making in good faith of a statement, or the giving in good\nfaith of a document or information, to the ACMA in connection\nwith a public inquiry under this Division.\n\n(4) The rule in subsection (3) applies whether or not the statement is\nmade, or the document or information is given, in connection with\na written submission or a public hearing.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-490-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-490-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-490-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-490-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5bcebb7169184360f7a1b49a5b38b1dc56dc644ba50d9e104d49fe728e691350"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-490",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "490 Written submissions and protection from civil actions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 422,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA must provide a reasonable opportunity for any\nmember of the public to make a written submission to the ACMA\nabout the matter to which a public inquiry relates.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ACMA is taken not to have\nprovided a reasonable opportunity to make submissions unless\nthere was a period of at least 28 days during which the submissions\ncould be made.\n\n(3) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss,\ndamage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because\nof the making in good faith of a statement, or the giving in good\nfaith of a document or information, to the ACMA in connection\nwith a public inquiry under this Division.\n\n(4) The rule in subsection (3) applies whether or not the statement is\nmade, or the document or information is given, in connection with\na written submission or a public hearing."
    },
