    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "491 Hearings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-491"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.422",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may hold hearings for the purposes of a public inquiry.\n\n(2) Hearings may be held, for example:\n\n(a) in order to receive submissions about the matter to which the\ninquiry relates; or\n\n(b) in order to provide a forum for public discussion of issues\nrelevant to that matter.\n\n(3) At a hearing, the ACMA may be constituted by:\n\n(a) a member or members determined in writing by the Chair for\nthe purposes of that hearing; or\n\n(b) if the functions or powers of the ACMA in relation to the\nhearing have been delegated to a person, or to a Division of\nthe ACMA, under section 50, 51 or 52 of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005—that person\nor Division.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACMA  Division 2\n\nSection 492\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The Chair is to preside at all hearings at which he or she is present.\n\n(5) If the Chair is not present at a hearing, the hearing is to be presided\nover by:\n\n(a) if paragraph (3)(a) applies—the member, specified in an\ninstrument under that paragraph, as the member who is to\npreside at the hearing; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (3)(b) applies and the delegation is to a person—\nthat person; or\n\n(c) if paragraph (3)(b) applies and the delegation is to a Division\nof the ACMA—a member of the Division chosen by the\nDivision.\n\n(6) The ACMA may regulate the conduct of proceedings at a hearing\nas it thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may hold hearings for the purposes of a public inquiry.\n\n(2) Hearings may be held, for example:\n\n(a) in order to receive submissions about the matter to which the\ninquiry relates; or\n\n(b) in order to provide a forum for public discussion of issues\nrelevant to that matter.\n\n(3) At a hearing, the ACMA may be constituted by:\n\n(a) a member or members determined in writing by the Chair for\nthe purposes of that hearing; or\n\n(b) if the functions or powers of the ACMA in relation to the\nhearing have been delegated to a person, or to a Division of\nthe ACMA, under section 50, 51 or 52 of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005—that person\nor Division.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACMA  Division 2\n\nSection 492\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The Chair is to preside at all hearings at which he or she is present.\n\n(5) If the Chair is not present at a hearing, the hearing is to be presided\nover by:\n\n(a) if paragraph (3)(a) applies—the member, specified in an\ninstrument under that paragraph, as the member who is to\npreside at the hearing; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (3)(b) applies and the delegation is to a person—\nthat person; or\n\n(c) if paragraph (3)(b) applies and the delegation is to a Division\nof the ACMA—a member of the Division chosen by the\nDivision.\n\n(6) The ACMA may regulate the conduct of proceedings at a hearing\nas it thinks appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-491-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ad742f130e2fbbfee11b3ff8d7a14052d352f525988b6f8bf7f167e3fbfabf1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-491",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "491 Hearings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 422,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may hold hearings for the purposes of a public inquiry.\n\n(2) Hearings may be held, for example:\n\n(a) in order to receive submissions about the matter to which the\ninquiry relates; or\n\n(b) in order to provide a forum for public discussion of issues\nrelevant to that matter.\n\n(3) At a hearing, the ACMA may be constituted by:\n\n(a) a member or members determined in writing by the Chair for\nthe purposes of that hearing; or\n\n(b) if the functions or powers of the ACMA in relation to the\nhearing have been delegated to a person, or to a Division of\nthe ACMA, under section 50, 51 or 52 of the Australian\nCommunications and Media Authority Act 2005—that person\nor Division.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACMA  Division 2\n\nSection 492\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The Chair is to preside at all hearings at which he or she is present.\n\n(5) If the Chair is not present at a hearing, the hearing is to be presided\nover by:\n\n(a) if paragraph (3)(a) applies—the member, specified in an\ninstrument under that paragraph, as the member who is to\npreside at the hearing; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (3)(b) applies and the delegation is to a person—\nthat person; or\n\n(c) if paragraph (3)(b) applies and the delegation is to a Division\nof the ACMA—a member of the Division chosen by the\nDivision.\n\n(6) The ACMA may regulate the conduct of proceedings at a hearing\nas it thinks appropriate."
    },
