      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) The basic rule is that the hearing must take place in public.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The AI system validates the hearing taking place in public."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-492-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "492(3) Hearing to be in public except in exceptional cases",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-492-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.423",
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, the hearing, or a part of the hearing, may be conducted\nin private if the ACMA is satisfied that:\n\n(a) evidence that may be given, or a matter that may arise, during\nthe hearing or a part of the hearing is of a confidential nature;\nor\n\n(b) hearing a matter, or part of a matter, in public would not be\nconducive to the due administration of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) However, the hearing, or a part of the hearing, may be conducted\nin private if the ACMA is satisfied that:\n\n(a) evidence that may be given, or a matter that may arise, during\nthe hearing or a part of the hearing is of a confidential nature;\nor\n\n(b) hearing a matter, or part of a matter, in public would not be\nconducive to the due administration of this Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-492"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-492-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-492-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fe891e488466cf53865a6b531b250ff23ce2e553e21277fdbaae67ea0adb827a",
      "skos:note": "Private hearing allowed under exceptional cases"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-492-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "492(3) Hearing to be in public except in exceptional cases",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 423,
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, the hearing, or a part of the hearing, may be conducted\nin private if the ACMA is satisfied that:\n\n(a) evidence that may be given, or a matter that may arise, during\nthe hearing or a part of the hearing is of a confidential nature;\nor\n\n(b) hearing a matter, or part of a matter, in public would not be\nconducive to the due administration of this Act."
    },
