    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "493 Confidential material not to be published",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-493"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.424",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in public;\nand\n\n(b) the ACMA is of the opinion that:\n\n(i) evidence or other material presented to the hearing; or\n\n(ii) material in a written submission lodged with the\nACMA;\n\nis of a confidential nature;\nthe ACMA may order that:\n\n(c) the evidence or material not be published; or\n\n(d) its disclosure be restricted.\n\n(3) A person must not fail to comply with an order under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has made an order under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: 50 penalty units.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(6) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACMA  Division 2\n\nSection 494\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in public;\nand\n\n(b) the ACMA is of the opinion that:\n\n(i) evidence or other material presented to the hearing; or\n\n(ii) material in a written submission lodged with the\nACMA;\n\nis of a confidential nature;\nthe ACMA may order that:\n\n(c) the evidence or material not be published; or\n\n(d) its disclosure be restricted.\n\n(3) A person must not fail to comply with an order under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has made an order under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: 50 penalty units.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(6) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACMA  Division 2\n\nSection 494\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) omit to perform an act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55db3750886cbfadc7637ecfae89e4592aac3ec087d521d21ad0fb450b19befe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-493",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "493 Confidential material not to be published",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 424,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in public;\nand\n\n(b) the ACMA is of the opinion that:\n\n(i) evidence or other material presented to the hearing; or\n\n(ii) material in a written submission lodged with the\nACMA;\n\nis of a confidential nature;\nthe ACMA may order that:\n\n(c) the evidence or material not be published; or\n\n(d) its disclosure be restricted.\n\n(3) A person must not fail to comply with an order under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has made an order under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order.\nPenalty: 50 penalty units.\n\n(5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(6) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:\n\n(a) do an act; or\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACMA  Division 2\n\nSection 494\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) omit to perform an act."
    },
    {
