    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "494 Direction about private hearings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-494"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.425",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.\n\n(2) If the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in private, the\nACMA:\n\n(a) must give directions as to the persons who may be present at\nthe hearing or the part of the hearing; and\n\n(b) may give directions restricting the disclosure of evidence or\nother material presented at the hearing or the part of the\nhearing.\n\n(3) A person must not fail to comply with a direction under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a direction under paragraph (2)(a); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the direction.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a direction under paragraph (2)(b); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the direction.\nPenalty: 50 penalty units.\n\n(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (6) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(7) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.\n\n(2) If the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in private, the\nACMA:\n\n(a) must give directions as to the persons who may be present at\nthe hearing or the part of the hearing; and\n\n(b) may give directions restricting the disclosure of evidence or\nother material presented at the hearing or the part of the\nhearing.\n\n(3) A person must not fail to comply with a direction under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a direction under paragraph (2)(a); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the direction.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a direction under paragraph (2)(b); and\n\n(b) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the person’s conduct contravenes the direction.\nPenalty: 50 penalty units.\n\n(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (6) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(7) In this section:\nengage in conduct means:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494-ss-2"
