      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.425",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (6) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (6) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-494-ss-6-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f3ed3a9ea1bd1db30757ce4f07c992886dc518e651063926ba139ac8c2dd406b",
      "skos:note": "Defendant bears evidential burden for reasonable excuse"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-494-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "494(6) Direction about private hearings",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 425,
      "values:originalText": "(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (6) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
