    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-495",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "495 Reports on inquiries",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-495"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.426",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACMA holds a public inquiry, the ACMA must prepare a\nreport setting out its findings as a result of the inquiry.\n\n(2) If the inquiry was held because of a direction given by the Minister\nunder section 486, the ACMA must give a copy of the report to the\nMinister.\n\n(3) If the inquiry was held otherwise than because of a direction given\nby the Minister under section 486, the ACMA must publish the\nreport.\n\n(4) The ACMA is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 493\nor 494.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 496\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the ACMA holds a public inquiry, the ACMA must prepare a\nreport setting out its findings as a result of the inquiry.\n\n(2) If the inquiry was held because of a direction given by the Minister\nunder section 486, the ACMA must give a copy of the report to the\nMinister.\n\n(3) If the inquiry was held otherwise than because of a direction given\nby the Minister under section 486, the ACMA must publish the\nreport.\n\n(4) The ACMA is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 493\nor 494.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 496\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-495-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-495-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-495-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-495-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1058c851704354ac65deddfe4c0abc7cc55360bfe84b1a505b59e7c846049d86"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-495",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "495 Reports on inquiries",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 426,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACMA holds a public inquiry, the ACMA must prepare a\nreport setting out its findings as a result of the inquiry.\n\n(2) If the inquiry was held because of a direction given by the Minister\nunder section 486, the ACMA must give a copy of the report to the\nMinister.\n\n(3) If the inquiry was held otherwise than because of a direction given\nby the Minister under section 486, the ACMA must publish the\nreport.\n\n(4) The ACMA is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 493\nor 494.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 496\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
