        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-495-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "09c90930a78f4e5dfaceabcd288c1dd110f2d8be544a2623ed6991aebc6d5b23",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from reporting confidential material"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-495-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "495(4) Reports on inquiries",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 426,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The ACMA is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 493\nor 494.\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 496\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
