    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "499 Discussion paper",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-499"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.428",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACCC\nmay cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:\n\n(a) identifies the issues that, in the ACCC’s opinion, are relevant\nto that matter; and\n\n(b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of,\nthose issues as the ACCC thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACCC must make copies of the discussion paper available at\neach of the ACCC offices. The ACCC may charge a reasonable\nprice for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance\nwith this subsection.\n\n(3) The ACCC may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including\nin electronic form. The ACCC may charge a fee for supplying a\npublication under this subsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACCC\nmay cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:\n\n(a) identifies the issues that, in the ACCC’s opinion, are relevant\nto that matter; and\n\n(b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of,\nthose issues as the ACCC thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACCC must make copies of the discussion paper available at\neach of the ACCC offices. The ACCC may charge a reasonable\nprice for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance\nwith this subsection.\n\n(3) The ACCC may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including\nin electronic form. The ACCC may charge a fee for supplying a\npublication under this subsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b0b85418a3640c59460df8ded5115629c2ce32b25a24f5d9da258e751fde4733"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-499",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "499 Discussion paper",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 428,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACCC\nmay cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:\n\n(a) identifies the issues that, in the ACCC’s opinion, are relevant\nto that matter; and\n\n(b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of,\nthose issues as the ACCC thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACCC must make copies of the discussion paper available at\neach of the ACCC offices. The ACCC may charge a reasonable\nprice for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance\nwith this subsection.\n\n(3) The ACCC may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including\nin electronic form. The ACCC may charge a fee for supplying a\npublication under this subsection."
    },
