    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "501 Hearings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-501"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.429",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may hold hearings for the purposes of a public inquiry.\n\n(2) Hearings may be held, for example:\n\n(a) in order to receive submissions about the matter to which the\ninquiry relates; or\n\n(b) in order to provide a forum for public discussion of issues\nrelevant to that matter.\n\n(3) At a hearing, the ACCC may be constituted by a member or\nmembers determined in writing by the Chairperson for the\npurposes of that hearing.\n\n(4) The Chairperson is to preside at all hearings at which he or she is\npresent.\n\n(5) If the Chairperson is not present at a hearing, the member\nspecified, in an instrument under subsection (3), as the member\nwho is to preside at the hearing is to preside.\n\n(6) The ACCC may regulate the conduct of proceedings at a hearing as\nit thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACCC may hold hearings for the purposes of a public inquiry.\n\n(2) Hearings may be held, for example:\n\n(a) in order to receive submissions about the matter to which the\ninquiry relates; or\n\n(b) in order to provide a forum for public discussion of issues\nrelevant to that matter.\n\n(3) At a hearing, the ACCC may be constituted by a member or\nmembers determined in writing by the Chairperson for the\npurposes of that hearing.\n\n(4) The Chairperson is to preside at all hearings at which he or she is\npresent.\n\n(5) If the Chairperson is not present at a hearing, the member\nspecified, in an instrument under subsection (3), as the member\nwho is to preside at the hearing is to preside.\n\n(6) The ACCC may regulate the conduct of proceedings at a hearing as\nit thinks appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-501-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2615471b60579bc7024cb145c36189c74af2de8ae9052dedaca3ad1eb89d8514"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-501",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "501 Hearings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 429,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may hold hearings for the purposes of a public inquiry.\n\n(2) Hearings may be held, for example:\n\n(a) in order to receive submissions about the matter to which the\ninquiry relates; or\n\n(b) in order to provide a forum for public discussion of issues\nrelevant to that matter.\n\n(3) At a hearing, the ACCC may be constituted by a member or\nmembers determined in writing by the Chairperson for the\npurposes of that hearing.\n\n(4) The Chairperson is to preside at all hearings at which he or she is\npresent.\n\n(5) If the Chairperson is not present at a hearing, the member\nspecified, in an instrument under subsection (3), as the member\nwho is to preside at the hearing is to preside.\n\n(6) The ACCC may regulate the conduct of proceedings at a hearing as\nit thinks appropriate."
    },
