    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-505",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "505 Reports on inquiries",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-505"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.432",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACCC holds a public inquiry, the ACCC must prepare a\nreport setting out its findings as a result of the inquiry.\n\n(2) If the inquiry was held because of a direction given by the Minister\nunder section 496, the ACCC must give a copy of the report to the\nMinister.\n\n(3) If the inquiry was held otherwise than because of a direction given\nby the Minister under section 496, the ACCC must publish the\nreport.\n\n(4) The ACCC is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 505A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 503\nor 504.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the ACCC holds a public inquiry, the ACCC must prepare a\nreport setting out its findings as a result of the inquiry.\n\n(2) If the inquiry was held because of a direction given by the Minister\nunder section 496, the ACCC must give a copy of the report to the\nMinister.\n\n(3) If the inquiry was held otherwise than because of a direction given\nby the Minister under section 496, the ACCC must publish the\nreport.\n\n(4) The ACCC is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 505A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 503\nor 504.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-505-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-505-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-505-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-505-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02405c45fb6729e6f7a8b4aa5c1bebd86db3493b1f1cf665f2b96f336b51a5f9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-505",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "505 Reports on inquiries",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 432,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACCC holds a public inquiry, the ACCC must prepare a\nreport setting out its findings as a result of the inquiry.\n\n(2) If the inquiry was held because of a direction given by the Minister\nunder section 496, the ACCC must give a copy of the report to the\nMinister.\n\n(3) If the inquiry was held otherwise than because of a direction given\nby the Minister under section 496, the ACCC must publish the\nreport.\n\n(4) The ACCC is not required to include in a report any material:\n\n\nPublic inquiries  Part 25\nInquiries by the ACCC  Division 3\n\nSection 505A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson; or\n\n(c) that is the subject of an order or direction under section 503\nor 504."
    },
    {
