      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.439",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) However, the ACMA is not required to inform the respondent that\nthe matter is to be investigated if:\n\n(a) the matter relates to a possible breach of:\n\n(i) the Spam Act 2003 or regulations under that Act; or\n\n(ii) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 or regulations under\nthat Act; and\n\n(b) the ACMA has reasonable grounds to believe that informing\nthe respondent is likely to result in the concealment, loss or\ndestruction of a thing connected with the breach.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) However, the ACMA is not required to inform the respondent that\nthe matter is to be investigated if:\n\n(a) the matter relates to a possible breach of:\n\n(i) the Spam Act 2003 or regulations under that Act; or\n\n(ii) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 or regulations under\nthat Act; and\n\n(b) the ACMA has reasonable grounds to believe that informing\nthe respondent is likely to result in the concealment, loss or\ndestruction of a thing connected with the breach.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-512"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-512-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-512-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5bb1d3d1677c78b062b6be23a1155e8e26a2ca37c73549a8a70a35d8da9cf2b7",
      "skos:note": "Inform respondent about investigation if breach is likely to be concealed, lost or destroyed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-512-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "512(1A) Conduct of investigations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 439,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) However, the ACMA is not required to inform the respondent that\nthe matter is to be investigated if:\n\n(a) the matter relates to a possible breach of:\n\n(i) the Spam Act 2003 or regulations under that Act; or\n\n(ii) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 or regulations under\nthat Act; and\n\n(b) the ACMA has reasonable grounds to believe that informing\nthe respondent is likely to result in the concealment, loss or\ndestruction of a thing connected with the breach."
    },
