    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-514",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "514 Reference of matters to Ombudsman or other responsible",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-514"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.441",
      "values:originalText": "person\n\n(1) If, before the ACMA starts, or after it has started, an investigation\nof a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA forms the\nopinion that:\n\n(a) a complaint relating to that matter has been, or could have\nbeen, made by the complainant to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6; and\n\n(b) the matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt\nwith by:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;\nthe ACMA may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to\ninvestigate the matter further, as the case may be.\n\n(2) If the ACMA decides as mentioned in subsection (1), it must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;",
      "skos:definition": "person\n\n(1) If, before the ACMA starts, or after it has started, an investigation\nof a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA forms the\nopinion that:\n\n(a) a complaint relating to that matter has been, or could have\nbeen, made by the complainant to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6; and\n\n(b) the matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt\nwith by:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;\nthe ACMA may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to\ninvestigate the matter further, as the case may be.\n\n(2) If the ACMA decides as mentioned in subsection (1), it must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-514-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-514-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "38a81e87e79631e602bf5fbd307ce2fcd382b1670c585ea09032aac778a80531"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-514",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "514 Reference of matters to Ombudsman or other responsible",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 441,
      "values:originalText": "person\n\n(1) If, before the ACMA starts, or after it has started, an investigation\nof a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA forms the\nopinion that:\n\n(a) a complaint relating to that matter has been, or could have\nbeen, made by the complainant to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6; and\n\n(b) the matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt\nwith by:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;\nthe ACMA may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to\ninvestigate the matter further, as the case may be.\n\n(2) If the ACMA decides as mentioned in subsection (1), it must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-514-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "514(1) Reference of matters to Ombudsman or other responsible",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-514-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.441",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, before the ACMA starts, or after it has started, an investigation\nof a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA forms the\nopinion that:\n\n(a) a complaint relating to that matter has been, or could have\nbeen, made by the complainant to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6; and\n\n(b) the matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt\nwith by:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;\nthe ACMA may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to\ninvestigate the matter further, as the case may be.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, before the ACMA starts, or after it has started, an investigation\nof a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA forms the\nopinion that:\n\n(a) a complaint relating to that matter has been, or could have\nbeen, made by the complainant to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6; and\n\n(b) the matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt\nwith by:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;\nthe ACMA may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to\ninvestigate the matter further, as the case may be.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-514"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-514-ss-1-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7719f7e63966469bb0857bd5d9c0f0a84b30bb4dc46516813cd479964f9b871e",
      "skos:note": "ACMA may decide not to investigate a matter if it can be more conveniently or effectively dealt with by another person or body."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-514-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "514(1) Reference of matters to Ombudsman or other responsible",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 441,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, before the ACMA starts, or after it has started, an investigation\nof a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA forms the\nopinion that:\n\n(a) a complaint relating to that matter has been, or could have\nbeen, made by the complainant to:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6; and\n\n(b) the matter could be more conveniently or effectively dealt\nwith by:\n\n(i) the Ombudsman; or\n\n(ii) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman; or\n\n(iii) another person or body responsible for handling\ncomplaints under a code registered, or standard\ndetermined, under Part 6;\nthe ACMA may decide not to investigate the matter, or not to\ninvestigate the matter further, as the case may be."
    },
