    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-515",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "515 Reference of matters to the ACCC",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-515"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.442",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, before the ACMA commences, or after it has commenced, an\ninvestigation of a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA\nforms the opinion that the matter could be more conveniently or\neffectively dealt with by the ACCC, it may decide not to\ninvestigate the matter, or not to investigate the matter further, as\nthe case may be.\n\n(2) If the ACMA so decides, it must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to the ACCC; and\n\n(b) give written notice to the complainant stating that the\ncomplaint has been so transferred; and\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 26\n\nSection 515A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) give to the ACCC any information or documents that relate\nto the complaint and that are in the ACMA’s possession or\nunder its control.\n\n(3) The ACCC may hold an investigation into the matter and, if it\ndecides to do so, it must report to the ACMA on:\n\n(a) the conduct of the investigation; and\n\n(b) any findings that it has made as a result of the investigation;\nand\n\n(c) the evidence and other material on which those findings were\nbased; and\n\n(d) such other matters relating to, or arising out of, the\ninvestigation as the ACCC thinks fit.\n\n(4) If the ACCC decides not to hold an investigation into the matter, it\nmust give to the ACMA a written notice informing the ACMA of\nits decision and of the reasons for its decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, before the ACMA commences, or after it has commenced, an\ninvestigation of a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA\nforms the opinion that the matter could be more conveniently or\neffectively dealt with by the ACCC, it may decide not to\ninvestigate the matter, or not to investigate the matter further, as\nthe case may be.\n\n(2) If the ACMA so decides, it must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to the ACCC; and\n\n(b) give written notice to the complainant stating that the\ncomplaint has been so transferred; and\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 26\n\nSection 515A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) give to the ACCC any information or documents that relate\nto the complaint and that are in the ACMA’s possession or\nunder its control.\n\n(3) The ACCC may hold an investigation into the matter and, if it\ndecides to do so, it must report to the ACMA on:\n\n(a) the conduct of the investigation; and\n\n(b) any findings that it has made as a result of the investigation;\nand\n\n(c) the evidence and other material on which those findings were\nbased; and\n\n(d) such other matters relating to, or arising out of, the\ninvestigation as the ACCC thinks fit.\n\n(4) If the ACCC decides not to hold an investigation into the matter, it\nmust give to the ACMA a written notice informing the ACMA of\nits decision and of the reasons for its decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-515-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-515-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-515-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-515-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55db21bae0d528a14b3400d5df343d7224d1de40d81a8c4a5c5717e09ab9949b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-515",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "515 Reference of matters to the ACCC",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 442,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, before the ACMA commences, or after it has commenced, an\ninvestigation of a matter to which a complaint relates, the ACMA\nforms the opinion that the matter could be more conveniently or\neffectively dealt with by the ACCC, it may decide not to\ninvestigate the matter, or not to investigate the matter further, as\nthe case may be.\n\n(2) If the ACMA so decides, it must:\n\n(a) transfer the complaint to the ACCC; and\n\n(b) give written notice to the complainant stating that the\ncomplaint has been so transferred; and\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 26\n\nSection 515A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) give to the ACCC any information or documents that relate\nto the complaint and that are in the ACMA’s possession or\nunder its control.\n\n(3) The ACCC may hold an investigation into the matter and, if it\ndecides to do so, it must report to the ACMA on:\n\n(a) the conduct of the investigation; and\n\n(b) any findings that it has made as a result of the investigation;\nand\n\n(c) the evidence and other material on which those findings were\nbased; and\n\n(d) such other matters relating to, or arising out of, the\ninvestigation as the ACCC thinks fit.\n\n(4) If the ACCC decides not to hold an investigation into the matter, it\nmust give to the ACMA a written notice informing the ACMA of\nits decision and of the reasons for its decision."
    },
