    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-517",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "517 Publication of reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-517"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.445",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA prepares a report under\nsection 516.\n\n(2) If the report was prepared under subsection 516(1), the ACMA\nmay cause the report to be published.\n\n(3) If the report was prepared under subsection 516(2), the Minister\nmay direct the ACMA to publish the report. The ACMA must\ncomply with the direction. The ACMA must not otherwise cause\nthe report to be published.\n\n(4) The ACMA is not required to publish, or to disclose to a person to\nwhose affairs it relates, a report or a part of a report if the\npublication or disclosure would:\n\n(a) disclose a matter of a confidential character; or\n\n(b) be likely to prejudice the fair trial of a person.\n\n(5) The ACMA is not required to publish a report or part of a report if\nthe publication would involve the unreasonable disclosure of\npersonal information about any individual (including a deceased\nindividual).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA prepares a report under\nsection 516.\n\n(2) If the report was prepared under subsection 516(1), the ACMA\nmay cause the report to be published.\n\n(3) If the report was prepared under subsection 516(2), the Minister\nmay direct the ACMA to publish the report. The ACMA must\ncomply with the direction. The ACMA must not otherwise cause\nthe report to be published.\n\n(4) The ACMA is not required to publish, or to disclose to a person to\nwhose affairs it relates, a report or a part of a report if the\npublication or disclosure would:\n\n(a) disclose a matter of a confidential character; or\n\n(b) be likely to prejudice the fair trial of a person.\n\n(5) The ACMA is not required to publish a report or part of a report if\nthe publication would involve the unreasonable disclosure of\npersonal information about any individual (including a deceased\nindividual).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-517-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-517-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-517-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-517-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-517-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "91722461957282cf0a6bcc740a35335a965e81bbaa485535714c5f8fb3922407"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-517",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "517 Publication of reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 445,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA prepares a report under\nsection 516.\n\n(2) If the report was prepared under subsection 516(1), the ACMA\nmay cause the report to be published.\n\n(3) If the report was prepared under subsection 516(2), the Minister\nmay direct the ACMA to publish the report. The ACMA must\ncomply with the direction. The ACMA must not otherwise cause\nthe report to be published.\n\n(4) The ACMA is not required to publish, or to disclose to a person to\nwhose affairs it relates, a report or a part of a report if the\npublication or disclosure would:\n\n(a) disclose a matter of a confidential character; or\n\n(b) be likely to prejudice the fair trial of a person.\n\n(5) The ACMA is not required to publish a report or part of a report if\nthe publication would involve the unreasonable disclosure of\npersonal information about any individual (including a deceased\nindividual)."
    },
