    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-519",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "519 Protection from civil actions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-519"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.446",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss,\ndamage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because\nof any of the following acts done in good faith:\n\n(a) the making of a complaint under section 509;\n\n(b) the making of a statement to, or the giving of a document or\ninformation to, the ACMA in connection with an\ninvestigation under section 510;\n\n(c) the making of a complaint to the Telecommunications\nIndustry Ombudsman;\n\n(d) subject to subsection (2), the making of a statement to, or the\ngiving of a document or information to, the\nTelecommunications Industry Ombudsman in connection\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 26\n\nSection 519\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nwith the consideration by the Telecommunications Industry\nOmbudsman of a complaint.\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(d) does not apply to the making of a statement, or\nthe giving of a document or information, by:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a person who is a service provider and who is participating in\nthe Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme under\nwhich the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman has\nbeen appointed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss,\ndamage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because\nof any of the following acts done in good faith:\n\n(a) the making of a complaint under section 509;\n\n(b) the making of a statement to, or the giving of a document or\ninformation to, the ACMA in connection with an\ninvestigation under section 510;\n\n(c) the making of a complaint to the Telecommunications\nIndustry Ombudsman;\n\n(d) subject to subsection (2), the making of a statement to, or the\ngiving of a document or information to, the\nTelecommunications Industry Ombudsman in connection\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 26\n\nSection 519\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nwith the consideration by the Telecommunications Industry\nOmbudsman of a complaint.\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(d) does not apply to the making of a statement, or\nthe giving of a document or information, by:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a person who is a service provider and who is participating in\nthe Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme under\nwhich the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman has\nbeen appointed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-519-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-519-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "86e93c25d693e336417f121a3c2ec45528cb40d4b5535f25c1a028d532a4d058"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-519",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "519 Protection from civil actions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 446,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss,\ndamage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because\nof any of the following acts done in good faith:\n\n(a) the making of a complaint under section 509;\n\n(b) the making of a statement to, or the giving of a document or\ninformation to, the ACMA in connection with an\ninvestigation under section 510;\n\n(c) the making of a complaint to the Telecommunications\nIndustry Ombudsman;\n\n(d) subject to subsection (2), the making of a statement to, or the\ngiving of a document or information to, the\nTelecommunications Industry Ombudsman in connection\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 26\n\nSection 519\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nwith the consideration by the Telecommunications Industry\nOmbudsman of a complaint.\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(d) does not apply to the making of a statement, or\nthe giving of a document or information, by:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a person who is a service provider and who is participating in\nthe Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme under\nwhich the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman has\nbeen appointed."
    },
