      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman scheme provides exemptions for carriers and service providers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-520",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "520 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-520"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.448",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe ACMA may obtain information from carriers, service\nproviders and other persons if the information is relevant to:\n\n(a)\nthe performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(b)\nthe exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers.\n•\nThe ACMA may make record-keeping rules that apply to\ncarriers and carriage service providers.\n\n\nThe ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27\nInformation-gathering powers  Division 2\n\nSection 521\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe ACMA may obtain information from carriers, service\nproviders and other persons if the information is relevant to:\n\n(a)\nthe performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(b)\nthe exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers.\n•\nThe ACMA may make record-keeping rules that apply to\ncarriers and carriage service providers.\n\n\nThe ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27\nInformation-gathering powers  Division 2\n\nSection 521\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-520-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-520-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a001ba0d91fe8ed9b8dbec70e08f82ea5f186a9ba6baf6aaa8f6e93b0057865d",
      "skos:note": "ACMA may obtain information from carriers and service providers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-520",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "520 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 448,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nThe ACMA may obtain information from carriers, service\nproviders and other persons if the information is relevant to:\n\n(a)\nthe performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(b)\nthe exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers.\n•\nThe ACMA may make record-keeping rules that apply to\ncarriers and carriage service providers.\n\n\nThe ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27\nInformation-gathering powers  Division 2\n\nSection 521\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-520-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-520"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-520-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-521",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "521 The ACMA may obtain information and documents from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-521"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.449",
      "values:originalText": "carriers and service providers\n\n(1) This section applies to a carrier or a service provider if the ACMA\nhas reason to believe that the carrier or provider:\n\n(a) has information or a document that is relevant to:\n\n(i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers; or\n\n(b) is capable of giving evidence which the ACMA has reason to\nbelieve is relevant to:\n\n(i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers.\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or provider,\nrequire the carrier or provider:\n\n(a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner\nand form specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\n(b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies; or\n\n(d) if the carrier or provider is an individual—to appear before\nthe ACMA at a time and place specified in the notice to give\nany such evidence, either orally or in writing, and produce\nany such documents; or\n\n(e) if the carrier or provider is a body corporate or a public\nbody—to cause a competent officer of the body to appear",
      "skos:definition": "carriers and service providers\n\n(1) This section applies to a carrier or a service provider if the ACMA\nhas reason to believe that the carrier or provider:\n\n(a) has information or a document that is relevant to:\n\n(i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers; or\n\n(b) is capable of giving evidence which the ACMA has reason to\nbelieve is relevant to:\n\n(i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers.\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or provider,\nrequire the carrier or provider:\n\n(a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner\nand form specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\n(b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies; or\n\n(d) if the carrier or provider is an individual—to appear before\nthe ACMA at a time and place specified in the notice to give\nany such evidence, either orally or in writing, and produce\nany such documents; or\n\n(e) if the carrier or provider is a body corporate or a public\nbody—to cause a competent officer of the body to appear",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-521-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-521-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "133e75b53b872f7eea24c859140e660afefb0efad2407f109e479dbab863ddf6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-521",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "521 The ACMA may obtain information and documents from",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 449,
      "values:originalText": "carriers and service providers\n\n(1) This section applies to a carrier or a service provider if the ACMA\nhas reason to believe that the carrier or provider:\n\n(a) has information or a document that is relevant to:\n\n(i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers; or\n\n(b) is capable of giving evidence which the ACMA has reason to\nbelieve is relevant to:\n\n(i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s\ntelecommunications functions; or\n\n(ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications\npowers.\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or provider,\nrequire the carrier or provider:\n\n(a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner\nand form specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\n(b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies; or\n\n(d) if the carrier or provider is an individual—to appear before\nthe ACMA at a time and place specified in the notice to give\nany such evidence, either orally or in writing, and produce\nany such documents; or\n\n(e) if the carrier or provider is a body corporate or a public\nbody—to cause a competent officer of the body to appear"
    },
    {
