    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-524",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "524 Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-524"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.452",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An individual is not excused from giving information or evidence\nor producing a document or a copy of a document under this\nDivision on the ground that the information or evidence or the\nproduction of the document or copy might tend to incriminate the\nindividual or expose the individual to a penalty.\n\n(2) However:\n\n(a) giving the information or evidence or producing the\ndocument or copy; or\n\n(b) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or evidence or\nproducing the document or copy;\nis not admissible in evidence against the individual in:\n\n\nThe ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27\nInformation-gathering powers  Division 2\n\nSection 525\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) criminal proceedings other than proceedings under, or arising\nout of, subsection 522(4) or section 525; or\n\n(d) proceedings under section 570 other than proceedings for\nrecovery of a pecuniary penalty in relation to a contravention\nof section 521.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An individual is not excused from giving information or evidence\nor producing a document or a copy of a document under this\nDivision on the ground that the information or evidence or the\nproduction of the document or copy might tend to incriminate the\nindividual or expose the individual to a penalty.\n\n(2) However:\n\n(a) giving the information or evidence or producing the\ndocument or copy; or\n\n(b) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or evidence or\nproducing the document or copy;\nis not admissible in evidence against the individual in:\n\n\nThe ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27\nInformation-gathering powers  Division 2\n\nSection 525\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) criminal proceedings other than proceedings under, or arising\nout of, subsection 522(4) or section 525; or\n\n(d) proceedings under section 570 other than proceedings for\nrecovery of a pecuniary penalty in relation to a contravention\nof section 521.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-524-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-524-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd4e538d21793ca7c76c376ee95f8dda9aa928f60d39d57da9dd22ec3b0f028d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-524",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "524 Self-incrimination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 452,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An individual is not excused from giving information or evidence\nor producing a document or a copy of a document under this\nDivision on the ground that the information or evidence or the\nproduction of the document or copy might tend to incriminate the\nindividual or expose the individual to a penalty.\n\n(2) However:\n\n(a) giving the information or evidence or producing the\ndocument or copy; or\n\n(b) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or evidence or\nproducing the document or copy;\nis not admissible in evidence against the individual in:\n\n\nThe ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27\nInformation-gathering powers  Division 2\n\nSection 525\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) criminal proceedings other than proceedings under, or arising\nout of, subsection 522(4) or section 525; or\n\n(d) proceedings under section 570 other than proceedings for\nrecovery of a pecuniary penalty in relation to a contravention\nof section 521."
    },
