    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-537",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "537 Contents of warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-537"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.462",
      "values:originalText": "The following must be stated in a warrant issued under\nsection 535:\n\n(a) the purpose for which the warrant is issued, and the nature of\nthe offence or breach in relation to which the entry and\nsearch are authorised;\n\n(b) whether entry is authorised to be made at any time of the day\nor night or during specified hours of the day or night;\n\n(c) a description of the kind of things to be seized;\n\n(d) a day, not later than 7 days after the day of issue of the\nwarrant, upon which the warrant ceases to have effect.\n538  Warrants may be issued by telephone etc.\n\nIf, because of circumstances of urgency, an inspector thinks it\nnecessary to do so, the inspector may apply to a magistrate for a\nwarrant under section 535 by telephone, telex, fax or other\nelectronic means.\n539  Provisions relating to issue of warrant by telephone etc.\n\n(1) Before applying under section 538 for a warrant, an inspector must\nprepare an information of a kind referred to in section 535 that sets\nout the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought.\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearch warrants relating to breaches of the Spam Act 2003 or Part 21 of this Act",
      "skos:definition": "The following must be stated in a warrant issued under\nsection 535:\n\n(a) the purpose for which the warrant is issued, and the nature of\nthe offence or breach in relation to which the entry and\nsearch are authorised;\n\n(b) whether entry is authorised to be made at any time of the day\nor night or during specified hours of the day or night;\n\n(c) a description of the kind of things to be seized;\n\n(d) a day, not later than 7 days after the day of issue of the\nwarrant, upon which the warrant ceases to have effect.\n538  Warrants may be issued by telephone etc.\n\nIf, because of circumstances of urgency, an inspector thinks it\nnecessary to do so, the inspector may apply to a magistrate for a\nwarrant under section 535 by telephone, telex, fax or other\nelectronic means.\n539  Provisions relating to issue of warrant by telephone etc.\n\n(1) Before applying under section 538 for a warrant, an inspector must\nprepare an information of a kind referred to in section 535 that sets\nout the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought.\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearch warrants relating to breaches of the Spam Act 2003 or Part 21 of this Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-537-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-537-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-537-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4521d21253089f7b7ac604b577d2bb023355028f59b78b5a3bef0de8b19a183a",
      "skos:note": "Mandatory requirements for issuing a warrant",
      "dc:description": "a, b, c, d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-537",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "537 Contents of warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 462,
      "values:originalText": "The following must be stated in a warrant issued under\nsection 535:\n\n(a) the purpose for which the warrant is issued, and the nature of\nthe offence or breach in relation to which the entry and\nsearch are authorised;\n\n(b) whether entry is authorised to be made at any time of the day\nor night or during specified hours of the day or night;\n\n(c) a description of the kind of things to be seized;\n\n(d) a day, not later than 7 days after the day of issue of the\nwarrant, upon which the warrant ceases to have effect.\n538  Warrants may be issued by telephone etc.\n\nIf, because of circumstances of urgency, an inspector thinks it\nnecessary to do so, the inspector may apply to a magistrate for a\nwarrant under section 535 by telephone, telex, fax or other\nelectronic means.\n539  Provisions relating to issue of warrant by telephone etc.\n\n(1) Before applying under section 538 for a warrant, an inspector must\nprepare an information of a kind referred to in section 535 that sets\nout the grounds on which the issue of the warrant is being sought.\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearch warrants relating to breaches of the Spam Act 2003 or Part 21 of this Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-537-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-537"
      },
