    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-546-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "546(3) Retention of things seized",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 469,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this section:\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-546-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-546-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "547 Searches to monitor compliance with Part 21",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-547"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.470",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector may, to the extent that it is reasonably necessary for\nthe purpose of ascertaining whether Part 21 has been complied\nwith, enter, at any time during the day or night, any premises that\nthe inspector has reasonable cause to believe are premises to which\nthis section applies and:\n\n(a) search the premises; or\n\n(b) inspect and take photographs, or make sketches, of the\npremises or any substance or thing at the premises; or\n\n(c) inspect any document kept at the premises; or\n\n(d) remove, or make copies of, any such document.\nThis section has effect subject to subsections (2) and (3).\n\n(2) An inspector may not, under subsection (1), enter premises that are\na residence unless the occupier of the premises has consented to\nthe entry.\n\n(3) An inspector is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the inspector to\nproduce his or her identity card for inspection by the\noccupier; and\n\n(b) the inspector fails to comply with the requirement.\n\n(4) This section applies to premises at which:\n\n(a) activities that are the subject of regulation under Part 21 are\nengaged in; or\n\n(b) records relating to any such activities are kept.\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearches to monitor compliance with the Spam Act 2003  Division 5A\n\nSection 547A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An inspector may, to the extent that it is reasonably necessary for\nthe purpose of ascertaining whether Part 21 has been complied\nwith, enter, at any time during the day or night, any premises that\nthe inspector has reasonable cause to believe are premises to which\nthis section applies and:\n\n(a) search the premises; or\n\n(b) inspect and take photographs, or make sketches, of the\npremises or any substance or thing at the premises; or\n\n(c) inspect any document kept at the premises; or\n\n(d) remove, or make copies of, any such document.\nThis section has effect subject to subsections (2) and (3).\n\n(2) An inspector may not, under subsection (1), enter premises that are\na residence unless the occupier of the premises has consented to\nthe entry.\n\n(3) An inspector is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the inspector to\nproduce his or her identity card for inspection by the\noccupier; and\n\n(b) the inspector fails to comply with the requirement.\n\n(4) This section applies to premises at which:\n\n(a) activities that are the subject of regulation under Part 21 are\nengaged in; or\n\n(b) records relating to any such activities are kept.\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearches to monitor compliance with the Spam Act 2003  Division 5A\n\nSection 547A\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
