    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "547F Announcement before entry",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-547f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.475",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector must, before entering premises under a warrant under\nsection 547D:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) An inspector is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or\nshe believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person; or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An inspector must, before entering premises under a warrant under\nsection 547D:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) An inspector is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or\nshe believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person; or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547f-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0e3cc703b07be15a2be9975d708e324d3942a7e102fc9aa1608d1656fda3bf36"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-547f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "547F Announcement before entry",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 475,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An inspector must, before entering premises under a warrant under\nsection 547D:\n\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n\n(2) An inspector is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or\nshe believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required:\n\n(a) to ensure the safety of a person; or\n\n(b) to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not\nfrustrated."
    },
    {
