    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "547H Occupier entitled to be present during search",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-547h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.476",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a warrant under section 547D in relation to premises is being\nexecuted; and\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearches to monitor compliance with the Spam Act 2003  Division 5A\n\nSection 547H\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe person is entitled to observe the search being conducted.\n\n(2) The right to observe the search being conducted ceases if the\nperson impedes the search.\n\n(3) This section does not prevent 2 or more areas of the premises being\nsearched at the same time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a warrant under section 547D in relation to premises is being\nexecuted; and\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearches to monitor compliance with the Spam Act 2003  Division 5A\n\nSection 547H\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe person is entitled to observe the search being conducted.\n\n(2) The right to observe the search being conducted ceases if the\nperson impedes the search.\n\n(3) This section does not prevent 2 or more areas of the premises being\nsearched at the same time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-547h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fbff1effb5e1f276c27bb3bf83869697a5a154e7379e9c69e1612dd384a2a8fd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-547h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "547H Occupier entitled to be present during search",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 476,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a warrant under section 547D in relation to premises is being\nexecuted; and\n\n(b) the occupier of the premises, or another person who\napparently represents the occupier, is present at the premises;\n\n\nEnforcement  Part 28\nSearches to monitor compliance with the Spam Act 2003  Division 5A\n\nSection 547H\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe person is entitled to observe the search being conducted.\n\n(2) The right to observe the search being conducted ceases if the\nperson impedes the search.\n\n(3) This section does not prevent 2 or more areas of the premises being\nsearched at the same time."
    },
