      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Decision validity unaffected by non-compliance",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Failure to comply does not affect decision validity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-558",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "558 Applications for reconsideration of decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-558"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.487",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person affected by a decision of a kind referred to in section 555\nwho is dissatisfied with the decision may apply to the ACMA for\nthe ACMA to reconsider the decision.\n\n(2) The application must:\n\n(a) be in a form approved in writing by the ACMA; and\n\n(b) set out the reasons for the application.\n\n(3) The application must be made within:\n\n(a) 28 days after the applicant is informed of the decision; or\n\n(b) if, either before or after the end of that period of 28 days, the\nACMA extends the period within which the application may\nbe made—the extended period for making the application.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person affected by a decision of a kind referred to in section 555\nwho is dissatisfied with the decision may apply to the ACMA for\nthe ACMA to reconsider the decision.\n\n(2) The application must:\n\n(a) be in a form approved in writing by the ACMA; and\n\n(b) set out the reasons for the application.\n\n(3) The application must be made within:\n\n(a) 28 days after the applicant is informed of the decision; or\n\n(b) if, either before or after the end of that period of 28 days, the\nACMA extends the period within which the application may\nbe made—the extended period for making the application.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-558-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-558-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-558-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af7c8553ab0ff88f6348304ce8248b20f7e4a2ffc03f811cadcc2a346a52d568"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-558",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "558 Applications for reconsideration of decisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 487,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person affected by a decision of a kind referred to in section 555\nwho is dissatisfied with the decision may apply to the ACMA for\nthe ACMA to reconsider the decision.\n\n(2) The application must:\n\n(a) be in a form approved in writing by the ACMA; and\n\n(b) set out the reasons for the application.\n\n(3) The application must be made within:\n\n(a) 28 days after the applicant is informed of the decision; or\n\n(b) if, either before or after the end of that period of 28 days, the\nACMA extends the period within which the application may\nbe made—the extended period for making the application."
    },
