    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-570",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "570 Pecuniary penalties for contravention of civil penalty provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-570"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.496",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has contravened a\ncivil penalty provision, the Court may order the person to pay to\nthe Commonwealth such pecuniary penalty, in respect of each\ncontravention, as the Court determines to be appropriate.\n\n(2) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\n(3) The pecuniary penalty payable under subsection (1) by a body\ncorporate is not to exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a contravention of subsection 68(1) or (2) or\n101(1) or (2)—$10 million for each contravention; or\n\n(aaa) in the case of a contravention of a civil penalty provision in",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has contravened a\ncivil penalty provision, the Court may order the person to pay to\nthe Commonwealth such pecuniary penalty, in respect of each\ncontravention, as the Court determines to be appropriate.\n\n(2) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\n(3) The pecuniary penalty payable under subsection (1) by a body\ncorporate is not to exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a contravention of subsection 68(1) or (2) or\n101(1) or (2)—$10 million for each contravention; or\n\n(aaa) in the case of a contravention of a civil penalty provision in",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-570-ss-1"
        },
