    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572g-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Equality of penalties",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The penalty to be specified in an infringement notice...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "must be equal to 12 penalty units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572H Withdrawal of an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.510",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an infringement notice is given to a person.\nWithdrawal\n\n(2) An authorised infringement notice officer may, by written notice\n(the withdrawal notice) given to the person, withdraw the\ninfringement notice.\n\n\nInfringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions  Part 31B\n\nSection 572J\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) To be effective, the withdrawal notice must be given to the person\nwithin 28 days after the infringement notice was given.\nRefund of penalty if infringement notice withdrawn\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) the penalty specified in the infringement notice is paid; and\n\n(b) the infringement notice is withdrawn after the penalty is paid;\nthe Commonwealth is liable to refund the penalty.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an infringement notice is given to a person.\nWithdrawal\n\n(2) An authorised infringement notice officer may, by written notice\n(the withdrawal notice) given to the person, withdraw the\ninfringement notice.\n\n\nInfringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions  Part 31B\n\nSection 572J\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) To be effective, the withdrawal notice must be given to the person\nwithin 28 days after the infringement notice was given.\nRefund of penalty if infringement notice withdrawn\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) the penalty specified in the infringement notice is paid; and\n\n(b) the infringement notice is withdrawn after the penalty is paid;\nthe Commonwealth is liable to refund the penalty.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572h-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572H Withdrawal of an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 510,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an infringement notice is given to a person.\nWithdrawal\n\n(2) An authorised infringement notice officer may, by written notice\n(the withdrawal notice) given to the person, withdraw the\ninfringement notice.\n\n\nInfringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions  Part 31B\n\nSection 572J\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) To be effective, the withdrawal notice must be given to the person\nwithin 28 days after the infringement notice was given.\nRefund of penalty if infringement notice withdrawn\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) the penalty specified in the infringement notice is paid; and\n\n(b) the infringement notice is withdrawn after the penalty is paid;\nthe Commonwealth is liable to refund the penalty."
    },
