    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572L(5) Appointment of authorised infringement notice officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572l-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.512",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorised infringement notice officer appointed under\nsubsection (1) must not give or withdraw an infringement notice if\nthe alleged contravention consists of a breach of:\n\n\nInfringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions  Part 31B\n\nSection 572M\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) section 68, to the extent to which that section relates to the\ncarrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 in so\nfar as that condition relates to section 142C, 143, 143B,\n151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(b) section 101, to the extent to which that section relates to the\nservice provider rule set out in Part 1 of Schedule 2 in so far\nas that rule relates to section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA,\n151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(c) section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF,\n151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An authorised infringement notice officer appointed under\nsubsection (1) must not give or withdraw an infringement notice if\nthe alleged contravention consists of a breach of:\n\n\nInfringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions  Part 31B\n\nSection 572M\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) section 68, to the extent to which that section relates to the\ncarrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 in so\nfar as that condition relates to section 142C, 143, 143B,\n151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(b) section 101, to the extent to which that section relates to the\nservice provider rule set out in Part 1 of Schedule 2 in so far\nas that rule relates to section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA,\n151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(c) section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF,\n151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-5-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e844be7f76cea394baff5aad645ad8c9de7600976fe3bd7ac3bedce9916506fe",
      "skos:note": "Authorized infringement notice officer must not issue or withdraw an infringement notice for certain contraventions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572l-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572L(5) Appointment of authorised infringement notice officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 512,
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorised infringement notice officer appointed under\nsubsection (1) must not give or withdraw an infringement notice if\nthe alleged contravention consists of a breach of:\n\n\nInfringement notices for contraventions of civil penalty provisions  Part 31B\n\nSection 572M\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) section 68, to the extent to which that section relates to the\ncarrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 in so\nfar as that condition relates to section 142C, 143, 143B,\n151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(b) section 101, to the extent to which that section relates to the\nservice provider rule set out in Part 1 of Schedule 2 in so far\nas that rule relates to section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA,\n151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(c) section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF,\n151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI."
    },
