    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572L(6) Appointment of authorised infringement notice officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572l-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.512",
      "values:originalText": "(6) An authorised infringement notice officer appointed under\nsubsection (3) must not give or withdraw an infringement notice\nunless the alleged contravention consists of a breach of:\n\n(a) section 68, to the extent to which that section relates to the\ncarrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 in so\nfar as that condition relates to section 142C, 143, 143B,\n151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(b) section 101, to the extent to which that section relates to the\nservice provider rule set out in Part 1 of Schedule 2 in so far\nas that rule relates to section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA,\n151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(c) section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF,\n151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) An authorised infringement notice officer appointed under\nsubsection (3) must not give or withdraw an infringement notice\nunless the alleged contravention consists of a breach of:\n\n(a) section 68, to the extent to which that section relates to the\ncarrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 in so\nfar as that condition relates to section 142C, 143, 143B,\n151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(b) section 101, to the extent to which that section relates to the\nservice provider rule set out in Part 1 of Schedule 2 in so far\nas that rule relates to section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA,\n151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(c) section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF,\n151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572l-ss-6-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4babe44f9f2f7a0906f60ee7aeb758c1cc3ab0967c559c9f116fc84e7876c03f",
      "skos:note": "Authorized infringement notice officer must not issue infringement notices for certain breaches."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572l-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572L(6) Appointment of authorised infringement notice officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 512,
      "values:originalText": "(6) An authorised infringement notice officer appointed under\nsubsection (3) must not give or withdraw an infringement notice\nunless the alleged contravention consists of a breach of:\n\n(a) section 68, to the extent to which that section relates to the\ncarrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 in so\nfar as that condition relates to section 142C, 143, 143B,\n151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(b) section 101, to the extent to which that section relates to the\nservice provider rule set out in Part 1 of Schedule 2 in so far\nas that rule relates to section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA,\n151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI; or\n\n(c) section 142C, 143, 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB, 151ZD, 151ZF,\n151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI."
    },
