    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "572M Guidelines relating to infringement notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.513",
      "values:originalText": "ACMA guidelines\n\n(1) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chair of the\nACMA, or a member of the staff of the ACMA appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines\nfor the purposes of subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "ACMA guidelines\n\n(1) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chair of the\nACMA, or a member of the staff of the ACMA appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines\nfor the purposes of subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-572m-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f2955b8a523c4cb9310453e19e64d9074568a7c8f5ecc0297c7de06b8b84a45"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-572m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "572M Guidelines relating to infringement notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 513,
      "values:originalText": "ACMA guidelines\n\n(1) If an authorised infringement notice officer is the Chair of the\nACMA, or a member of the staff of the ACMA appointed under\nsection 572L, the officer must, in exercising a power conferred on\nthe officer by this Part, have regard to any relevant guidelines in\nforce under subsection (2).\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, formulate guidelines\nfor the purposes of subsection (1)."
    },
