    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-574a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "574A Definition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-574a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.515",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(c) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 and regulations under that\nAct.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part:\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(c) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 and regulations under that\nAct.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-574a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b084a5cc079c694031ed91f04faca5f3d27472e1bab0600ea6a42c38190f34fe",
      "skos:note": "Defines scope of this Part"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-574a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "574A Definition",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 515,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part:\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(c) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 and regulations under that\nAct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-574a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-574a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-575",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "575 Liability of corporations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-575"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.516",
      "values:originalText": "State of mind\n\n(1) If, in a proceeding under this Act in respect of conduct engaged in\nby a corporation, it is necessary to establish the state of mind of the\ncorporation, it is sufficient to show that:\n\n(a) a director, employee or agent of the corporation engaged in\nthat conduct; and\n\n(b) the director, employee or agent was, in engaging in that\nconduct, acting within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority; and\n\n(c) the director, employee or agent had that state of mind.\nConduct\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) conduct is engaged in on behalf of a corporation by a\ndirector, employee or agent of the corporation; and\n\n(b) the conduct is within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority;\nthe conduct is taken, for the purposes of a proceeding under this\nAct, to have been engaged in by the corporation unless the\ncorporation establishes that it took reasonable precautions and\nexercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\nExtended meaning of state of mind\n\n(3) A reference in subsection (1) to the state of mind of a person\nincludes a reference to:\n\n(a) the knowledge, intention, opinion, belief or purpose of the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the person’s reasons for the intention, opinion, belief or\npurpose.\n\n\nVicarious liability  Part 32\n\nSection 576\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nExtended meaning of director\n\n(4) A reference in this section to a director of a corporation includes a\nreference to a constituent member of a body corporate incorporated\nfor a public purpose by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nExtended meaning of engaging in conduct\n\n(5) A reference in this section to engaging in conduct includes a\nreference to failing or refusing to engage in conduct.",
      "skos:definition": "State of mind\n\n(1) If, in a proceeding under this Act in respect of conduct engaged in\nby a corporation, it is necessary to establish the state of mind of the\ncorporation, it is sufficient to show that:\n\n(a) a director, employee or agent of the corporation engaged in\nthat conduct; and\n\n(b) the director, employee or agent was, in engaging in that\nconduct, acting within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority; and\n\n(c) the director, employee or agent had that state of mind.\nConduct\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) conduct is engaged in on behalf of a corporation by a\ndirector, employee or agent of the corporation; and\n\n(b) the conduct is within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority;\nthe conduct is taken, for the purposes of a proceeding under this\nAct, to have been engaged in by the corporation unless the\ncorporation establishes that it took reasonable precautions and\nexercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\nExtended meaning of state of mind\n\n(3) A reference in subsection (1) to the state of mind of a person\nincludes a reference to:\n\n(a) the knowledge, intention, opinion, belief or purpose of the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the person’s reasons for the intention, opinion, belief or\npurpose.\n\n\nVicarious liability  Part 32\n\nSection 576\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nExtended meaning of director\n\n(4) A reference in this section to a director of a corporation includes a\nreference to a constituent member of a body corporate incorporated\nfor a public purpose by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nExtended meaning of engaging in conduct\n\n(5) A reference in this section to engaging in conduct includes a\nreference to failing or refusing to engage in conduct.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-575-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-575-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-575-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-575-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-575-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "039ffb948c9e43df11a0de44d91d812a11dc463383a29c79fed010496d5ba342"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-575",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "575 Liability of corporations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 516,
      "values:originalText": "State of mind\n\n(1) If, in a proceeding under this Act in respect of conduct engaged in\nby a corporation, it is necessary to establish the state of mind of the\ncorporation, it is sufficient to show that:\n\n(a) a director, employee or agent of the corporation engaged in\nthat conduct; and\n\n(b) the director, employee or agent was, in engaging in that\nconduct, acting within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority; and\n\n(c) the director, employee or agent had that state of mind.\nConduct\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) conduct is engaged in on behalf of a corporation by a\ndirector, employee or agent of the corporation; and\n\n(b) the conduct is within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority;\nthe conduct is taken, for the purposes of a proceeding under this\nAct, to have been engaged in by the corporation unless the\ncorporation establishes that it took reasonable precautions and\nexercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.\nExtended meaning of state of mind\n\n(3) A reference in subsection (1) to the state of mind of a person\nincludes a reference to:\n\n(a) the knowledge, intention, opinion, belief or purpose of the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the person’s reasons for the intention, opinion, belief or\npurpose.\n\n\nVicarious liability  Part 32\n\nSection 576\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nExtended meaning of director\n\n(4) A reference in this section to a director of a corporation includes a\nreference to a constituent member of a body corporate incorporated\nfor a public purpose by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nExtended meaning of engaging in conduct\n\n(5) A reference in this section to engaging in conduct includes a\nreference to failing or refusing to engage in conduct."
    },
    {
