    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.519",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nTelstra may give the following undertakings:\n\n(a)\nan undertaking about structural separation;\n\n(b)\nan undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks;\n\n(c)\nan undertaking about subscription television\nbroadcasting licences.\n•\nAn undertaking about structural separation applies to certain\ndesignated Telstra successor companies.\n•\nAn undertaking comes into force when it is accepted by the\nACCC.\n•\nThe Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nthe excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra. If the\nMinister does so, Telstra will not be allowed to supply\nservices using a designated part of the spectrum unless all 3\nundertakings given by Telstra are in force.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nTelstra may give the following undertakings:\n\n(a)\nan undertaking about structural separation;\n\n(b)\nan undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks;\n\n(c)\nan undertaking about subscription television\nbroadcasting licences.\n•\nAn undertaking about structural separation applies to certain\ndesignated Telstra successor companies.\n•\nAn undertaking comes into force when it is accepted by the\nACCC.\n•\nThe Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nthe excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra. If the\nMinister does so, Telstra will not be allowed to supply\nservices using a designated part of the spectrum unless all 3\nundertakings given by Telstra are in force.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99ea00405215fa234ba7f2cd2202b5578ac80daf4039e9f4dd8ceda5c0ac8999",
      "skos:note": "Telstra undertakings regarding structural separation, hybrid fibre-coaxial networks, and subscription television broadcasting licences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 519,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nTelstra may give the following undertakings:\n\n(a)\nan undertaking about structural separation;\n\n(b)\nan undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks;\n\n(c)\nan undertaking about subscription television\nbroadcasting licences.\n•\nAn undertaking about structural separation applies to certain\ndesignated Telstra successor companies.\n•\nAn undertaking comes into force when it is accepted by the\nACCC.\n•\nThe Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nthe excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra. If the\nMinister does so, Telstra will not be allowed to supply\nservices using a designated part of the spectrum unless all 3\nundertakings given by Telstra are in force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577A Acceptance of undertaking about structural separation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.521",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may accept a written undertaking given by Telstra that:\n\n(a) at all times after the designated day:\n\n(i) Telstra will not supply fixed-line carriage services to\nretail customers in Australia using a\ntelecommunications network over which Telstra is in a\nposition to exercise control; and\n\n(ii) Telstra will not be in a position to exercise control of a\ncompany that supplies fixed-line carriage services to\nretail customers in Australia using a\ntelecommunications network over which Telstra is in a\nposition to exercise control; and\n\n(b) Telstra will, in connection with paragraph (a), take specified\naction and/or refrain from taking specified action.\nNote 1:\nFor when Telstra is in a position to exercise control of a network, see\nsection 577Q.\nNote 2:\nFor control of a company, see section 577P.\nTransparency and equivalence\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a matter relating to\ntransparency and equivalence in relation to the supply by Telstra of\nregulated services to:\n\n(a) Telstra’s wholesale customers; and\n\n(b) Telstra’s retail business units;\nduring the period:\n\n(c) beginning when the undertaking comes into force; and\n\n(d) ending at the start of the designated day;\nis taken to be a matter that is in connection with paragraph (1)(a).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACCC may accept a written undertaking given by Telstra that:\n\n(a) at all times after the designated day:\n\n(i) Telstra will not supply fixed-line carriage services to\nretail customers in Australia using a\ntelecommunications network over which Telstra is in a\nposition to exercise control; and\n\n(ii) Telstra will not be in a position to exercise control of a\ncompany that supplies fixed-line carriage services to\nretail customers in Australia using a\ntelecommunications network over which Telstra is in a\nposition to exercise control; and\n\n(b) Telstra will, in connection with paragraph (a), take specified\naction and/or refrain from taking specified action.\nNote 1:\nFor when Telstra is in a position to exercise control of a network, see\nsection 577Q.\nNote 2:\nFor control of a company, see section 577P.\nTransparency and equivalence\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a matter relating to\ntransparency and equivalence in relation to the supply by Telstra of\nregulated services to:\n\n(a) Telstra’s wholesale customers; and\n\n(b) Telstra’s retail business units;\nduring the period:\n\n(c) beginning when the undertaking comes into force; and\n\n(d) ending at the start of the designated day;\nis taken to be a matter that is in connection with paragraph (1)(a).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ce4f62804c220d0ec8154a771e26725bf9fbca011651e6b6636854471f2b5590"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577A Acceptance of undertaking about structural separation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 521,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may accept a written undertaking given by Telstra that:\n\n(a) at all times after the designated day:\n\n(i) Telstra will not supply fixed-line carriage services to\nretail customers in Australia using a\ntelecommunications network over which Telstra is in a\nposition to exercise control; and\n\n(ii) Telstra will not be in a position to exercise control of a\ncompany that supplies fixed-line carriage services to\nretail customers in Australia using a\ntelecommunications network over which Telstra is in a\nposition to exercise control; and\n\n(b) Telstra will, in connection with paragraph (a), take specified\naction and/or refrain from taking specified action.\nNote 1:\nFor when Telstra is in a position to exercise control of a network, see\nsection 577Q.\nNote 2:\nFor control of a company, see section 577P.\nTransparency and equivalence\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a matter relating to\ntransparency and equivalence in relation to the supply by Telstra of\nregulated services to:\n\n(a) Telstra’s wholesale customers; and\n\n(b) Telstra’s retail business units;\nduring the period:\n\n(c) beginning when the undertaking comes into force; and\n\n(d) ending at the start of the designated day;\nis taken to be a matter that is in connection with paragraph (1)(a)."
    },
    {
