    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ad",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577AD Compliance with undertaking about structural separation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577ad"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.532",
      "values:originalText": "If an undertaking is in force under section 577A and imposes\nobligations or prohibitions on a designated Telstra successor\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nStructural separation  Division 2\n\nSection 577B\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncompany, the designated Telstra successor company must comply\nwith the undertaking.",
      "skos:definition": "If an undertaking is in force under section 577A and imposes\nobligations or prohibitions on a designated Telstra successor\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nStructural separation  Division 2\n\nSection 577B\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncompany, the designated Telstra successor company must comply\nwith the undertaking.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ad-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ad-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a07d59e9086740c01a4aee19cd78755999bf404b6758fe6c9a7ccd8a5b958bf",
      "skos:note": "Designated Telstra successor company must comply with the undertaking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577ad",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577AD Compliance with undertaking about structural separation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 532,
      "values:originalText": "If an undertaking is in force under section 577A and imposes\nobligations or prohibitions on a designated Telstra successor\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nStructural separation  Division 2\n\nSection 577B\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncompany, the designated Telstra successor company must comply\nwith the undertaking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ad-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ad"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ad-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must comply",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577B Variation of undertaking about structural separation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.533",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an undertaking is in force under\nsection 577A.\n\n(2) If the undertaking imposes obligations or prohibitions on a\ndesignated Telstra successor company, the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company may give the ACCC a variation of the\nundertaking, in so far as the undertaking:\n\n(a) is covered by paragraph 577A(1)(b); and\n\n(b) does not consist of provisions of a final migration plan.\nNote:\nFor variation of a final migration plan, see section 577BF.\n\n(3) After considering the variation, the ACCC must decide to:\n\n(a) accept the variation; or\n\n(b) reject the variation.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\n(a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under\nsubsection (5); and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by writing, set out matters for the purposes of\nparagraph (4)(a).\n\n(5A) Before making or varying an instrument under subsection (5), the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the draft instrument or variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister\nabout the draft instrument or variation within 14 days\nafter the notice is published; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period\nmentioned in paragraph (a).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an undertaking is in force under\nsection 577A.\n\n(2) If the undertaking imposes obligations or prohibitions on a\ndesignated Telstra successor company, the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company may give the ACCC a variation of the\nundertaking, in so far as the undertaking:\n\n(a) is covered by paragraph 577A(1)(b); and\n\n(b) does not consist of provisions of a final migration plan.\nNote:\nFor variation of a final migration plan, see section 577BF.\n\n(3) After considering the variation, the ACCC must decide to:\n\n(a) accept the variation; or\n\n(b) reject the variation.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\n(a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under\nsubsection (5); and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by writing, set out matters for the purposes of\nparagraph (4)(a).\n\n(5A) Before making or varying an instrument under subsection (5), the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the draft instrument or variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister\nabout the draft instrument or variation within 14 days\nafter the notice is published; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period\nmentioned in paragraph (a).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577b-ss-5a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "68125a5904092073d757e68ee43d06afaca30b43d53d4a1dc66d4f4195604bf3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577B Variation of undertaking about structural separation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 533,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an undertaking is in force under\nsection 577A.\n\n(2) If the undertaking imposes obligations or prohibitions on a\ndesignated Telstra successor company, the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company may give the ACCC a variation of the\nundertaking, in so far as the undertaking:\n\n(a) is covered by paragraph 577A(1)(b); and\n\n(b) does not consist of provisions of a final migration plan.\nNote:\nFor variation of a final migration plan, see section 577BF.\n\n(3) After considering the variation, the ACCC must decide to:\n\n(a) accept the variation; or\n\n(b) reject the variation.\n\n(4) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\n(a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under\nsubsection (5); and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by writing, set out matters for the purposes of\nparagraph (4)(a).\n\n(5A) Before making or varying an instrument under subsection (5), the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the draft instrument or variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister\nabout the draft instrument or variation within 14 days\nafter the notice is published; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period\nmentioned in paragraph (a)."
    },
    {
