    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577bd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577BD Approval of draft migration plan by the ACCC—plan given",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577bd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.549",
      "values:originalText": "after undertaking about structural separation comes into\nforce\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if Telstra gives the ACCC a draft migration\nplan (the original plan) in accordance with an undertaking in force\nunder section 577A.\nDecision\n\n(2) The ACCC must:\n\n(a) if the ACCC is satisfied that the original plan complies with\nthe migration plan principles—approve the original plan; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) refuse to approve the original plan; and\n\n(ii) by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to give\nthe ACCC, within 30 days after the notice is given, a\nreplacement draft migration plan that complies with the\nmigration plan principles.\nNote:\nFor migration plan principles, see section 577BB.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before making a decision under subsection (2), the ACCC must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the ACCC’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the original plan; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the ACCC\nabout the original plan within 28 days after the notice is\npublished; and",
      "skos:definition": "after undertaking about structural separation comes into\nforce\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if Telstra gives the ACCC a draft migration\nplan (the original plan) in accordance with an undertaking in force\nunder section 577A.\nDecision\n\n(2) The ACCC must:\n\n(a) if the ACCC is satisfied that the original plan complies with\nthe migration plan principles—approve the original plan; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) refuse to approve the original plan; and\n\n(ii) by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to give\nthe ACCC, within 30 days after the notice is given, a\nreplacement draft migration plan that complies with the\nmigration plan principles.\nNote:\nFor migration plan principles, see section 577BB.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before making a decision under subsection (2), the ACCC must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the ACCC’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the original plan; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the ACCC\nabout the original plan within 28 days after the notice is\npublished; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577bd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577bd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577bd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "76b25b8442c4a4b611ed16b369022fc2057367e6b30417f7df203182408cfdd2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577bd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577BD Approval of draft migration plan by the ACCC—plan given",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 549,
      "values:originalText": "after undertaking about structural separation comes into\nforce\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if Telstra gives the ACCC a draft migration\nplan (the original plan) in accordance with an undertaking in force\nunder section 577A.\nDecision\n\n(2) The ACCC must:\n\n(a) if the ACCC is satisfied that the original plan complies with\nthe migration plan principles—approve the original plan; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) refuse to approve the original plan; and\n\n(ii) by written notice given to Telstra, direct Telstra to give\nthe ACCC, within 30 days after the notice is given, a\nreplacement draft migration plan that complies with the\nmigration plan principles.\nNote:\nFor migration plan principles, see section 577BB.\nConsultation\n\n(3) Before making a decision under subsection (2), the ACCC must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the ACCC’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the original plan; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the ACCC\nabout the original plan within 28 days after the notice is\npublished; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577bd-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577BD(1) Approval of draft migration plan by the ACCC—plan given",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577bd-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
