    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577D Variation of undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.566",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an undertaking given by Telstra is in force\nunder section 577C.\n\n(2) Telstra may give the ACCC a variation of the undertaking in so far\nas the undertaking is covered by paragraph 577C(1)(b).\n\n(3) After considering the variation, the ACCC must decide to:\n\n(a) accept the variation; or\n\n(b) reject the variation.\n\n(3A) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\n(a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under\nsubsection (3B); and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(3B) The Minister may, by writing, set out matters for the purposes of\nparagraph (3A)(a).\n\n(3C) Before making or varying an instrument under subsection (3B), the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the draft instrument or variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister\nabout the draft instrument or variation within 14 days\nafter the notice is published; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period\nmentioned in paragraph (a).\n\n(4) The variation takes effect when it is accepted by the ACCC.\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nHybrid fibre-coaxial networks  Division 3\n\nSection 577D\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(5) As soon as practicable after the variation takes effect, the ACCC\nmust publish the variation on its website.\n\n(6) The Minister must cause a copy of an instrument under\nsubsection (3B) to be published on the Department’s website.\n\n(7) An instrument under subsection (3B) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if an undertaking given by Telstra is in force\nunder section 577C.\n\n(2) Telstra may give the ACCC a variation of the undertaking in so far\nas the undertaking is covered by paragraph 577C(1)(b).\n\n(3) After considering the variation, the ACCC must decide to:\n\n(a) accept the variation; or\n\n(b) reject the variation.\n\n(3A) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\n(a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under\nsubsection (3B); and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(3B) The Minister may, by writing, set out matters for the purposes of\nparagraph (3A)(a).\n\n(3C) Before making or varying an instrument under subsection (3B), the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the draft instrument or variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister\nabout the draft instrument or variation within 14 days\nafter the notice is published; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period\nmentioned in paragraph (a).\n\n(4) The variation takes effect when it is accepted by the ACCC.\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nHybrid fibre-coaxial networks  Division 3\n\nSection 577D\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(5) As soon as practicable after the variation takes effect, the ACCC\nmust publish the variation on its website.\n\n(6) The Minister must cause a copy of an instrument under\nsubsection (3B) to be published on the Department’s website.\n\n(7) An instrument under subsection (3B) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-3b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-3c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577d-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "57363d886d67fe28918f60feabcc13585d32a9caac0ff1325ae2c19bb538792b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577D Variation of undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 566,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if an undertaking given by Telstra is in force\nunder section 577C.\n\n(2) Telstra may give the ACCC a variation of the undertaking in so far\nas the undertaking is covered by paragraph 577C(1)(b).\n\n(3) After considering the variation, the ACCC must decide to:\n\n(a) accept the variation; or\n\n(b) reject the variation.\n\n(3A) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\n(a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under\nsubsection (3B); and\n\n(b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(3B) The Minister may, by writing, set out matters for the purposes of\nparagraph (3A)(a).\n\n(3C) Before making or varying an instrument under subsection (3B), the\nMinister must:\n\n(a) cause to be published on the Department’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the draft instrument or variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the Minister\nabout the draft instrument or variation within 14 days\nafter the notice is published; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the 14-day period\nmentioned in paragraph (a).\n\n(4) The variation takes effect when it is accepted by the ACCC.\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nHybrid fibre-coaxial networks  Division 3\n\nSection 577D\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(5) As soon as practicable after the variation takes effect, the ACCC\nmust publish the variation on its website.\n\n(6) The Minister must cause a copy of an instrument under\nsubsection (3B) to be published on the Department’s website.\n\n(7) An instrument under subsection (3B) is not a legislative\ninstrument."
    },
