      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) If the Federal Court is satisfied...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The designated Telstra successor company must not exercise its rights."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577fa-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits exercise of rights",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) an order prohibiting or deferring the payment of any sums due to a person...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The designated Telstra successor company must not pay sums."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577fa-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits disposal of assets",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) an order directing the disposal of network units, shares or other assets;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The designated Telstra successor company must not dispose of assets."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577G Enforcement of undertakings in force under section 577C or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.576",
      "values:originalText": "577E\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577C or 577E; and\n\n(b) the ACCC considers that Telstra has breached the\nundertaking;\nthe ACCC may apply to the Federal Court for an order under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(2) If the Federal Court is satisfied that Telstra has breached the\nundertaking, the Court may make any or all of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing Telstra to comply with the undertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the disposal of network units, shares or\nother assets;\n\n(c) an order restraining the exercise of any rights attached to\nshares;\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nEnforcement of undertakings  Division 5\n\nSection 577G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) an order prohibiting or deferring the payment of any sums\ndue to a person in respect of shares held by Telstra;\n\n(e) an order that any exercise of rights attached to shares be\ndisregarded;\n\n(f) an order directing Telstra to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that Telstra\nhas obtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably\nattributable to the breach;\n\n(g) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing\nTelstra to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n\n(h) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\n(3) In addition to the Federal Court’s powers under subsection (2), the\ncourt:\n\n(a) has power, for the purpose of securing compliance with any\nother order made under this section, to make an order\ndirecting any person to do or refrain from doing a specified\nact; and\n\n(b) has power to make an order containing such ancillary or\nconsequential provisions as the court thinks just.\n\n(4) The Federal Court may, before making an order under this section,\ndirect that notice of the application be given to such persons as it\nthinks fit or be published in such manner as it thinks fit, or both.\n\n(5) The Federal Court may, by order, rescind, vary or discharge an\norder made by it under this section or suspend the operation of\nsuch an order.",
      "skos:definition": "577E\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577C or 577E; and\n\n(b) the ACCC considers that Telstra has breached the\nundertaking;\nthe ACCC may apply to the Federal Court for an order under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(2) If the Federal Court is satisfied that Telstra has breached the\nundertaking, the Court may make any or all of the following\norders:\n\n(a) an order directing Telstra to comply with the undertaking;\n\n(b) an order directing the disposal of network units, shares or\nother assets;\n\n(c) an order restraining the exercise of any rights attached to\nshares;\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nEnforcement of undertakings  Division 5\n\nSection 577G\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) an order prohibiting or deferring the payment of any sums\ndue to a person in respect of shares held by Telstra;\n\n(e) an order that any exercise of rights attached to shares be\ndisregarded;\n\n(f) an order directing Telstra to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that Telstra\nhas obtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably\nattributable to the breach;\n\n(g) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing\nTelstra to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n\n(h) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\n(3) In addition to the Federal Court’s powers under subsection (2), the\ncourt:\n\n(a) has power, for the purpose of securing compliance with any\nother order made under this section, to make an order\ndirecting any person to do or refrain from doing a specified\nact; and\n\n(b) has power to make an order containing such ancillary or\nconsequential provisions as the court thinks just.\n\n(4) The Federal Court may, before making an order under this section,\ndirect that notice of the application be given to such persons as it\nthinks fit or be published in such manner as it thinks fit, or both.\n\n(5) The Federal Court",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
