    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577H Designated part of the spectrum",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.578",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, each of the following parts of the\nspectrum is a designated part of the spectrum:\n\n(a) frequencies higher than 520 MHz, up to and including 820\nMHz;\n\n(b) frequencies higher than 2.5 GHz, up to and including 2.69\nGHz.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified part of the spectrum is not a designated part of the\nspectrum for the purposes of this Act.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified part of the spectrum is a designated part of the spectrum\nfor the purposes of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, each of the following parts of the\nspectrum is a designated part of the spectrum:\n\n(a) frequencies higher than 520 MHz, up to and including 820\nMHz;\n\n(b) frequencies higher than 2.5 GHz, up to and including 2.69\nGHz.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified part of the spectrum is not a designated part of the\nspectrum for the purposes of this Act.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified part of the spectrum is a designated part of the spectrum\nfor the purposes of this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577h-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bd74f9ac069289967c365987f91eda96a382c9a4c3b0d0da4554590d920cab2e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577H Designated part of the spectrum",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 578,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, each of the following parts of the\nspectrum is a designated part of the spectrum:\n\n(a) frequencies higher than 520 MHz, up to and including 820\nMHz;\n\n(b) frequencies higher than 2.5 GHz, up to and including 2.69\nGHz.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified part of the spectrum is not a designated part of the\nspectrum for the purposes of this Act.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that a\nspecified part of the spectrum is a designated part of the spectrum\nfor the purposes of this Act."
    },
