    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577J Limits on allocation of certain spectrum licences to Telstra",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.578",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra, the ACMA\nmust not allocate a spectrum licence to Telstra if the licence relates\nto a designated part of the spectrum.\nNote:\nFor excluded spectrum regime, see section 577GA.\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nLimits on allocation of spectrum licences etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 577J\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577A; and\n\n(ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577C; or\n\n(ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (3); and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577E; or\n\n(ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (5).\nNote 1:\nSection 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation.\nNote 2:\nSection 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial\nnetworks.\nNote 3:\nSection 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television\nbroadcasting licences.\n\n(2A) This subsection covers a section 577A undertaking if:\n\n(a) the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a\ndraft migration plan;\n\n(ii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given\nthe ACCC a draft migration plan;\n\n(iii) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under\nsection 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or\n\n(b) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a\ndraft migration plan.\n\n(3) The Minister may declare, in writing, that Telstra is exempt from\nthe requirement to have an undertaking under section 577C.\n\n(4) The Minister must not make a declaration under subsection (3)\nunless the ACCC has made a decision to accept an undertaking\ngiven by Telstra under section 577A, and:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra, the ACMA\nmust not allocate a spectrum licence to Telstra if the licence relates\nto a designated part of the spectrum.\nNote:\nFor excluded spectrum regime, see section 577GA.\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nLimits on allocation of spectrum licences etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 577J\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577A; and\n\n(ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577C; or\n\n(ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (3); and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577E; or\n\n(ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (5).\nNote 1:\nSection 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation.\nNote 2:\nSection 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial\nnetworks.\nNote 3:\nSection 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television\nbroadcasting licences.\n\n(2A) This subsection covers a section 577A undertaking if:\n\n(a) the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a\ndraft migration plan;\n\n(ii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given\nthe ACCC a draft migration plan;\n\n(iii) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under\nsection 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or\n\n(b) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a\ndraft migration plan.\n\n(3) The Minister may declare, in writing, that Telstra is exempt from\nthe requirement to have an undertaking under section 577C.\n\n(4) The Minister must not make a declaration under subsection (3)\nunless the ACCC has made a decision to accept an undertaking\ngiven by Telstra under section 577A, and:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "42c4128824f5eae8112095c75f5ea4970b6b6ffda350ec005cf7e565da7c82e3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577J Limits on allocation of certain spectrum licences to Telstra",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 578,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra, the ACMA\nmust not allocate a spectrum licence to Telstra if the licence relates\nto a designated part of the spectrum.\nNote:\nFor excluded spectrum regime, see section 577GA.\n\n\nVoluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33\nLimits on allocation of spectrum licences etc.  Division 6\n\nSection 577J\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) both:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577A; and\n\n(ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577C; or\n\n(ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (3); and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under\nsection 577E; or\n\n(ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (5).\nNote 1:\nSection 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation.\nNote 2:\nSection 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial\nnetworks.\nNote 3:\nSection 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television\nbroadcasting licences.\n\n(2A) This subsection covers a section 577A undertaking if:\n\n(a) the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n(i) the undertaking requires Telstra to give the ACCC a\ndraft migration plan;\n\n(ii) in accordance with the undertaking, Telstra has given\nthe ACCC a draft migration plan;\n\n(iii) the ACCC has approved the draft migration plan under\nsection 577BD, 577BDA, 577BDB or 577BDC; or\n\n(b) the undertaking does not require Telstra to give the ACCC a\ndraft migration plan.\n\n(3) The Minister may declare, in writing, that Telstra is exempt from\nthe requirement to have an undertaking under section 577C.\n\n(4) The Minister must not make a declaration under subsection (3)\nunless the ACCC has made a decision to accept an undertaking\ngiven by Telstra under section 577A, and:"
    },
