    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577M Associate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.585",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company in relation to control of:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network; or\n\n(b) a company;\nis:\n\n(c) a partner of the designated Telstra successor company; or\n\n(d) if the designated Telstra successor company or another\nperson who is an associate of the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company under another paragraph receives benefits\nor is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the\ntrust; or\n\n(e) a person (whether a company or not) who:\n\n(i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or\n\n(ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding\n(whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to\nact;\n\nin accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of,\nor in concert with:\n\n(iii) the designated Telstra successor company; or\n\n(iv) the designated Telstra successor company and another\nperson who is an associate of the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company under another paragraph; or\n\n(f) another company if:\n\n(i) the other company is a related body corporate of the\ndesignated Telstra successor company for the purposes\nof the Corporations Act 2001; or",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company in relation to control of:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network; or\n\n(b) a company;\nis:\n\n(c) a partner of the designated Telstra successor company; or\n\n(d) if the designated Telstra successor company or another\nperson who is an associate of the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company under another paragraph receives benefits\nor is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the\ntrust; or\n\n(e) a person (whether a company or not) who:\n\n(i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or\n\n(ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding\n(whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to\nact;\n\nin accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of,\nor in concert with:\n\n(iii) the designated Telstra successor company; or\n\n(iv) the designated Telstra successor company and another\nperson who is an associate of the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company under another paragraph; or\n\n(f) another company if:\n\n(i) the other company is a related body corporate of the\ndesignated Telstra successor company for the purposes\nof the Corporations Act 2001; or",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577m-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577m-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f5e521ea60b879d9644da65bdf1980c8f5ed8017a603e17c4fc448ce31a2869a",
      "skos:note": "Associate definition for control of telecommunications network, company, or trust"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577M Associate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 585,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company in relation to control of:\n\n(a) a telecommunications network; or\n\n(b) a company;\nis:\n\n(c) a partner of the designated Telstra successor company; or\n\n(d) if the designated Telstra successor company or another\nperson who is an associate of the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company under another paragraph receives benefits\nor is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the\ntrust; or\n\n(e) a person (whether a company or not) who:\n\n(i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or\n\n(ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding\n(whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to\nact;\n\nin accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of,\nor in concert with:\n\n(iii) the designated Telstra successor company; or\n\n(iv) the designated Telstra successor company and another\nperson who is an associate of the designated Telstra\nsuccessor company under another paragraph; or\n\n(f) another company if:\n\n(i) the other company is a related body corporate of the\ndesignated Telstra successor company for the purposes\nof the Corporations Act 2001; or"
    },
