    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "577P Control of a company",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.587",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the question of whether a person is in\na position to exercise control of a company is to be determined\nunder Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992.\n\n(2) However, in determining that question:\n\n(a) the definition of associate in subsection 6(1) of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992 does not apply; and\n\n(b) the definition of associate in section 577M of this Act applies\ninstead.\n577Q  When Telstra or a designated Telstra successor company is in\na position to exercise control of a network\n\n(1A) For the purposes of this Part, a designated Telstra successor\ncompany is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(a) a hybrid fibre-coaxial network; or\n\n(b) another telecommunications network;\nif:\n\n(c) the designated Telstra successor company legally or\nbeneficially owns the network (whether alone or together\nwith one or more other persons); or",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the question of whether a person is in\na position to exercise control of a company is to be determined\nunder Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992.\n\n(2) However, in determining that question:\n\n(a) the definition of associate in subsection 6(1) of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992 does not apply; and\n\n(b) the definition of associate in section 577M of this Act applies\ninstead.\n577Q  When Telstra or a designated Telstra successor company is in\na position to exercise control of a network\n\n(1A) For the purposes of this Part, a designated Telstra successor\ncompany is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(a) a hybrid fibre-coaxial network; or\n\n(b) another telecommunications network;\nif:\n\n(c) the designated Telstra successor company legally or\nbeneficially owns the network (whether alone or together\nwith one or more other persons); or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577p-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "30a483e4d6666830d3ff017b44d822aad2dd86a7189ceb965eba894650055fa2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-577p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "577P Control of a company",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 587,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the question of whether a person is in\na position to exercise control of a company is to be determined\nunder Schedule 1 to the Broadcasting Services Act 1992.\n\n(2) However, in determining that question:\n\n(a) the definition of associate in subsection 6(1) of the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992 does not apply; and\n\n(b) the definition of associate in section 577M of this Act applies\ninstead.\n577Q  When Telstra or a designated Telstra successor company is in\na position to exercise control of a network\n\n(1A) For the purposes of this Part, a designated Telstra successor\ncompany is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(a) a hybrid fibre-coaxial network; or\n\n(b) another telecommunications network;\nif:\n\n(c) the designated Telstra successor company legally or\nbeneficially owns the network (whether alone or together\nwith one or more other persons); or"
    },
