    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581F Telstra successor company",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.597",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of each prescribed telecommunications law,\nTelstra successor company means a demerged Telstra company.\nNote:\nFor demerged Telstra company, see section 581J.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to subsections (6), (7) and (8).\nDeclarations—extended meaning of Telstra successor company\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a\nspecified company (other than a demerged Telstra company) is a\nTelstra successor company for the purposes of each prescribed\ntelecommunications law.\nNote 1:\nFor criteria, see section 581H.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a\nspecified company (other than a demerged Telstra company) is a\nTelstra successor company for the purposes of one or more\nspecified prescribed telecommunications laws.\nNote 1:\nFor criteria, see section 581H.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a\nspecified company (other than a demerged Telstra company) is a\nTelstra successor company for the purposes of one or more\nspecified provisions of one or more prescribed telecommunications\nlaws.\nNote 1:\nFor criteria, see section 581H.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of each prescribed telecommunications law,\nTelstra successor company means a demerged Telstra company.\nNote:\nFor demerged Telstra company, see section 581J.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to subsections (6), (7) and (8).\nDeclarations—extended meaning of Telstra successor company\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a\nspecified company (other than a demerged Telstra company) is a\nTelstra successor company for the purposes of each prescribed\ntelecommunications law.\nNote 1:\nFor criteria, see section 581H.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(4) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a\nspecified company (other than a demerged Telstra company) is a\nTelstra successor company for the purposes of one or more\nspecified prescribed telecommunications laws.\nNote 1:\nFor criteria, see section 581H.\nNote 2:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that a\nspecified company (other than a demerged Telstra company) is a\nTelstra successor company for the purposes of one or more\nspecified provisions of one or more prescribed telecommunications\nlaws.\nNote 1:\nFor criteria, see section 581H.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
