    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581MA Notification of proposed transfer of prescribed business",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581ma"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.606",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a company is:\n\n(i) a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company; and\n\n(ii) a constitutional corporation; and\n\n(b) the company proposes to transfer the whole or a part of a\nprescribed business after the commencement of Schedule 2 to\nthe Telstra Corporation and Other Legislation Amendment\nAct 2021; and\n\n(c) the proposed transferee is a not a constitutional corporation;\nthe company must:\n\n(d) notify the ACMA in writing of the proposed transfer; and\n\n(e) do so at least 30 days before the proposed transfer date.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(3) If the ACMA receives a notification under subsection (1), the\nACMA must give a copy of the notification to the Minister.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, prescribed business means a\nbusiness in a prescribed class of businesses.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that one or\nmore specified classes of businesses are prescribed classes of\nbusinesses for the purpose of subsection (4).\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nTransfer of assets  Division 4\n\nSection 581N\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a company is:\n\n(i) a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company; and\n\n(ii) a constitutional corporation; and\n\n(b) the company proposes to transfer the whole or a part of a\nprescribed business after the commencement of Schedule 2 to\nthe Telstra Corporation and Other Legislation Amendment\nAct 2021; and\n\n(c) the proposed transferee is a not a constitutional corporation;\nthe company must:\n\n(d) notify the ACMA in writing of the proposed transfer; and\n\n(e) do so at least 30 days before the proposed transfer date.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(3) If the ACMA receives a notification under subsection (1), the\nACMA must give a copy of the notification to the Minister.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, prescribed business means a\nbusiness in a prescribed class of businesses.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that one or\nmore specified classes of businesses are prescribed classes of\nbusinesses for the purpose of subsection (4).\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nTransfer of assets  Division 4\n\nSection 581N\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e3b9c6a259401cf76fedbcab289e55e5e980b00c01eba36240ca39346f338aa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581ma",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581MA Notification of proposed transfer of prescribed business",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 606,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a company is:\n\n(i) a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company; and\n\n(ii) a constitutional corporation; and\n\n(b) the company proposes to transfer the whole or a part of a\nprescribed business after the commencement of Schedule 2 to\nthe Telstra Corporation and Other Legislation Amendment\nAct 2021; and\n\n(c) the proposed transferee is a not a constitutional corporation;\nthe company must:\n\n(d) notify the ACMA in writing of the proposed transfer; and\n\n(e) do so at least 30 days before the proposed transfer date.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(3) If the ACMA receives a notification under subsection (1), the\nACMA must give a copy of the notification to the Minister.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, prescribed business means a\nbusiness in a prescribed class of businesses.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that one or\nmore specified classes of businesses are prescribed classes of\nbusinesses for the purpose of subsection (4).\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nTransfer of assets  Division 4\n\nSection 581N\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ma-ss-1",
