    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581P Notification of transfer of telecommunications asset",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.607",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of Schedule 2 to the Telstra\nCorporation and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2021, a\nTelstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor\ncompany transfers a telecommunications asset; and\n\n(b) the transfer is not covered by a declaration under\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(c) the telecommunications asset is not covered by a declaration\nunder subsection (3); and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of Schedule 2 to the Telstra\nCorporation and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2021, a\nTelstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor\ncompany transfers a telecommunications asset; and\n\n(b) the transfer is not covered by a declaration under\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(c) the telecommunications asset is not covered by a declaration\nunder subsection (3); and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581p-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cfc76a0bcf8cf0283f48e3a8ca9c93cb839954a8f768fa9970eb2b33988fc608",
      "skos:note": "Notification of transfer of telecommunications asset"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581P Notification of transfer of telecommunications asset",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 607,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of Schedule 2 to the Telstra\nCorporation and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2021, a\nTelstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor\ncompany transfers a telecommunications asset; and\n\n(b) the transfer is not covered by a declaration under\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(c) the telecommunications asset is not covered by a declaration\nunder subsection (3); and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581p-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581p"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581pa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581PA Notification of proposed transfer of prescribed asset",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581pa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.608",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a company is:\n\n(i) a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company; and\n\n(ii) a constitutional corporation; and\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nTransfer of assets  Division 4\n\nSection 581Q\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the company proposes to transfer a prescribed asset after the\ncommencement of Schedule 2 to the Telstra Corporation and\nOther Legislation Amendment Act 2021; and\n\n(c) the proposed transferee is a not a constitutional corporation;\nthe company must:\n\n(d) notify the ACMA in writing of the proposed transfer; and\n\n(e) do so at least 30 days before the proposed transfer date.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(3) If the ACMA receives a notification under subsection (1), the\nACMA must give a copy of the notification to the Minister.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, prescribed asset means an asset in\na prescribed class of assets.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that one or\nmore specified classes of assets are prescribed classes of assets for\nthe purpose of subsection (4).\n\n(6) The Minister must not specify a class of assets under subsection (5)\nunless each asset in the class is, or was, used by a Telstra successor\ncompany or a designated Telstra successor company:\n\n(a) in connection with the fulfillment of any of the obligations\nimposed on the company by or under a telecommunications\nlaw; or\n\n(b) in order to maintain the company’s capability (including the\ntechnical, operational or organisational capability) to comply\nwith obligations imposed on the company by or under a\ntelecommunications law.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a company is:\n\n(i) a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra\nsuccessor company; and\n\n(ii) a constitutional corporation; and\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nTransfer of assets  Division 4\n\nSection 581Q\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the company proposes to transfer a prescribed asset after the\ncommencement of Schedule 2 to the Telstra Corporation and\nOther Legislation Amendment Act 2021; and\n\n(c) the proposed transferee is a not a constitutional corporation;\nthe company must:\n\n(d) notify the ACMA in writing of the proposed transfer; and\n\n(e) do so at least 30 days before the proposed transfer date.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(3) If the ACMA receives a notification under subsection (1), the\nACMA must give a copy of the notification to the Minister.\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, prescribed asset means an asset in\na prescribed class of assets.\n\n(5) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that one or\nmore specified classes of assets are prescribed classes of assets for\nthe purpose of subsection (4).\n\n(6) The Minister must not specify a class of assets under subsection (5)\nunless each asset in the class is, or was, used by a Telstra successor\ncompany or a designated Telstra successor company:\n\n(a) in connection with the fulfillment of any of the obligations\nimposed on the company by or under a telecommunications\nlaw; or\n\n(b) in order to maintain the company’s capability (including the\ntechnical, operational or organisational capability) to comply\nwith obligations imposed on the company by or under a\ntelecommunications law.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581pa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581pa-ss-2"
        },
