      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ta-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581TA(2) Facilitation of compliance with a direction given by the",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581ta-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.612",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA must not give a direction to a body corporate under\nsubsection (1) unless:\n\n(a) the ACMA is satisfied that the action specified in the\ndirection will facilitate the first designated Telstra successor\ncompany complying with the first direction; and\n\n(b) the ACMA is satisfied that the body corporate:\n\n(i) has the capability (including the technical, operational\nand organisational capability) to comply with the\ndirection; or\n\n(ii) could reasonably acquire the capability (including the\ntechnical, operational and organisational capability) to\ncomply with the direction; and\n\n(c) the body corporate:\n\n(i) is a constitutional corporation; or\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nDirections  Division 6\n\nSection 581TA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) carries on a telecommunications business covered by\nparagraph 581L(1)(a), (b) or (c).\nCompliance with requirement",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The ACMA must not give a direction to a body corporate under\nsubsection (1) unless:\n\n(a) the ACMA is satisfied that the action specified in the\ndirection will facilitate the first designated Telstra successor\ncompany complying with the first direction; and\n\n(b) the ACMA is satisfied that the body corporate:\n\n(i) has the capability (including the technical, operational\nand organisational capability) to comply with the\ndirection; or\n\n(ii) could reasonably acquire the capability (including the\ntechnical, operational and organisational capability) to\ncomply with the direction; and\n\n(c) the body corporate:\n\n(i) is a constitutional corporation; or\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nDirections  Division 6\n\nSection 581TA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) carries on a telecommunications business covered by\nparagraph 581L(1)(a), (b) or (c).\nCompliance with requirement",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ta"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ta-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581ta-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "818ecca7e3ccfef9bfb58687fb330b0eda2db389e1fde11330427d0af8043e90",
      "skos:note": "The ACMA must give a direction to a body corporate only if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581ta-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581TA(2) Facilitation of compliance with a direction given by the",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 612,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The ACMA must not give a direction to a body corporate under\nsubsection (1) unless:\n\n(a) the ACMA is satisfied that the action specified in the\ndirection will facilitate the first designated Telstra successor\ncompany complying with the first direction; and\n\n(b) the ACMA is satisfied that the body corporate:\n\n(i) has the capability (including the technical, operational\nand organisational capability) to comply with the\ndirection; or\n\n(ii) could reasonably acquire the capability (including the\ntechnical, operational and organisational capability) to\ncomply with the direction; and\n\n(c) the body corporate:\n\n(i) is a constitutional corporation; or\n\n\nTelstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A\nDirections  Division 6\n\nSection 581TA\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) carries on a telecommunications business covered by\nparagraph 581L(1)(a), (b) or (c).\nCompliance with requirement"
    },
