      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.620",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsection (1) does not impose an obligation to the extent (if any)\nto which the imposition of the obligation would have any of the\nfollowing effects:\n\n(a) depriving any person of a right under a contract that was in\nforce at the time the request was made;\n\n\nAccess to supplementary facilities and telecommunications transmission towers  Part\n34B\nAccess to supplementary facilities  Division 2\n\nSection 581Y\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) preventing a designated Telstra successor company from\ncomplying with an undertaking in force under section 577A;\n\n(c) preventing Telstra from complying with an undertaking in\nforce under section 577C or 577E;\n\n(d) if a final migration plan is in force—requiring a designated\nTelstra successor company to engage in conduct in\nconnection with matters covered by the final migration plan.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Subsection (1) does not impose an obligation to the extent (if any)\nto which the imposition of the obligation would have any of the\nfollowing effects:\n\n(a) depriving any person of a right under a contract that was in\nforce at the time the request was made;\n\n\nAccess to supplementary facilities and telecommunications transmission towers  Part\n34B\nAccess to supplementary facilities  Division 2\n\nSection 581Y\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) preventing a designated Telstra successor company from\ncomplying with an undertaking in force under section 577A;\n\n(c) preventing Telstra from complying with an undertaking in\nforce under section 577C or 577E;\n\n(d) if a final migration plan is in force—requiring a designated\nTelstra successor company to engage in conduct in\nconnection with matters covered by the final migration plan.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43f1b9eef161dd0b71e1068533eb3eb13052984135bbb785f07c298a75b1c5f5",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from obligations under subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581y-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581Y(4) Access to supplementary facilities",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 620,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsection (1) does not impose an obligation to the extent (if any)\nto which the imposition of the obligation would have any of the\nfollowing effects:\n\n(a) depriving any person of a right under a contract that was in\nforce at the time the request was made;\n\n\nAccess to supplementary facilities and telecommunications transmission towers  Part\n34B\nAccess to supplementary facilities  Division 2\n\nSection 581Y\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) preventing a designated Telstra successor company from\ncomplying with an undertaking in force under section 577A;\n\n(c) preventing Telstra from complying with an undertaking in\nforce under section 577C or 577E;\n\n(d) if a final migration plan is in force—requiring a designated\nTelstra successor company to engage in conduct in\nconnection with matters covered by the final migration plan."
    },
    {
