    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581Y(5) Access to supplementary facilities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581y-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.620",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If, at the time the request was made:\n\n(a) one or more provisions (the contingent provisions) of a\ncontract have not come into force because:\n\n(i) the contingent provisions are subject to a condition\nprecedent; and\n\n(ii) the condition precedent has not been satisfied; and\n\n(b) there is a possibility that the condition precedent could\nbecome satisfied; and\n\n(c) assuming that the condition precedent had been satisfied:\n\n(i) the contingent provisions would come into force; and\n\n(ii) the person would have a right under the contingent\nprovisions;\nparagraph (4)(a) has effect, in relation to the contract, as if, at the\ntime the request was made:\n\n(d) the contract was in force; and\n\n(e) the person had the right under the contract.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If, at the time the request was made:\n\n(a) one or more provisions (the contingent provisions) of a\ncontract have not come into force because:\n\n(i) the contingent provisions are subject to a condition\nprecedent; and\n\n(ii) the condition precedent has not been satisfied; and\n\n(b) there is a possibility that the condition precedent could\nbecome satisfied; and\n\n(c) assuming that the condition precedent had been satisfied:\n\n(i) the contingent provisions would come into force; and\n\n(ii) the person would have a right under the contingent\nprovisions;\nparagraph (4)(a) has effect, in relation to the contract, as if, at the\ntime the request was made:\n\n(d) the contract was in force; and\n\n(e) the person had the right under the contract.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5-logic-linearlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581y-ss-5-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a813b4a5ce25cccf04b5bc2e2940b1f29549ee777880802d53a85210e30b4b62",
      "skos:note": "If a condition precedent could become satisfied, the contingent provisions would come into force and the person would have a right under the contract."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581y-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581Y(5) Access to supplementary facilities",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 620,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If, at the time the request was made:\n\n(a) one or more provisions (the contingent provisions) of a\ncontract have not come into force because:\n\n(i) the contingent provisions are subject to a condition\nprecedent; and\n\n(ii) the condition precedent has not been satisfied; and\n\n(b) there is a possibility that the condition precedent could\nbecome satisfied; and\n\n(c) assuming that the condition precedent had been satisfied:\n\n(i) the contingent provisions would come into force; and\n\n(ii) the person would have a right under the contingent\nprovisions;\nparagraph (4)(a) has effect, in relation to the contract, as if, at the\ntime the request was made:\n\n(d) the contract was in force; and\n\n(e) the person had the right under the contract."
    },
