        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.626",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In determining whether compliance with subsection (1) in relation\nto a tower is technically feasible, the ACCC must have regard to:\n\n\nAccess to supplementary facilities and telecommunications transmission towers  Part\n34B\nAccess to telecommunications transmission towers  Division 3\n\nSection 581ZD\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) whether compliance is likely to result in significant\ndifficulties of a technical or engineering nature; and\n\n(b) whether compliance is likely to result in a significant threat\nto the health or safety of persons who operate, or work on,\nthe tower; and\n\n(c) if compliance is likely to have a result referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b)—whether there are practicable means of\navoiding such a result, including (but not limited to):\n\n(i) changing the configuration or operating parameters of a\nfacility situated on the tower; and\n\n(ii) making alterations to the tower; and\n\n(d) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In determining whether compliance with subsection (1) in relation\nto a tower is technically feasible, the ACCC must have regard to:\n\n\nAccess to supplementary facilities and telecommunications transmission towers  Part\n34B\nAccess to telecommunications transmission towers  Division 3\n\nSection 581ZD\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) whether compliance is likely to result in significant\ndifficulties of a technical or engineering nature; and\n\n(b) whether compliance is likely to result in a significant threat\nto the health or safety of persons who operate, or work on,\nthe tower; and\n\n(c) if compliance is likely to have a result referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b)—whether there are practicable means of\navoiding such a result, including (but not limited to):\n\n(i) changing the configuration or operating parameters of a\nfacility situated on the tower; and\n\n(ii) making alterations to the tower; and\n\n(d) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zd"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zd-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zd-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zd-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92e7c9ba80d7ebd0148e541a279b05ddd5149c7878e1eb1b89c0afab0a20e16f",
      "skos:note": "The ACCC must consider certain factors when determining technical feasibility of compliance with subsection (1) in relation to a tower."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581zd-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581ZD(5) Access to telecommunications transmission towers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 626,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In determining whether compliance with subsection (1) in relation\nto a tower is technically feasible, the ACCC must have regard to:\n\n\nAccess to supplementary facilities and telecommunications transmission towers  Part\n34B\nAccess to telecommunications transmission towers  Division 3\n\nSection 581ZD\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) whether compliance is likely to result in significant\ndifficulties of a technical or engineering nature; and\n\n(b) whether compliance is likely to result in a significant threat\nto the health or safety of persons who operate, or work on,\nthe tower; and\n\n(c) if compliance is likely to have a result referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b)—whether there are practicable means of\navoiding such a result, including (but not limited to):\n\n(i) changing the configuration or operating parameters of a\nfacility situated on the tower; and\n\n(ii) making alterations to the tower; and\n\n(d) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant."
    },
