    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "581ZH Review of corporate control percentage",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581zh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.631",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Within 6 months after the commencement of this section, the\nACCC must conduct a review of whether a determination should\nbe made under subsection 581W(3) and, if so, the percentage that\nshould be specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The ACCC must:\n\n(a) prepare a written report of the review; and\n\n(b) give the report to the Minister.\n\n(3) The ACCC must, by notifiable instrument, specify the day on\nwhich the report was given to the Minister.\n\n(4) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe day on which the report is given to the Minister.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Within 6 months after the commencement of this section, the\nACCC must conduct a review of whether a determination should\nbe made under subsection 581W(3) and, if so, the percentage that\nshould be specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The ACCC must:\n\n(a) prepare a written report of the review; and\n\n(b) give the report to the Minister.\n\n(3) The ACCC must, by notifiable instrument, specify the day on\nwhich the report was given to the Minister.\n\n(4) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe day on which the report is given to the Minister.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zh-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zh-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581zh-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f9ecd34b58452b9cd8d8c6798a4792ab8f7ac4f0d11d3fff1908008f27120ffd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-581zh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "581ZH Review of corporate control percentage",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 631,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Within 6 months after the commencement of this section, the\nACCC must conduct a review of whether a determination should\nbe made under subsection 581W(3) and, if so, the percentage that\nshould be specified in the determination.\n\n(2) The ACCC must:\n\n(a) prepare a written report of the review; and\n\n(b) give the report to the Minister.\n\n(3) The ACCC must, by notifiable instrument, specify the day on\nwhich the report was given to the Minister.\n\n(4) The Minister must cause copies of the report to be tabled in each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe day on which the report is given to the Minister."
    },
