    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-584",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "584 Procedure relating to certain continuing offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-584"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.634",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If section 43 applies to an offence against a provision of this Act,\ncharges against the same person for any number of offences against\nthat provision may be joined in the same information, complaint or\nsummons if:\n\n(a) those charges are founded on the same facts; or\n\n(b) form, or are part of, a series of offences of the same or a\nsimilar character.\n\n(2) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences against such a\nprovision, the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or\nall of those offences, but that penalty must not exceed the sum of\nthe maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty\nwere imposed in respect of each offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If section 43 applies to an offence against a provision of this Act,\ncharges against the same person for any number of offences against\nthat provision may be joined in the same information, complaint or\nsummons if:\n\n(a) those charges are founded on the same facts; or\n\n(b) form, or are part of, a series of offences of the same or a\nsimilar character.\n\n(2) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences against such a\nprovision, the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or\nall of those offences, but that penalty must not exceed the sum of\nthe maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty\nwere imposed in respect of each offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-584-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-584-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19e3c3f91af52d0cabab578fc0a21a8f88e4682e9315eded52cfe3a7b20cbc69"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-584",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "584 Procedure relating to certain continuing offences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 634,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If section 43 applies to an offence against a provision of this Act,\ncharges against the same person for any number of offences against\nthat provision may be joined in the same information, complaint or\nsummons if:\n\n(a) those charges are founded on the same facts; or\n\n(b) form, or are part of, a series of offences of the same or a\nsimilar character.\n\n(2) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences against such a\nprovision, the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or\nall of those offences, but that penalty must not exceed the sum of\nthe maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty\nwere imposed in respect of each offence."
    },
