    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-585",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "585 Treatment of partnerships",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-585"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.634",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Act applies to a partnership as if the partnership were a\nperson, but it applies with the following changes:\n\n(a) obligations that would be imposed on the partnership are\nimposed instead on each partner, but may be discharged by\nany of the partners;\n\n(b) any offence against this Act that would otherwise be\ncommitted by the partnership is taken to have been\ncommitted by each partner who:\n\n(i) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the relevant act or\nomission; or\n\n(ii) was in any way knowingly concerned in, or party to, the\nrelevant act or omission (whether directly or indirectly\nand whether by any act or omission of the partner).\n\n(2) In this section:\ncivil penalty provision includes:\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 586\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) a civil penalty provision within the meaning of the Spam Act\n2003; and\n\n(b) a civil penalty provision within the meaning of the Do Not\nCall Register Act 2006.\noffence includes a breach of a civil penalty provision.\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(c) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 and regulations under that\nAct.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Act applies to a partnership as if the partnership were a\nperson, but it applies with the following changes:\n\n(a) obligations that would be imposed on the partnership are\nimposed instead on each partner, but may be discharged by\nany of the partners;\n\n(b) any offence against this Act that would otherwise be\ncommitted by the partnership is taken to have been\ncommitted by each partner who:\n\n(i) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the relevant act or\nomission; or\n\n(ii) was in any way knowingly concerned in, or party to, the\nrelevant act or omission (whether directly or indirectly\nand whether by any act or omission of the partner).\n\n(2) In this section:\ncivil penalty provision includes:\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 586\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) a civil penalty provision within the meaning of the Spam Act\n2003; and\n\n(b) a civil penalty provision within the meaning of the Do Not\nCall Register Act 2006.\noffence includes a breach of a civil penalty provision.\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(c) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 and regulations under that\nAct.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-585-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-585-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f5db0cb6c2c2bb67317bb7a2b979a80b1cd73eb902f0a3b4ea7686884e78ef6e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-585",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "585 Treatment of partnerships",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 634,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Act applies to a partnership as if the partnership were a\nperson, but it applies with the following changes:\n\n(a) obligations that would be imposed on the partnership are\nimposed instead on each partner, but may be discharged by\nany of the partners;\n\n(b) any offence against this Act that would otherwise be\ncommitted by the partnership is taken to have been\ncommitted by each partner who:\n\n(i) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the relevant act or\nomission; or\n\n(ii) was in any way knowingly concerned in, or party to, the\nrelevant act or omission (whether directly or indirectly\nand whether by any act or omission of the partner).\n\n(2) In this section:\ncivil penalty provision includes:\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 586\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) a civil penalty provision within the meaning of the Spam Act\n2003; and\n\n(b) a civil penalty provision within the meaning of the Do Not\nCall Register Act 2006.\noffence includes a breach of a civil penalty provision.\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(c) the Do Not Call Register Act 2006 and regulations under that\nAct."
    },
