        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-588",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "588 Service of summons or process on foreign corporations—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-588"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.636",
      "values:originalText": "criminal proceedings\n\n(1) This section applies to a summons or process in any criminal\nproceedings under this Act, where:\n\n(a) the summons or process is required to be served on a body\ncorporate incorporated outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the body corporate does not have a registered office or a\nprincipal office in Australia; and\n\n(c) the body corporate has an agent in Australia.\n\n(2) Service of the summons or process may be effected by serving it\non the agent.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) has effect in addition to section 28A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nSection 28A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 deals with the service\nof documents.\n\n(4) In this section:\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 589\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncriminal proceeding includes a proceeding to determine whether a\nperson should be tried for an offence.\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "criminal proceedings\n\n(1) This section applies to a summons or process in any criminal\nproceedings under this Act, where:\n\n(a) the summons or process is required to be served on a body\ncorporate incorporated outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the body corporate does not have a registered office or a\nprincipal office in Australia; and\n\n(c) the body corporate has an agent in Australia.\n\n(2) Service of the summons or process may be effected by serving it\non the agent.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) has effect in addition to section 28A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nSection 28A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 deals with the service\nof documents.\n\n(4) In this section:\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 589\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncriminal proceeding includes a proceeding to determine whether a\nperson should be tried for an offence.\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-588-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-588-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-588-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-588-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f589d777c1e1adf1820bcf31f13f7e19110049d12a7d521c051f5d8723325f40"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-588",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "588 Service of summons or process on foreign corporations—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 636,
      "values:originalText": "criminal proceedings\n\n(1) This section applies to a summons or process in any criminal\nproceedings under this Act, where:\n\n(a) the summons or process is required to be served on a body\ncorporate incorporated outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the body corporate does not have a registered office or a\nprincipal office in Australia; and\n\n(c) the body corporate has an agent in Australia.\n\n(2) Service of the summons or process may be effected by serving it\non the agent.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) has effect in addition to section 28A of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901.\nNote:\nSection 28A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 deals with the service\nof documents.\n\n(4) In this section:\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 589\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncriminal proceeding includes a proceeding to determine whether a\nperson should be tried for an offence.\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act."
    },
