    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-590",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "590 Arbitration—acquisition of property",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-590"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.638",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a provision of this Act that authorises the\nconduct of an arbitration (whether by the ACCC or another\nperson).\n\n(2) The provision has no effect to the extent (if any) to which it\npurports to authorise the acquisition of property if that acquisition:\n\n(a) is otherwise than on just terms; and\n\n(b) would be invalid because of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 591\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a provision of this Act that authorises the\nconduct of an arbitration (whether by the ACCC or another\nperson).\n\n(2) The provision has no effect to the extent (if any) to which it\npurports to authorise the acquisition of property if that acquisition:\n\n(a) is otherwise than on just terms; and\n\n(b) would be invalid because of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 591\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-590-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-590-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-590-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a303609d08da0fe95de45dc8e2d30d0d7c84c12e6a0e38dabe3ef70c8d7b3414"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-590",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "590 Arbitration—acquisition of property",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 638,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a provision of this Act that authorises the\nconduct of an arbitration (whether by the ACCC or another\nperson).\n\n(2) The provision has no effect to the extent (if any) to which it\npurports to authorise the acquisition of property if that acquisition:\n\n(a) is otherwise than on just terms; and\n\n(b) would be invalid because of paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 35\n\nSection 591\n\nTelecommunications Act 1997\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\nthis Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act."
    },
