    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-591",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "591 Compensation—constitutional safety net",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-591"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.639",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) apart from this section, the operation of this Act would result\nin the acquisition of property from a person otherwise than\non just terms; and\n\n(b) the acquisition would be invalid because of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution;\nthe Commonwealth is liable to pay compensation of a reasonable\namount to the person in respect of the acquisition.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) apart from this section, the operation of this Act would result\nin the acquisition of property from a person otherwise than\non just terms; and\n\n(b) the acquisition would be invalid because of\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution;\nthe Commonwealth is liable to pay compensation of a reasonable\namount to the person in respect of the acquisition.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in the\nFederal Court for the recovery from the Commonwealth of such\nreasonable amount of compensation as the court determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in\nparagraph 51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\nthis Act includes:\n\n(a) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service\nStandards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act; and\n\n(b) the Spam Act 2003 and regulations under that Act; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-591-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-591-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-591-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "60b28cb2b7fa805a0af8fefd7e6f1ae61aaec551780363e8f5588f10605a96e1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-act-1997#sec-591",
